/annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 179.70991840629108 -33.208800332088 L 180.26338996639123 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(179.99,0) translate(0,-22.73) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.56)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.65em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.27em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="22.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.E7.m1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\Phi_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}^{\mathbb{FM}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝕄</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\Phi_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}^{\mathbb{FM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(179.99,0) translate(0,-12.91)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 179.70991840629108 -33.208800332088 L 180.26338996639123 -12.914505311029819" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 179.70991840629108 -12.914505311029819 L 180.26338996639123 -12.914505311029819" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g></svg></span>
</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.3. </span>Main results on quantitative Floer theory</h4>

<div id="S1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Many successful applications of Hamiltonian Floer theory have a quantitative flavor. We also have the quantitative package under our framework. As many applications take advantage of using different coefficients, we phrase the statements using a general Novikov ring/field.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">1.3.1. </span>Action filtration and spectral invariants</h5>

<div id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We state the following theorem for the convenience for readers to cite. The proof has no difference from cases proved using other approaches is hence omitted.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem K</span></span><span id="Thmthma11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Filtered Floer complex and continuation map)<span id="Thmthma11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthma11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthma11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a commutative ring with unit and let <math id="Thmthma11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math> be a Floer complex provided by Theorem <a href="#Thmthma1" title="Theorem A (Floer chain complex). ‣ 1.1.1. Floer complexes and Floer homology ‣ 1.1. Main results on Floer complexes ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> tensored with <math id="Thmthma11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S1.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S1.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I9.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The differential of the Floer complex preserves the energy filtration. More precisely, for each </span><math id="S1.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I9.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the differential preserves the subgroups</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau}:=\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}p_{i}\in CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})\ |\ {\mathcal{A}}_{H}(p_{i})\leq\tau\Big\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau}:=\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}p_{i}\in CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})\ |\ {\mathcal{A}}_{H}(p_{i})\leq\tau\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I9.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I9.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau}:=\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}p_{i}\in CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})\ |\ {\mathcal{A}}_{H}(p_{i})&lt;\tau\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau}:=\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}p_{i}\in CF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})\ |\ {\mathcal{A}}_{H}(p_{i})&lt;\tau\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S1.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I9.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S1.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H_{1};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H_{1};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I9.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S1.I9.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H_{2};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H_{2};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I9.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be two Floer complexes. Denote</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=\int_{S^{1}}\sup_{X}(H_{1,t}-H_{2,t})dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>X</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=\int_{S^{1}}\sup_{X}(H_{1,t}-H_{2,t})dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I9.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I9.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then there exists a continuation map </span><math id="S1.I9.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{12}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>12</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{12}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I9.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that for all </span><math id="S1.I9.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I9.i2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \Phi^{12}(\Theta)(CF(H_{1};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau})\subseteq CF(H_{2};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau+c},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>12</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \Phi^{12}(\Theta)(CF(H_{1};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau})\subseteq CF(H_{2};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau+c},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \Phi^{12}(\Theta)(CF(H_{1};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau})\subseteq CF(H_{2};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau+c}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>12</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \Phi^{12}(\Theta)(CF(H_{1};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau})\subseteq CF(H_{2};\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau+c}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The filtered version of continuation map implies that for any nondegenerate Hamiltonian <math id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, the filtered homology groups</p>
<table id="S1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ HF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ HF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{\leq\tau},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ HF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ HF(H;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})^{&lt;\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">only depend on <math id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed in the local context, we omit the coefficient from the notations. Moreover, there are well-defined maps</p>
<table id="S1.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="HF(H)^{&lt;\tau}\to HF(X)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">HF(H)^{&lt;\tau}\to HF(X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">compatible with maps (for <math id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1}\leq\tau_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1}\leq\tau_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
<table id="S1.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="HF(H)^{&lt;\tau_{1}}\to HF(H)^{&lt;\tau_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">HF(H)^{&lt;\tau_{1}}\to HF(H)^{&lt;\tau_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">This allows us to define the <span id="S1.SS3.SSS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">spectral invariants</span> of Floer homology classes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1.8</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a Hamiltonian <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, the <span id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">spectral invariant</span> of <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H}(x):=\lim_{i\to\infty}\Big\{\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}\ |\ x\in{\rm Im}\big(HF(H_{i})^{&lt;\tau}\to HF(X)\big)\Big\}\in{\mathbb{R}}\cup\{-\infty\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(x):=\lim_{i\to\infty}\Big\{\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}\ |\ x\in{\rm Im}\big(HF(H_{i})^{&lt;\tau}\to HF(X)\big)\Big\}\in{\mathbb{R}}\cup\{-\infty\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here the limit is taken for a sequence of nondegenerate Hamiltonians <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> converging to <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem L</span></span><span id="Thmthma12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Spectral invariants)<span id="Thmthma12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthma12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a Noetherian ring <math id="Thmthma12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. The spectral numbers <math id="Thmthma12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmthma12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the following properties.</span></p>
<ol id="S1.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S1.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Spectrality)</span><span id="S1.I10.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For any </span><math id="S1.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the number</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H}(x)=-\infty\Longrightarrow x=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(x)=-\infty\Longrightarrow x=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I10.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and for </span><math id="S1.I10.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, there exists a cycle </span><math id="S1.I10.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{x}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> representing </span><math id="S1.I10.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{H}({\mathfrak{x}})=c_{H}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{H}({\mathfrak{x}})=c_{H}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S1.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Shifting Property)</span><span id="S1.I10.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For </span><math id="S1.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in HF(X;\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S1.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\Lambda_{R}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, one has</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H}(ax)=c_{H}(x)-{\mathfrak{v}}(a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(ax)=c_{H}(x)-{\mathfrak{v}}(a).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S1.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Lipschitz Continuity)</span><span id="S1.I10.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S1.I10.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is Lipschitz continuous with respect to the Hofer metric on the space of 1-periodic Hamiltonians.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I10.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S1.I10.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Isotopy Invariance)</span><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S1.I10.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> only depends on the element </span><math id="S1.I10.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S1.I10.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm H}\widetilde{\rm am}(X,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>am</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm H}\widetilde{\rm am}(X,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the Hamiltonian isotopy induced from </span><math id="S1.I10.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as an element of the universal cover of the Hamiltonian diffeomorphism group. Hence we can denote </span><math id="S1.I10.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by </span><math id="S1.I10.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\tilde{\phi}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\tilde{\phi}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I10.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S1.I10.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I10.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Symplectic Invariance)</span><span id="S1.I10.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For any symplectomorphism </span><math id="S1.I10.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:X\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:X\to X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, one has </span><math id="S1.I10.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{H\circ\rho}(x)=c_{H}(\rho_{*}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H\circ\rho}(x)=c_{H}(\rho_{*}(x))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="S1.I10.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the automorphism</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{*}:HF(X)\to HF(X)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{*}:HF(X)\to HF(X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I10.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">induced by </span><math id="S1.I10.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I10.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="S1.I10.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I10.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Triangle Inequality)</span><span id="S1.I10.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For any </span><math id="S1.I10.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in HF(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in HF(X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S1.I10.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi},\tilde{\psi}\in{\rm H}\widetilde{\rm am}(X,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>am</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi},\tilde{\psi}\in{\rm H}\widetilde{\rm am}(X,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, one has</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\tilde{\phi}\tilde{\psi}}(x\star y)\leq c_{\tilde{\phi}}(x)+c_{\tilde{\psi}}(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\tilde{\phi}\tilde{\psi}}(x\star y)\leq c_{\tilde{\phi}}(x)+c_{\tilde{\psi}}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I10.i6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here </span><math id="S1.I10.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i6.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the pair-of-pants product on Floer homology defined by Theorem </span><a href="#Thmthma3" title="Theorem C (Pair-of-pants product). ‣ 1.1.2. Pair-of-pants product ‣ 1.1. Main results on Floer complexes ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a><span id="S1.I10.i6.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I10.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(7)</span> 
<div id="S1.I10.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I10.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Poincaré Duality)</span><span id="S1.I10.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Let </span><math id="S1.I10.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R={\bf K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R={\bf K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a field. Let </span><math id="S1.I10.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{0}^{\rm PD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>PD</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{0}^{\rm PD}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the composition</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.55554pt\hbox{\kern 61.81519pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-61.81519pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{HF(X;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi})\otimes HF(X;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 62.95053pt\raise 6.20831pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-3.20831pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\Phi^{\rm PD}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 85.81519pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 85.81519pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 130.28323pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 130.28323pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\bf K}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-11.14645356605438px" height="28.33" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="85.53 11.15 286.58 28.33" width="286.58"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 85.53367309654767 28.32731798804613) translate(0,3.54) translate(85.53,0)"> <g transform="translate(-85.53,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.76em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="162.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 85.53367309654767 -0.27673578005007266 L 85.53367309654767 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(87.11,0) translate(0,8.59) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-4.44)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="21.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">PD</mi></msup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(118.74,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 85.53367309654767 -0.27673578005007266 L 118.74247342863568 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 118.74247342863568 -0.27673578005007266 L 118.74247342863568 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(118.74,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.45em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="20.02"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 147.06411186187648 -0.27673578005007266 L 147.06411186187648 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(180.28,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 147.06411186187648 -0.27673578005007266 L 180.2729121939645 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 180.2729121939645 -0.27673578005007266 L 180.2729121939645 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(180.28,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.9em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="12.47"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mi>𝐊</mi></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.55554pt\hbox{\kern 61.81519pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-61.81519pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{HF(X;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi})\otimes HF(X;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 62.95053pt\raise 6.20831pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-3.20831pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\Phi^{\rm PD}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 85.81519pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 85.81519pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 130.28323pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 130.28323pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\bf K}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I10.i7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I10.i7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S1.I10.i7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{H}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i7.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the reversal of the Hamiltonian </span><math id="S1.I10.i7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I10.i7.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then one has</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="c_{H}(x)=-\inf\Big\{c_{\overline{H}}(y)\ |\ y\in HF(X;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}),\ \Phi_{0}^{\rm PD}(x,y)\neq 0\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>PD</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{H}(x)=-\inf\Big\{c_{\overline{H}}(y)\ |\ y\in HF(X;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}),\ \Phi_{0}^{\rm PD}(x,y)\neq 0\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">1.3.2. </span>Barcodes</h5>

<div id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Another quantitative structure widely used in applications is the barcode. We follow the approach of Usher–Zhang <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite> which requires slightly modified setup.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a symplectic manifold <math id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with the abelian group <math id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> defined by (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In 1.1.1. Floer complexes and Floer homology ‣ 1.1. Main results on Floer complexes ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), a (concise) <span id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">barcode</span> (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>) is a finite multiset of elements of <math id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({\mathbb{R}}/\omega(\Pi))\times(0,+\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{R}}/\omega(\Pi))\times(0,+\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is most useful when considering Floer barcodes with field coefficients. Then the complex</p>
<table id="S1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}):=CF(H;\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\Pi})\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}):=CF(H;\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\Pi})\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">is a (slight generalization of) Floer-type complex in the sense of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Definition 4.1]</cite>. It follows from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Definition 6.3, Theorem 7.1]</cite> that there is a barcode canonically associated to the complex <math id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H;\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1.9</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Floer barcodes)<span id="S1.Thmthm9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The barcode associated to the Floer complex <math id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H;\Lambda_{{\bf K}}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H;\Lambda_{{\bf K}}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math> only depends on the Hamiltonian <math id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the dependence on <math id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz with respect to the bottleneck distance on barcodes and the Hofer metric on the space of <math id="S1.Thmthm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic Hamiltonians.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.SS3.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from applying Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmthm38" title="Proposition 7.38. ‣ 7.5.1. Nonarchimedean linear algebra ‣ 7.5. Quantitative theories ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.38</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S7.Thmthm40" title="Theorem 7.40. ‣ 7.5.3. Barcodes ‣ 7.5. Quantitative theories ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.40</span></a> to the filtered Floer complex constructed in Theorem <a href="#Thmthma11" title="Theorem K (Filtered Floer complex and continuation map). ‣ 1.3.1. Action filtration and spectral invariants ‣ 1.3. Main results on quantitative Floer theory ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">1.3.3. </span>Quantitative features of equivariant Floer theory</h5>

<div id="S1.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The equivariant Floer cochain complex also has an energy filtration. Notice that the equivariant cochain complex <math id="S1.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})</annotation></semantics></math> is a module over <math id="S1.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can prove that it is a Floer-type complex. On the other hand, the ordinary Floer complex <math id="S1.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H;\Lambda_{{\bf F}_{\sf p}}^{\Pi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H;\Lambda_{{\bf F}_{\sf p}}^{\Pi})</annotation></semantics></math> also induces an equivariant complex coming from its own <math id="S1.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}</annotation></semantics></math>-fold tensor power, denoted by</p>
<table id="S1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(CF(H)^{\otimes{\sf p}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(CF(H)^{\otimes{\sf p}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is also a Floer-type complex.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem M</span></span><span id="Thmthma13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Barcode stretching under prime iteration)<span id="Thmthma13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthma13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthma13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact symplectic manifold, <math id="Thmthma13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}</annotation></semantics></math> be a prime, and <math id="Thmthma13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be a Hamiltonian on <math id="Thmthma13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> such that the <math id="Thmthma13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration <math id="Thmthma13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\natural{\sf p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\natural{\sf p}}</annotation></semantics></math> is nondegenerate.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma13.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S1.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S1.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I11.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The equivariant Floer cochain complex </span><math id="S1.I11.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I11.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a Floer-type complex over the Novikov field </span><math id="S1.I11.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I11.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S1.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I11.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The equivariant pair-of-pants product has a chain-level realization</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P:C_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(CF(H)^{\otimes{\sf p}})\to CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P:C_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(CF(H)^{\otimes{\sf p}})\to CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I11.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I11.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which is a filtered chain homotopy equivalence for Floer-type complexes.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I11.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S1.I11.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I11.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose the bar-length spectrum of </span><math id="S1.I11.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF(H)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S1.I11.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\beta_{1}(H)\leq\cdots\leq\beta_{m}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\beta_{1}(H)\leq\cdots\leq\beta_{m}(H)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then the bar-length spectrum of </span><math id="S1.I11.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta_{i,{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}}(H^{\natural 2})=2\beta_{i}(H),\ i=1,\ldots,m" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}}(H^{\natural 2})=2\beta_{i}(H),\ i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I11.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">when </span><math id="S1.I11.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}=2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\beta_{2i-1,{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})=\beta_{2i,{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})={\sf p}\beta_{i}(H),\ i=1,\ldots,m" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝗉</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2i-1,{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})=\beta_{2i,{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})={\sf p}\beta_{i}(H),\ i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I11.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">when </span><math id="S1.I11.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I11.i3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">1.3.4. </span>Quantitative Hamiltonian Floer theory for noncontractible orbits</h5>

<div id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We state the main quantitative results about Floer theory for noncontractible orbits. We follow very much the treatment of Sugimoto <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>. Since the resulting homology group always vanishes, there are no spectral invariants; hence the barcodes are the main quantitative aspects here.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Choose a possibly noncontractible loop <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:S^{1}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:S^{1}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> which represents a nonzero class</p>
<table id="S1.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\gamma]\neq 0\in H_{1}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})_{\rm free}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>free</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\gamma]\neq 0\in H_{1}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})_{\rm free}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">One can consider noncontractible periodic orbits of a Hamiltonian <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> which are homologous (over <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>) to <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1.10</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S1.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be a 1-periodic Hamiltonian on <math id="S1.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S1.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S1.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x:S^{1}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x:S^{1}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> be a 1-periodic orbit of <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. A <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I12.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-capping</span> of <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is an oriented cobordism <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\Sigma\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\Sigma\to X</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="S1.I12.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> could be a higher genus surface).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S1.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two <math id="S1.I12.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-cappings are equivalent if their difference, which is a class in <math id="S1.I12.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})</annotation></semantics></math>, has zero symplectic area. A <math id="S1.I12.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I12.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-capped orbit</span> of <math id="S1.I12.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is a 1-periodic orbit together with an equivalence class of <math id="S1.I12.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-cappings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I12.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S1.I12.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I12.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="S1.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{O}}_{\gamma}(H)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{O}}_{\gamma}(H)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I12.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">denote the set of <math id="S1.I12.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-capped orbits of <math id="S1.I12.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, on which there is a free action by the group</p>
<table id="S1.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma:=H_{2}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})/{\rm ker}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma:=H_{2}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})/{\rm ker}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In our setup we do not keep the <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>-grading but only consider the <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-grading on <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-capped orbits. Each <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-capped orbit <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> has a well-defined symplectic action <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{H,\gamma}(p)\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{H,\gamma}(p)\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The construction of the filtered Floer complex is summarized below and will be proved in Section <a href="#S28" title="28. Quantitative Theory for Noncontractible Hamiltonian Orbits ‣ Part IV EQUIVARIANT FLOER THEORY AND STEENROD OPERATIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.11</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Filtered Floer chain complex for noncontractible periodic orbits)<span id="S1.Thmthm11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact symplectic manifold and let <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:S^{1}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:S^{1}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth loop with <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\gamma]\neq 0\in H_{1}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})_{\rm free}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>free</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\gamma]\neq 0\in H_{1}(X;{\mathbb{Z}})_{\rm free}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be a nondegenerate <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic Hamiltonian. Then for each <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-periodic family of <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-compatible almost complex structures <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a differential on the <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}/2</annotation></semantics></math>-graded abelian group</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="CF_{\gamma}(H):=\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}p_{i}\ |\ a_{i}\in{\mathbb{Z}},\ p_{i}\in\tilde{\mathcal{O}}_{\gamma}(H),\ \lim_{i\to\infty}{\mathcal{A}}_{H,\gamma}(p_{i})=-\infty\Big\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>γ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.389em">,</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{\gamma}(H):=\Big\{\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}p_{i}\ |\ a_{i}\in{\mathbb{Z}},\ p_{i}\in\tilde{\mathcal{O}}_{\gamma}(H),\ \lim_{i\to\infty}{\mathcal{A}}_{H,\gamma}(p_{i})=-\infty\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">leading to a <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}/2</annotation></semantics></math>-graded complex of abelian groups</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{\gamma}(H,J,\Xi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{\gamma}(H,J,\Xi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for each field <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the tensor product</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{\gamma}(H)\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{\gamma}(H)\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is a Floer-type complex over <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> whose filtered isomorphism class only depends on <math id="S1.Thmthm11.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Under the assumption that <math id="S1.SS3.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\gamma]\neq 0\in H_{1}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\gamma]\neq 0\in H_{1}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, we expect that a continuation map argument can prove the vanishing of the resulting homology group. The main use of the noncontractible Floer chain complex is on the quantitative side. The main purpose of developing this theory is to generalize the work of Sugimoto <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>, which uses the equivariant pair-of-pants product as a primary tool. We state the main result regarding the quantitative implications, which is also proved in Section <a href="#S28" title="28. Quantitative Theory for Noncontractible Hamiltonian Orbits ‣ Part IV EQUIVARIANT FLOER THEORY AND STEENROD OPERATIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1.12</span></span><span id="S1.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumption of Theorem <a href="#S1.Thmthm11" title="Theorem 1.11 (Filtered Floer chain complex for noncontractible periodic orbits). ‣ 1.3.4. Quantitative Hamiltonian Floer theory for noncontractible orbits ‣ 1.3. Main results on quantitative Floer theory ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.11</span></a>, let <math id="S1.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}</annotation></semantics></math> be a prime and suppose <math id="S1.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\natural{\sf p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\natural{\sf p}}</annotation></semantics></math> is nondegenerate.</span></p>
<ol id="S1.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S1.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a Floer-type complex</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}},\gamma)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I13.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">over </span><math id="S1.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> which is freely generated by </span><math id="S1.I13.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-periodic orbits homologous to </span><math id="S1.I13.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Its filtered isomorphism class only depends on </span><math id="S1.I13.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S1.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a filtered homotopy equivalence</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\gamma}:C_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(CF_{\gamma}(H)^{\otimes{\sf p}})\to CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}},\gamma^{({\sf p})})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\gamma}:C_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(CF_{\gamma}(H)^{\otimes{\sf p}})\to CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}},\gamma^{({\sf p})})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I13.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">of Floer-type complexes over </span><math id="S1.I13.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{{\bf K}_{\sf p}}^{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S1.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H)\leq\cdots\leq\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H)\leq\cdots\leq\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I13.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be the bar-length spectrum of </span><math id="S1.I13.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{\gamma}(H)\otimes\Lambda_{{\bf F}_{\sf p}}^{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{\gamma}(H)\otimes\Lambda_{{\bf F}_{\sf p}}^{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then it only depends on </span><math id="S1.I13.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the homology class of </span><math id="S1.I13.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Moreover, the bar-length spectrum of </span><math id="S1.I13.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}},\gamma^{({\sf p})}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝗉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">♮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CF_{{{\mathbb{Z}}_{\sf p}},\gamma^{({\sf p})}}(H^{\natural{\sf p}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H),\ldots,2\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H),\ldots,2\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I13.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">when </span><math id="S1.I13.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}=2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (with the same number of finite bars) and is</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H),{\sf p}\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H),\ldots,{\sf p}\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H),{\sf p}\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H),{\sf p}\beta_{1}^{\gamma}(H),\ldots,{\sf p}\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H),{\sf p}\beta_{N}^{\gamma}(H)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.I13.i3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">when </span><math id="S1.I13.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sf p}&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝗉</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sf p}&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S1.I13.i3.p1.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (with twice the number of finite bars).</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.4. </span>What we do “virtually”</h4>

<div id="S1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to explain the general principle of our construction (on the virtual side) along with some historical remarks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In a very general sense, the Floer complexes and other chain-level structures are constructed via counting solutions to the Floer equation. To count beyond the cases where transversality can be achieved by geometric perturbations (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>), the so-called virtual technique was invented (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite> etc.). Such constructions, depending on the extent of applications, usually require building a complete package of abstract theory (such as Kuranishi theory and polyfold theory); the application of these abstract theories can typically be broken down into two main components: (virtual) regularization and (virtual) perturbation/integration.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From now on we only discuss under the finite-dimensional/Kuranishi approach, the one upon which the current paper is based, rather than the infinite-dimensional/polyfold approach. The issues and challenges we will address in the finite-dimensional approach may not be manifested in the infinite-dimensional situation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A central issue in the finite-dimensional construction is the choice-dependence. Unlike the algebro-geometric situation, one rarely obtains canonical objects such as a perfect obstruction theory (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>). To obtain choice-independent results, one needs to include various kinds of equivalence relations in the abstract package, or perhaps higher categorical structures. The choice-independence is not yet a significant challenge in cases where one deals with a single or finitely many moduli spaces, such as Gromov–Witten theory. But it causes much more serious difficulties in Floer-type theories. In Floer theory, essentially one obtains virtual fundamental chains rather than cycles; the virtual fundamental chains satisfy expected properties (such as <math id="S1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>) only if we make the constructions for infinitely many moduli spaces compatibly. It could be a delicate issue when developing the abstract package incorporating such compatibility conditions and when fulfilling these conditions in the concrete regularization procedure.<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
              
              
              
            The work of Abouzaid <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> takes a different approach where the choices are made universally in his notion of “theories of virtual counts.”</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to emphasize two important developments which precede the current piece of work. The first one, regarding the perturbation component, starts from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> which proposed the principle leading to integer-valued curve counts even when the orbifold locus of a moduli space is obstructed. After technical exploration by Parker <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>, the authors rigorously established this new perturbation method in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, which we call the FOP perturbation scheme. The second one, regarding the regularization component, is the construction of global Kuranishi charts starting from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>. It provides a powerful method producing global Kuranishi models regularizing any single moduli space and greatly reduces the technicality when discussing the compatibility among local Kuranishi charts. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> we produced the global Kuranishi chart construction for Floer complexes and PSS maps, which is being extended to other chain-level structures in the current paper (with certain upgrades coming from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now we summarize the technical framework underlying our implementation of the virtual technique. Compared to the regularization component, the perturbation component is to simply apply a blackbox theorem (Theorem <a href="#Thmthma14" title="Theorem N. ‣ 8.2. FOP perturbations on flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies ‣ 8. FOP Perturbations ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">N</span></a>) which was already established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>. However, the delicate prerequisite for the blackbox theorem, along with other requirements, demands careful fine-tunings of the regularization component. Since each stage produces different kinds of objects whose compatibility conditions all look similar to flow category structure, each stage-wise construction is phrased as producing a flow category enriched in a particular “regular stratification category.” The objects of such a category are stratified in a way similar to manifolds with corners, with a monoidal structure corresponding to (direct) product and disjoint union.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To be more concrete, the whole procedure we are describing can be summarized in the following zig-zag of functors</p>
<table id="S1.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hbox to0.0pt{$\overbrace{\phantom{\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}\leftarrow\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm finite}^{\rm NC}\rightarrow\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}}}^{{\rm regularization}}$\hss}\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}\leftarrow\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}\rightarrow\underbrace{\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}\leftarrow\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}\rightarrow\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}}_{\rm perturbation}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.0pt;" width="0.0pt"><mover><mover accent="true"><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="true">⏞</mo></mover><mi>regularization</mi></mover></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>FOP</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>perturbation</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hbox to0.0pt{$\overbrace{\phantom{\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}\leftarrow\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm finite}^{\rm NC}\rightarrow\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}}}^{{\rm regularization}}$\hss}\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}\leftarrow\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}\rightarrow\underbrace{\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}\leftarrow\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}\rightarrow\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}}_{\rm perturbation}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">The items are all regular stratification categories where</p>
<ul id="S1.I14" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S1.I14.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the category of stratified topological spaces;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S1.I14.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> is the category of <span id="S1.I14.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">normally complex smooth Kuranishi charts</span>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S1.I14.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the category of <span id="S1.I14.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">normally complex derived orbifolds</span>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I14.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I14.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I14.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S1.I14.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the category of <span id="S1.I14.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pseudomanifolds</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S1.SS4.p7.3" class="ltx_p">In the case of Floer complex, the geometric data of Floer theory (the Hamiltonian and the almost complex structure) provides a flow category enriched in <math id="S1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The regularization component can be summarized as constructing a “lift” of this flow category to <math id="S1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>. This step is basically accomplished by repackaging the <span id="S1.SS4.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AMS construction</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> (where the construction of the normal complex structure also borrows ideas from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>), which contains several delicate steps. Once this lift is constructed, it automatically descends to a flow category enriched in <math id="S1.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the blackbox theorem on FOP perturbations can be directly applied. After the FOP perturbation, the flow category becomes enriched in <math id="S1.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which automatically produces a chain complex over integers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain chain-level structures such as continuation maps, pair-of-pants products etc., we also consider two “higher” analogues of flow categories, i.e., flow multimodules and flow homotopies. Typically, flow categories induce chain complexes, multimodules induce chain maps, and flow homotopies induce chain homotopies. These chain-level structures are also obtained from compatibly implementing the AMS+FOP procedure, namely, producing multimodules and homotopies enriched in categories appearing in the above zig-zag diagram. The differences from the flow category cases only lie in various sub-technical levels.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">1.4.1. </span>Other AMS-type regularization schemes</h5>

<div id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There have been several related works which carry out AMS-type constructions in Floer theory, which aim at constructing not only a single global chart construction, but a compatible system for all involved moduli spaces. These works include <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>, as well as our previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One distinct feature of our work is the formal description of the compatibility condition using the notion of “lifts” of flow categories to various “regular stratification categories.” Having realized that each step of the AMS construction requires a certain compatibility for the choices made for individual moduli spaces (such as the thickening data, stable smoothing, normal complex structure etc.), the formal notions of regular stratification categories and lifts are more convenient and rigorous, although one needs to carefully define each regular stratification category.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The compatibility condition we require here is also most refined since we need to construct genuine perturbations (essentially the same level of refinedness should be established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">57</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>, both of which use the FOP perturbation method developed by us). The specific requirement is contained in the definition of various regular stratification categories, most notably <math id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>, the category of <span id="S1.SS4.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">collared rigidified normally complex smooth Kuranishi spaces</span>. Here the collaredness and rigidifiedness are what make the inductive perturbation possible, from low-energy moduli spaces to high-energy ones. Some other works such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> where genuine perturbations are not needed, the requirement of compatibility can be relaxed. On the other hand, the work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite>, which also relies on constructing compatible (multi-valued) perturbations, uses a different strategy to interpolate not-so-compatible choices over the collar regions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.5. </span>Structure of the paper</h4>

<div id="S1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper is divided into four main parts. In Part 1, we introduce a series of formal notions, including various categories such as those of pseudomanifolds with corners, Kuranishi spaces, derived orbifolds, and their variants; the notions of flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies; the abstract construction of chain-level objects; and the blackbox of FOP perturbation method. In Part 2, we introduce flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies appearing in (non-equivariant) Floer theory, state the main technical theorems about AMS regularization, and prove most of the main results stated in the introduction. In Part 3, we provide the details of the AMS construction asserted in Part 2. In Part 4, we modify all the previous constructions in the equivariant setting and establish results related to the quantum Steenrod operations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.6. </span>Acknowledgements</h4>

<div id="S1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We thank Egor Shelukhin and Nicolas Wilkins for related discussions involving our collaboration <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. We thank Zihong Chen, Helmut Hofer, Rohil Prasad, Sobhan Seyfaddini for their interest in our work and encouragement.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_part">Part I </span>FORMAL NOTIONS</h2>

<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Outline of Part 1</h3>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the abstract framework underlying the formulation of Floer theory in various levels. Several concepts related to Floer theory and the virtual construction are described in more abstract ways, including the abstract notion of flow categories/multimodules/homotopies/concatenations enriched in so-called regular stratification categories and their lifts to different categories. Concrete examples of such regular stratification categories will appear in the geometric construction, including Kuranishi spaces, derived orbifolds, pseudomanifolds, etc. We also formulate the abstract mechanism for deriving chain-level structures from flow categories/multimodules/homotopies. Lastly, we provide the FOP perturbation method as a blackbox theorem which can be directly applied.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>Regular Stratification Categories</h3>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1. </span>Regular posets</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The purpose of this subsection is to introduce notions associated with partially ordered sets which will be used to define the index sets of stratifications of various moduli spaces coming from geometric constructions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.1.1. </span>Partially ordered sets</h5>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The term “partially ordered set” is abbreviated as <span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">poset</span>, which is always assumed to be countable. The partial order relations are denoted by <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\preceq</annotation></semantics></math>, etc. A poset map is a map of the underlying sets which respects the partial orders.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a poset <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\max}=A^{\rm top}\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>top</mi></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\max}=A^{\rm top}\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math> be the subset of maximal elements. A poset <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has a canonical <span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Alexandrov topology</span>: a subset <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math> is Alexandrov open if <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in U</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> imply that <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in U</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, poset maps are continuous under the Alexandrov topology. A special class of closed subset indexed by <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in A</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}A=\{\beta\in A\ |\ \beta\leq\alpha\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}A=\{\beta\in A\ |\ \beta\leq\alpha\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">is used frequently in this paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our convention is opposite from that of Abouzaid <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, where he regards top strata as minimal elements of the labelling poset.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The product of finitely many posets carries a canonically induced partial order from the lexicographic order. Indeed, if <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are posets, then the relation</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{k})\leq(\beta_{1},\ldots,\beta_{k})\ \text{if and only if}\ \alpha_{i}\leq\beta_{i}\ \forall i=1,\ldots,k," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>if and only if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{1},\ldots,\alpha_{k})\leq(\beta_{1},\ldots,\beta_{k})\ \text{if and only if}\ \alpha_{i}\leq\beta_{i}\ \forall i=1,\ldots,k,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">is a partial order on <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{1}\times\cdots\times A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}\times\cdots\times A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_notation">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Notation 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be a countable subset. Let <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(S)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(S)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of all finite subsets of <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> whose partial order is <math id="S2.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta\Longrightarrow\beta\subseteq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta\Longrightarrow\beta\subseteq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. So its maximal element is the empty set.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we introduce the kind of posets which can model manifolds with corners.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Homogeneous posets)</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A poset <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">homogeneous</span> if for each <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, the length of a maximal sequence of elements <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha_{0}&lt;\alpha_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha_{0}&lt;\alpha_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}\in A^{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}\in A^{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, is finite and only depends on <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (but not the maximal string and <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>). This length is called the <span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">depth</span> or <span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">codimension</span> of <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm depth}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm depth}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in A^{\max}\Longleftrightarrow{\rm depth}(\alpha)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in A^{\max}\Longleftrightarrow{\rm depth}(\alpha)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A poset map between homogeneous posets is called <span id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">homogeneous of degree <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span> if the map increases the depth function by <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a homogeneous poset <math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}:=\{\beta&lt;\gamma\ |\ {\rm depth}(\beta)={\rm depth}(\gamma)+1\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}:=\{\beta&lt;\gamma\ |\ {\rm depth}(\beta)={\rm depth}(\gamma)+1\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}:=\{\beta\in\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}\ |\ \alpha\leq\beta&lt;\gamma\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}:=\{\beta\in\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}\ |\ \alpha\leq\beta&lt;\gamma\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.4</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A homogeneous poset <math id="S2.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S2.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">regular</span> if every <math id="S2.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is always a finite set (but not necessarily <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The natural map to the set of subsets of <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}:\partial^{\gamma}A\to A^{(\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma})},\ \alpha\mapsto\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}:\partial^{\gamma}A\to A^{(\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma})},\ \alpha\mapsto\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is injective.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any finite subset <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\mathbb{Face}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcap_{\beta\in S}\partial^{\beta}A=\left\{\begin{array}[]{cc}\emptyset,&amp;S\notin{\rm Im}f_{\gamma},\\
\partial^{\alpha}A,&amp;S=f_{\gamma}(\alpha)\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcap_{\beta\in S}\partial^{\beta}A=\left\{\begin{array}[]{cc}\emptyset,&amp;S\notin{\rm Im}f_{\gamma},\\
\partial^{\alpha}A,&amp;S=f_{\gamma}(\alpha)\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We often need to identify the faces that are only adjacent to one top stratum.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.5</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a regular poset.</p>
<ol id="S2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">true boundary stratum</span> of <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is an element <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in A</annotation></semantics></math> of depth <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> which has only one top stratum above. The <span id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">true boundary</span> of <math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is the Alexandrov closure of the set of true boundary strata.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A regular poset is called <span id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">normal</span> if each depth-one element is either adjacent to one top stratum (true boundary) or adjacent to two top strata (fake boundary).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.6</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The poset <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(S)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(S)}</annotation></semantics></math> in Notation <a href="#S2.Thmthm2" title="Notation 2.2. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> is regular with depth function given by <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm depth}(\alpha)=\#\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm depth}(\alpha)=\#\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, the poset of three elements <math id="S2.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta&lt;\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta&lt;\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous but not regular.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We prove several important properties of regular posets.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.7</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Properties of regular posets)<span id="S2.Thmthm7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a regular poset. Then the following is true.</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Any Alexandrov closed subset or Alexandrov open subset is also regular.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="S2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the natural map</span></p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma\alpha}:\{\beta\in A\ |\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma\}\to A^{(\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma})},\ \beta\mapsto\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma\alpha}:\{\beta\in A\ |\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma\}\to A^{(\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma})},\ \beta\mapsto\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is a homogeneous bijection.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="S2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm depth}(\alpha)={\rm depth}(\gamma)+\#\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm depth}(\alpha)={\rm depth}(\gamma)+\#\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="S2.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, there is a canonical bijection</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\setminus\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}\cong\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\setminus\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}\cong\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I4.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, when </span><math id="S2.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the composition </span><math id="S2.I4.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}\to\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\to\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}\to\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\to\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i4.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> coincides with the inclusion </span><math id="S2.I4.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}\to\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>δ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}\to\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> defined from the above bijection.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S2.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:A\to A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:A\to A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a homogeneous poset injection to another regular poset </span><math id="S2.I4.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then for any </span><math id="S2.I4.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S2.I4.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the induced map </span><math id="S2.I4.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\to\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\to\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I4.i5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a bijection.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">(1) follows from the definition of the Alexandrov topology and the definition of regular posets. For (2), we show that the <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is bijective. By the definition of regular posets, this is an injection. For surjectivity, assume on the contrary that <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is not in the range of <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it is not in the range of <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> either. By the definition of regular posets, we must have</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcap_{\beta\in S}\partial^{\beta}A=\emptyset." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcap_{\beta\in S}\partial^{\beta}A=\emptyset.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">However, the above intersection at least contains <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction. Hence <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective. Moreover, it is clear that <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is a poset map. One can verify that <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous by an easy inductive argument. Then (3) follows from the homogeneity condition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (4), for any <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\setminus\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\setminus\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\lambda}A\cap\partial^{\beta}A=\partial^{\lambda}A\cap\bigcap_{\tau\in\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}}\partial^{\tau}A." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\lambda}A\cap\partial^{\beta}A=\partial^{\lambda}A\cap\bigcap_{\tau\in\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}}\partial^{\tau}A.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then the subset <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda\}\cup\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}\subseteq\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda\}\cup\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}\subseteq\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, under the inverse of <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\gamma\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\gamma\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives an element <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> whose depth is one bigger than that of <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, hence defines a map from <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\setminus\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\setminus\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can verify that this is a bijection.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (5), the homogeneity condition implies that <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> induces an injection from <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by (3), we have</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\#\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}={\rm depth}(\gamma)-{\rm depth}(\alpha)={\rm depth}(i(\gamma))-{\rm depth}(i(\alpha))=\#\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\#\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}={\rm depth}(\gamma)-{\rm depth}(\alpha)={\rm depth}(i(\gamma))-{\rm depth}(i(\alpha))=\#\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">which shows that the induced map is a bijection.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to check that regular posets admit finite products (Cartesian product) and finite coproducts (disjoint union).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.8</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The category of regular posets, denoted by <math id="S2.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}</annotation></semantics></math>, has objects being countable regular posets and morphisms being injective homogeneous poset maps.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2.9</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a distributive monoidal category with respect to the direct product and disjoint union, whose units are posets with a single element.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is straightforward from checking the definitions.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2. </span>Regular stratification categories and presentations</h4>

<div id="S2.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.10</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">regular stratification category</span> is a distributive monoidal category <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> together with a distributive monoidal functor <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}</annotation></semantics></math>, called the <span id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">forgetful functor</span>, satisfying the following properties. In the following, we say an object <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> an <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object if the forgetful functor sends <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.Thmthm10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="S2.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is an initial object which is <math id="S2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any morphism <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:A\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:A\to B</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a canonical “pullback,” which is an <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}K</annotation></semantics></math>, together with a canonical morphism <math id="S2.I5.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}:f^{*}K\to K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}:f^{*}K\to K</annotation></semantics></math>. The pullback needs to satisfy the functoriality condition. Namely, the composition of pullbacks is the pullback by the composition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.I5.i2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I5.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, for any <math id="S2.I5.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object <math id="S2.I5.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I5.i2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in A</annotation></semantics></math> there is a <span id="S2.I5.i2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">restriction</span> <math id="S2.I5.i2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}K</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="S2.I5.i2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As we will see below, there are a few examples of regular stratification categories such as those of regularly stratified topological spaces (with morphisms being embeddings), regularly stratified topological/smooth manifolds, regularly stratified Kuranishi charts, and Kuranishi presentations. On the other hand, if <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is any category, then the product <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}\times\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}\times\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a regular stratification category with respect to the obvious forgetful functor.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3. </span>Stratified spaces, manifolds, and pseudomanifolds</h4>

<section id="S2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.3.1. </span>Regularly stratified spaces</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although we can define stratified spaces in general, in this paper all such spaces have strata indexed by regular posets. Therefore, we restrict to this situation. We will specify a regular stratification category <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math> of regularly stratified topological spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.11</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a countable regular poset. An <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-stratified space</span> (<math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-space for short) is a locally compact, Hausdorff and second countable topological space <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> endowed with a map</p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s:X\to A" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s:X\to A</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is continuous with respect to the Alexandrov topology on <math id="S2.Thmthm11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> whose range is finite.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, we can write</p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in A}X_{\alpha},\ {\rm where}\ X_{\alpha}:=s^{-1}(\alpha)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>where</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in A}X_{\alpha},\ {\rm where}\ X_{\alpha}:=s^{-1}(\alpha),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which satisfies the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S2.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="S2.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (called a <span id="S2.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stratum</span>) is locally closed.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All but finitely many strata are empty.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S2.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, the subset</p>
<table id="S2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X:=\bigsqcup_{\beta\leq\alpha}X_{\beta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X:=\bigsqcup_{\beta\leq\alpha}X_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I6.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is a closed set (which may contain the closure of <math id="S2.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> properly<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                        
                        
                        
                      This condition is weaker than the “axiom of frontier:” <math id="footnote6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}\cap\overline{X_{\beta}}\neq\emptyset\Longrightarrow X_{\alpha}\subseteq\overline{X_{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}\cap\overline{X_{\beta}}\neq\emptyset\Longrightarrow X_{\alpha}\subseteq\overline{X_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is part of the usual definition of a stratification.</span></span></span>). Note that this condition follows from the continuity of <math id="S2.I6.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.12</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An open subset of an <math id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified space is still regarded as <math id="S2.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified, although the subset may have more empty strata.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the following notions for stratified spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.13</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Category of regularly stratified spaces)</p>
<ol id="S2.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A map from an <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to an <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="74.98" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-58.06730383079511px" version="1.1" viewBox="18.93 58.07 98.12 74.98" width="98.12"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 18.92507892765411 74.9791600454459) translate(0,3.46) translate(18.93,0)"><g transform="translate(-13.53,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{X_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{X_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.529522976176578 -0.27673578005007266 L 13.529522976176578 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(22.74,0) translate(0,8.46) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="6.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.74,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.529522976176578 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.73830219467794 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.73830219467794 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.73830219467794 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-18.93,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{s_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{s_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.74,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{X_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{X_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 59.99106827721781 -9.685900096859001 L 60.544539837317956 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(60.27,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{s_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">s</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{s_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(60.27,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 59.99106827721781 -33.208800332088 L 60.544539837317956 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 59.99106827721781 -33.208800332088 L 60.544539837317956 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-12.44,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{A_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{A_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.443714556199842 -43.63264139549389 L 12.443714556199842 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(24.03,0) translate(0,-50.71) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.2)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.46em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.41)" width="3.91"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{i}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(47.82,0) translate(0,-43.36)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.443714556199842 -43.63264139549389 L 47.824089501068045 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 47.824089501068045 -43.63264139549389 L 47.824089501068045 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(47.82,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{A_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{A_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I7.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:A_{1}\to A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:A_{1}\to A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a morphism in <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous map. We usually call such a map a <span id="S2.I7.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stratified map</span> to emphasize that it respects the stratifications.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A stratified map <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X_{1}\to X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X_{1}\to X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as above is called an <span id="S2.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">embedding</span> if <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a homeomorphism onto its image. <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is called an <span id="S2.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">open embedding</span> if it is an embedding with an open image; it is called a homeomorphism if <math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is a homeomorphism of topological spaces and the underlying poset map is an isomorphism.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S2.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The category <math id="S2.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the category of topological spaces stratified by regular posets whose morphisms are stratified embeddings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S2.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a topological group. A <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action on an <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> which preserves each stratum. In this case, the <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}A</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X</annotation></semantics></math> has an induced <math id="S2.I7.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.3.2. </span>Notations for corners</h5>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to define stratified pseudomanifolds, we need to fix the notations for corners. Let <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive real number. The model for collars is the space <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,\epsilon)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\epsilon)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> which is stratified by subsets of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math>. More generally, for any finite set <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, consider</p>
<table id="S2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,\epsilon)^{S}=\{(x_{a})_{a\in S}\ |\ x_{a}\in[0,\epsilon)\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\epsilon)^{S}=\{(x_{a})_{a\in S}\ |\ x_{a}\in[0,\epsilon)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is stratified by <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(S)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(S)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.14</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a countable regular poset.</p>
<ol id="S2.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is said to <span id="S2.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">have corners</span> if for each <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and each maximal <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A^{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A^{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a <span id="S2.I8.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">corner chart</span>, i.e., a stratified open embedding onto an open neighborhood of <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.Ex18.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="71.56" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-57.20105559825567px" version="1.1" viewBox="53.80 57.20 175.51 71.56" width="175.51"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 53.80054356168708 71.55692212822791) translate(0,3.46) translate(53.8,0)"><g transform="translate(-53.8,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.18em;--ltx-fo-height:0.88em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.18)" width="99.3"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 53.80054356168708 -0.27673578005007266 L 53.80054356168708 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(62.62,0) translate(0,7.18) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="7.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\varphi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\varphi}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(87.01,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 53.80054356168708 -0.27673578005007266 L 87.00934389377508 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 87.00934389377508 -0.27673578005007266 L 87.00934389377508 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.15)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.15384166607211 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.15384166607211 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.15384166607211" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(87.01,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.91em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="26.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}X\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}X\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 104.08350024890385 -7.610350076103501 L 104.636971809004 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(104.36,0) translate(0,-35.83)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 104.08350024890385 -35.830579952727184 L 104.636971809004 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 104.08350024890385 -35.830579952727184 L 104.636971809004 -35.830579952727184" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-46.58,0) translate(0,-46.13) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.13em;--ltx-fo-height:0.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.29)" width="84.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\{\alpha\}\times A^{(\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma})}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\{\alpha\}\times A^{(\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma})}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.57868347970285 -46.408191267609745 L 46.57868347970285 -45.8547197075096" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(88.1,0) translate(0,-46.13)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.57868347970285 -46.408191267609745 L 88.09515231375181 -45.8547197075096" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 88.09515231375181 -46.408191267609745 L 88.09515231375181 -45.8547197075096" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(88.1,0) translate(0,-46.13) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="24.23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}A}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I8.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{x,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{x,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open neighborhood of <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is stratified by <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha\}</annotation></semantics></math>). Here the underlying poset map, whose image is <math id="S2.I8.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta\in A\ |\ \alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma\}\subseteq\partial^{\gamma}A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta\in A\ |\ \alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma\}\subseteq\partial^{\gamma}A</annotation></semantics></math>, is the inverse of the isomorphism (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In item 2 ‣ Lemma 2.7 (Properties of regular posets). ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-stratified manifold</span> is an <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified space <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> which has corners such that each <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (the “interior” of <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X</annotation></semantics></math>) is a topological manifold.<span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        It follows from this condition that each <math id="footnote7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X</annotation></semantics></math> is a topological manifold with boundary whose interior is <math id="footnote7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> A <span id="S2.I8.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">smooth structure</span> on an <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified manifold <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> consists of smooth structures on all <math id="S2.I8.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and a maximal atlas of corner charts which are smoothly compatible.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then we can define the notion of smooth functions, tensors, vector bundles, Lie group actions, on smooth <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-manifolds. We omit the details. Moreover, we obtain a regular stratification category <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Man}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Man}}</annotation></semantics></math> of topological manifolds and a regular stratification category <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}</annotation></semantics></math> of smooth manifolds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.3.3. </span>Stratified pseudomanifolds</h5>

<div id="S2.Thmthm15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.15</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm15.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional <span id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">pseudomanifold</span> is a topological space <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> with a partition <math id="S2.Thmthm15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M={\rm Int}M\sqcup\delta M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M={\rm Int}M\sqcup\delta M</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<ol id="S2.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Int}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Int}M</annotation></semantics></math> is open, dense, and itself an <math id="S2.I9.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional topological manifold.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta M</annotation></semantics></math> admits a partition into topological manifolds of dimensions at most <math id="S2.I9.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.16</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm16.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a countable regular poset. An <math id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-stratified <math id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional pseudomanifold</span> is an <math id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified space <math id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> together with partitions <math id="S2.Thmthm16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}={\rm Int}X_{\alpha}\sqcup\delta X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}={\rm Int}X_{\alpha}\sqcup\delta X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<ol id="S2.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S2.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}={\rm Int}X_{\alpha}\sqcup\delta X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊔</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}={\rm Int}X_{\alpha}\sqcup\delta X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is a pseudomanifold of dimension <math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-{\rm depth}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>depth</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-{\rm depth}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S2.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and each maximal <math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A^{\rm max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A^{\rm max}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a corner chart</p>
<table id="S2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\to\partial^{\gamma}X" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\to\partial^{\gamma}X</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I10.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which sends <math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\rm Int}U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Int</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Int}U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta U_{x,\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Int}\partial^{\gamma}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Int}\partial^{\gamma}X</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(\partial^{\gamma}X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(\partial^{\gamma}X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that a stratified zero-dimensional pseudomanifold is a discrete collection of points and a stratified 1-dimensional pseudomanifold is a disjoint union of 1-manifolds (with boundary).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmthm17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmthm17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.17</span></span><span id="S2.Thmthm17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmthm17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An embedding of stratified pseudomanifolds from <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an embedding of stratified spaces <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X_{1}\to X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X_{1}\to X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f({\rm Int}X_{1})\subseteq{\rm Int}(X_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f({\rm Int}X_{1})\subseteq{\rm Int}(X_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\delta X_{1})\subseteq\delta X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\delta X_{1})\subseteq\delta X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The category of stratified pseudomanifolds, denoted by <math id="S2.Thmthm17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, has objects being stratified pseudomanifolds and morphisms being embeddings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One can check that <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a regular stratification category (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Definition 2.10. ‣ 2.2. Regular stratification categories and presentations ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Kuranishi Spaces</h3>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Kuranishi theory for moduli spaces of pseudoholomorphic curves originated from the efforts of extending the definition of symplectic Gromov–Witten invariants and Hamiltonian Floer homology to full generality. It is based on the fundamental fact that the Cauchy–Riemann operator is elliptic. Fukaya–Ono <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite> firstly introduced the package of Kuranishi structures, alongside another finite-dimensional reduction approach of Li–Tian <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> (see also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>). While the method of Kuranishi structures was further developed by Fukaya–Oh–Ohta–Ono (see the comprehensive treatment in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>) together with closely related works by McDuff–Wehrheim <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>, <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>, <a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">48</a>]</cite>, there are alternate approaches with considerable novelties, including the algebraic version of Pardon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite> as well as the more recent “global chart construction” of Abouzaid–McLean–Smith <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> (followed up by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The AMS construction was adopted by the authors in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> in the Gromov–Witten setting and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> in the Hamiltonian Floer setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the category of Kuranishi charts in topological, smooth, or stably complex categories. When the discussion can be unified in the three cases, we simply use <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>. See below for the detailed definitions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1. </span>Kuranishi spaces</h4>

<div id="S3.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a countable regular poset.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified <span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(topological) Kuranishi space</span> (K-space for short) is a quadruple <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a compact Lie group, <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold with a continuous <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action, <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to V</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle, and <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:V\to E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:V\to E</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant section, such that the <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> has only finite stabilizers.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A Kuranishi space <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be <span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">smooth</span> if <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold, the <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action is smooth, and <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to V</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth equivariant vector bundle (we do not impose any smoothness condition on <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.1. </span>Morphisms of Kuranishi spaces</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to define a regular stratification category (see Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Definition 2.10. ‣ 2.2. Regular stratification categories and presentations ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>), we need to specify morphisms. We first define a general form of maps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict map</span> of smooth/topological Kuranishi spaces from <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}=(G_{1},V_{1},E_{1},S_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}=(G_{1},V_{1},E_{1},S_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}=(G_{2},V_{2},E_{2},S_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}=(G_{2},V_{2},E_{2},S_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of a Lie group homomorphism <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{G}:G_{1}\to G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{G}:G_{1}\to G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and a commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="80.53" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-61.9451940612244px" version="1.1" viewBox="37.63 61.95 134.13 80.53" width="134.13"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 37.63097771243038 80.53448250700498) translate(0,3.46) translate(37.63,0)"><g transform="translate(-12.76,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{E_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{E_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.760798400313062 -0.27673578005007266 L 12.760798400313062 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(18.18,0) translate(0,9.29) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.9)" width="14.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}^{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">E</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}^{E}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.1,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.760798400313062 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.104155620038135 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.104155620038135 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.104155620038135 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.1,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.22"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{E_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{E_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.58819712671449 -9.685900096859001 L 59.14166868681463 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(58.87,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.58819712671449 -33.208800332088 L 59.14166868681463 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.58819712671449 -33.208800332088 L 59.14166868681463 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-12.83,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.25em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.35"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-37.63,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="8" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="12.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{S_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">S</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{S_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-11.52,0) translate(0,-9.69)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.54 -3.56" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.28 -7.09" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 -43.355905615443824 C -22.139179107805365 -28.903908925513697 -22.139179107805365 -14.451954462756849 0 0" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.828066287338281 -43.63264139549389 L 12.828066287338281 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(18.18,0) translate(0,-52.65) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.9)" width="14.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}^{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}^{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.04,0) translate(0,-43.36)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.828066287338281 -43.63264139549389 L 46.036866619426284 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.036866619426284 -43.63264139549389 L 46.036866619426284 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.04,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.25em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.35"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{V_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{V_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(75.47,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="8" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="12.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{S_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">S</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{S_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(70.39,0) translate(0,-9.69)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.28 -7.09" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 6.54 -3.56" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.864932906764565 -43.355905615443824 C 81.00413312815657 -28.903908925513697 81.00413312815657 -14.451954462756849 58.864932906764565 0" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is an equivariant smooth/continuous map and <math id="S3.Thmthm2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>E</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is an equivariant smooth/continuous bundle map.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that strict maps can be composed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We list a few special kinds of strict maps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conjugation)<span id="S3.Thmthm3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> be a K-chart. The <span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">conjugation</span> of <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math> is the strict map <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{g}:K\to K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{g}:K\to K</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{g}^{G}:G\to G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{g}^{G}:G\to G</annotation></semantics></math> is the conjugation <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\mapsto g^{-1}hg" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\mapsto g^{-1}hg</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{g}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{g}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{g}^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{g}^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the action of the form <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto g^{-1}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto g^{-1}x</annotation></semantics></math>. Two strict maps <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21},\iota_{21}^{\prime}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21},\iota_{21}^{\prime}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are said to be <span id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">conjugate</span> if there exists <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{2}\in G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{2}\in G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.Thmthm3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{\prime}=\iota_{g_{2}}\circ\iota_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{\prime}=\iota_{g_{2}}\circ\iota_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stabilization)<span id="S3.Thmthm4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified K-chart. Let <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{N}:N\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{N}:N\to V</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant continuous resp. smooth vector bundle and let <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subseteq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subseteq N</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant open (disk) subbundle.<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
                    
                    
                    
                  When we talk about disk bundles, we always assume that it is a subset of a certain vector bundle, although it may not appear so in notations.</span></span></span> The <span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stabilization</span> of <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{D}(K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{D}(K)</annotation></semantics></math>, is the <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified K-chart</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{D}(K)=(G,D,\pi_{N}^{*}E\oplus\pi_{N}^{*}N,\pi_{N}^{*}S\oplus\tau_{N})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{D}(K)=(G,D,\pi_{N}^{*}E\oplus\pi_{N}^{*}N,\pi_{N}^{*}S\oplus\tau_{N})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{N}:N\to\pi_{N}^{*}N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{N}:N\to\pi_{N}^{*}N</annotation></semantics></math> is the tautological section. By abuse of language, we also call the morphism</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{D}:K\to{\rm Stab}_{D}(K)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{D}:K\to{\rm Stab}_{D}(K)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">induced by the zero section <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\to D</annotation></semantics></math> and the obvious bundle embedding <math id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to\pi_{N}^{*}E\oplus\pi_{N}^{*}N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to\pi_{N}^{*}E\oplus\pi_{N}^{*}N</annotation></semantics></math> a <span id="S3.Thmthm4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stabilization morphism</span>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.5</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Shrinking and open embedding)<span id="S3.Thmthm5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> be a K-chart. A <span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">shrinking</span> of <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is a K-chart <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}=(G,V^{\prime},E^{\prime},S^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}=(G,V^{\prime},E^{\prime},S^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\prime}\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\prime}\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant open neighborhood of <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\prime}=E|_{V^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\prime}=E|_{V^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.I2.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=S|_{V^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=S|_{V^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A morphism <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is called an <span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">open embedding</span> if the underlying poset map is an isomorphism onto an Alexandrov open subset, the map <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}\to V_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}\to V_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism onto an open subset, and the bundle map is an isomorphism of vector bundles when restricted to the open subset identified with <math id="S3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.6</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Group enlargement)<span id="S3.Thmthm6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> be a K-chart. A <span id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">group enlargement</span> of <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> by a Lie group embedding <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\hookrightarrow G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\hookrightarrow G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a K-chart</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}\times_{G}K=(G^{\prime},G^{\prime}\times_{G}V,G^{\prime}\times_{G}E,S^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}\times_{G}K=(G^{\prime},G^{\prime}\times_{G}V,G^{\prime}\times_{G}E,S^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}:G^{\prime}\times_{G}V\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}:G^{\prime}\times_{G}V\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}E</annotation></semantics></math> is the section naturally induced from <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. By abuse of language, the K-chart morphism</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}K" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">induced from the natural maps <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to G^{\prime}\times_{G}E</annotation></semantics></math> is also called a group enlargement.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the morphism which will be used most frequently in this paper is a combination of the above more elementary kinds.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.7</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Morphisms of Kuranishi spaces)<span id="S3.Thmthm7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict morphism</span> or <span id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict embedding</span> of Kuranishi spaces from <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a strict map <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that there exists a commutative diagram of strict maps</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<span id="S3.E1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_align_bottom"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.E1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="71.15" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-57.212119117653415px" version="1.1" viewBox="18.45 57.21 96.49 71.15" width="96.49"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 18.447025099021033 71.15287142075722) translate(18.45,0)"><g transform="translate(-13.63,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{K_{3}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{K_{3}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.625610908961187 -0.27673578005007266 L 13.625610908961187 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(21.49,0) translate(0,6.97) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.35)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.66em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.64" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="9.17"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\iota_{b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\iota_{b}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.83,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.625610908961187 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.83441124104919 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.83441124104919 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.83441124104919 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.83,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{K_{4}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{K_{4}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 60.18328636996031 -9.685900096859001 L 60.73675793006045 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(60.46,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.67em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="9.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\iota_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\iota_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(60.46,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 60.18328636996031 -33.208800332088 L 60.73675793006045 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 60.18328636996031 -33.208800332088 L 60.73675793006045 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-13.63,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{K_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{K_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-18.45,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.73em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\iota_{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\iota_{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(0,-9.69)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.625610908961187 -43.63264139549389 L 13.625610908961187 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(18.98,0) translate(0,-50.28) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="14.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.83,0) translate(0,-43.36)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.625610908961187 -43.63264139549389 L 46.83441124104919 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.83441124104919 -43.63264139549389 L 46.83441124104919 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.83,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.E1.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{K_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{K_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stabilization by a disk bundle, <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> is a group enlargement, and <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open embedding. It implies in particular the group morphism <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, the base map <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{V}:V_{1}\to V_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{V}:V_{1}\to V_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the bundle map <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{E}:E_{1}\to E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{E}:E_{1}\to E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, are all embeddings.
A conjugacy class of strict morphisms from <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is called a <span id="S3.Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">morphism</span>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 3.8</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The above definition basically says that a morphism <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an embedding if (up to group enlargement) the domain map is an embedding and the restriction of <math id="S3.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to a neighborhood of the embedding image is isomorphic to a stabilization. One can also define a weaker “infinitesimal version” of K-chart embeddings. In the smooth category one can prove that the infinitesimal version is equivalent to the above definition. However, in the topological category it may not be so.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">One can check that compositions of embeddings are still embeddings, which ultimately follows from the fact that every <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle over <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}/G</annotation></semantics></math> for a group embedding <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\hookrightarrow G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\hookrightarrow G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is induced from a <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representation. Also notice that stabilization maps, open embeddings, and group enlargements are all special cases of embeddings.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.9</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The categories of regularly stratified topological and smooth Kuranishi spaces, denoted by <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, are the categories whose objects are stratified Kuranishi charts in the topological and smooth categories and whose morphisms are embeddings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3.10</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and <math id="S3.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}</annotation></semantics></math> are regular stratification categories.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Disjoint union and direct product make the category <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math> distributive monoidal, with monoidal unit being the singleton <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0}=(\{0\},{\rm pt},0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>pt</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0}=(\{0\},{\rm pt},0,0)</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, one can obviously take pullbacks of any <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified Kuranishi space with respect to homogeneous poset maps <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:B\to A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:B\to A</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.2. </span>Free quotients</h5>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is another relation among Kuranishi spaces which will appear in the construction. This notion first appeared as <span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">group enlargement</span> in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Section 4]</cite> and then showed up as <span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">free quotient</span> in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Lemma 3.5]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.11</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\sim}=(G^{\sim},V^{\sim},E^{\sim},S^{\sim})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\sim}=(G^{\sim},V^{\sim},E^{\sim},S^{\sim})</annotation></semantics></math> be a (topological or smooth) Kuranishi space where <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\sim}=G\times G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\sim}=G\times G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the product of two compact Lie groups. Suppose the <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math> is free. Then the <span id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">free quotient</span> of <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Kuranishi space</p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=K/G^{\prime}:=(G,V^{\sim}/G^{\prime},E^{\sim}/G^{\prime},S^{\sim}/G^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=K/G^{\prime}:=(G,V^{\sim}/G^{\prime},E^{\sim}/G^{\prime},S^{\sim}/G^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that there is a natural strict morphism (which is not an embedding) from <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>∼</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\sim}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>. We also call the morphism a free quotient by <math id="S3.Thmthm11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>Rigidified embeddings</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our geometric construction we can obtain objects and morphisms living in a more rigid category of Kuranishi charts. In short, we only allow the stabilization to be a product bundle coming from a <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.12</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be a strict embedding.</p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidification</span> (which may not exist) of <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> (viewed as a <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{21}:\underline{\smash{W}}_{21}\to V_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{21}:\underline{\smash{W}}_{21}\to V_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>), a <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant open neighborhood <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{21}\subseteq W_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{21}\subseteq W_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> of the origin (viewed as a disk bundle over <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>), and an open embedding <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}:G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}(K_{1})\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}:G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}(K_{1})\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the diagram (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In Definition 3.7 (Morphisms of Kuranishi spaces). ‣ 3.1.1. Morphisms of Kuranishi spaces ‣ 3.1. Kuranishi spaces ‣ 3. Kuranishi Spaces ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>) is realized by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 31.01587pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-31.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}(K_{1})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 36.70277pt\raise 5.03749pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-0.9764pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\iota_{b}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 55.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 55.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}(K_{1})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 101.40936pt\raise-15.83333pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.93056pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\theta_{21}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 101.40936pt\raise-24.33334pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-9.84723pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{K_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-13.33167pt\raise-15.83333pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.00694pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\iota_{a}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-8.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 42.5721pt\raise-36.6736pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.00694pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 91.56213pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 91.56213pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{K_{2}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-57.67336653132351px" height="71.61" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="42.92 57.67 247.43 71.61" width="247.43"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 42.916658559049395 71.61411883442732) translate(42.92,0)"> <g transform="translate(-42.92,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="77.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 42.916679672636036 -0.27673578005007266 L 42.916679672636036 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(50.79,0) translate(0,6.97) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.35)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.66em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.11em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.64" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="9.17"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">b</mi></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(76.13,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 42.916679672636036 -0.27673578005007266 L 76.1254588911374 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 76.1254588911374 -0.27673578005007266 L 76.1254588911374 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(76.13,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="120.09"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 140.04340091978216 -11.069600110696001 L 140.5968724798823 -11.069600110696001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(140.32,0) translate(0,-21.91) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.67)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.11em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.11" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="15.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">θ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(140.32,0) translate(0,-33.67)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 140.04340091978216 -33.6700477457581 L 140.5968724798823 -11.069600110696001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 140.04340091978216 -33.6700477457581 L 140.5968724798823 -33.6700477457581" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(-13.63,0) translate(0,-43.82) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.6700477457581 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.6700477457581" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(-18.45,0) translate(0,-21.91) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.73em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">a</mi></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(0,-11.07)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.6700477457581 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.069600110696001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -11.069600110696001 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.069600110696001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.625610908961187 -44.093888809163985 L 13.625610908961187 -43.54041724906384" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(58.91,0) translate(0,-50.75) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="14.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ι</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(126.7,0) translate(0,-43.82)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.625610908961187 -44.093888809163985 L 126.69452579087104 -43.54041724906384" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 126.69452579087104 -44.093888809163985 L 126.69452579087104 -43.54041724906384" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(126.7,0) translate(0,-43.82) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="18.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 31.01587pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-31.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}(K_{1})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 36.70277pt\raise 5.03749pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-0.9764pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\iota_{b}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 55.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 55.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}(K_{1})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 101.40936pt\raise-15.83333pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.93056pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\theta_{21}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 101.40936pt\raise-24.33334pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-9.84723pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{K_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-13.33167pt\raise-15.83333pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.00694pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\iota_{a}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-8.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 42.5721pt\raise-36.6736pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.00694pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\iota_{21}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 91.56213pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 91.56213pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{K_{2}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We denote the rigidification by <math id="S3.I3.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{21}\subseteq W_{21},\theta_{21})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{21}\subseteq W_{21},\theta_{21})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two rigidifications <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{21}\subseteq W_{21},\theta_{21})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{21}\subseteq W_{21},\theta_{21})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{21}^{\prime}\subseteq W_{21}^{\prime},\theta_{21}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{21}^{\prime}\subseteq W_{21}^{\prime},\theta_{21}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> are called <span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">equivalent</span> if there exists an isomorphism <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:W_{21}\cong W_{21}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>≅</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:W_{21}\cong W_{21}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of representations, which induces an isomorphism of K-charts</p>
<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}K_{1}\cong{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}^{\prime}}K_{1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}K_{1}\cong{\rm Stab}_{D_{21}^{\prime}}K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">such that after shrinking <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{21}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{21}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> properly, as K-chart morphisms one has</p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}=\theta_{21}^{\prime}\circ\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}=\theta_{21}^{\prime}\circ\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidified embedding</span> from <math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an embedding together with an equivalence class of rigidifications.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that not all embeddings can be rigidified. On the other hand, rigidified embeddings are well-behaved. We prove that the composition of rigidified embeddings is naturally rigidified.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3.13</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be an embedding with a rigidification <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{21}\subseteq W_{21},\theta_{21})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{21}\subseteq W_{21},\theta_{21})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{32}:K_{2}\to K_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{32}:K_{2}\to K_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be an embedding with a rigidification <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D_{32}\subseteq W_{32},\theta_{32})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{32}\subseteq W_{32},\theta_{32})</annotation></semantics></math>. Viewing <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{32}</annotation></semantics></math> as a <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-representation via the group embedding <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}\to G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}\to G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{31}:=W_{21}\oplus W_{32},\ D_{31}:=D_{21}\oplus D_{32}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{31}:=W_{21}\oplus W_{32},\ D_{31}:=D_{21}\oplus D_{32}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define <math id="S3.Thmthm13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{31}:{\rm Stab}_{D_{31}}(K_{1})\to K_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{31}:{\rm Stab}_{D_{31}}(K_{1})\to K_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> as the composition</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.55554pt\hbox{\kern 31.01587pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-31.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\rm Stab}_{D_{31}}(K_{1})\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 52.39087pt\raise 6.15pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.75pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\cong}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 85.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 55.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 85.01587pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{\rm Stab}_{D_{32}}({\rm Stab}_{D_{21}}(K_{1}))\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 193.091pt\raise 6.68332pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-1.17778pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{{\rm Stab}_{D_{32}}\theta_{21}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 243.38492pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 213.38492pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.55554pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 243.38492