<p id="S3.I6.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the right vertical arrow is complex, such that for all <math id="S3.I6.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, the following induced diagram of linear maps commutes.</p>
<table id="S3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.Ex23.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="83.44" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-63.016011834688925px" version="1.1" viewBox="11.09 63.02 86.23 83.44" width="86.23"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 11.093627372288813 83.43519372070448) translate(0,3.46) translate(11.09,0)"><g transform="translate(-11.09,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.77" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.7)" width="13.89"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\check{E}_{x}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\check{E}_{x}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 11.09364848587545 -0.27673578005007266 L 11.09364848587545 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(15.42,0) translate(0,10.21) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.49em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.12" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.7)" width="20.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\check{\tau}_{1,x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">τ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.710em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\check{\tau}_{1,x}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(44.3,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 11.09364848587545 -0.27673578005007266 L 44.30242770437682 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 44.30242770437682 -0.27673578005007266 L 44.30242770437682 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(44.3,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.7)" width="22.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\check{F}_{1,x}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\check{F}_{1,x}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 59.44340295344282 -11.569253138458645 L 59.99687451354296 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(59.72,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 59.44340295344282 -33.208800332088 L 59.99687451354296 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 59.44340295344282 -33.208800332088 L 59.99687451354296 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-11.09,0) translate(0,-42.6) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.77" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.7)" width="13.89"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\check{E}_{x}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\check{E}_{x}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 11.09364848587545 -42.87356572872345 L 11.09364848587545 -42.32009416862331" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(15.42,0) translate(0,-52.81) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.49em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.12" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.7)" width="20.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\check{\tau}_{2,x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">τ</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn><mo mathsize="0.710em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\check{\tau}_{2,x}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(44.3,0) translate(0,-42.6)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 11.09364848587545 -42.87356572872345 L 44.30242770437682 -42.32009416862331" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 44.30242770437682 -42.87356572872345 L 44.30242770437682 -42.32009416862331" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(44.3,0) translate(0,-42.6) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.7)" width="22.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.Ex23.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\check{F}_{2,x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\check{F}_{2,x}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant <span id="S3.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">normal complex structure</span> on <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is a normal equivalence class of stable complex structures. Notice that a normal complex structure on <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> equips each <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{E}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{E}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> with a <math id="S3.I6.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant complex structure.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{1},E_{2}\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{1},E_{2}\to V</annotation></semantics></math> are equipped with <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant normal complex structures. A <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant stable morphism <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:E_{1}\overset{s}{\to}E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑠</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:E_{1}\overset{s}{\to}E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S3.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">normally complex</span> if for each <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, the induced linear map <math id="S3.I6.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{E}_{1,x}\to\check{E}_{2,x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{E}_{1,x}\to\check{E}_{2,x}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex linear.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now we define the notion of normal complex Kuranishi spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmthm24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmthm24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.24</span></span><span id="S3.Thmthm24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmthm24.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">normally complex Kuranishi space</span> (NC Kuranishi space for short) is a smooth Kuranishi space <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with a <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant complex structure on <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant normal complex structure on <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV/{\mathfrak{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>𝔤</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV/{\mathfrak{g}}</annotation></semantics></math>. An <span id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">open embedding</span> of NC Kuranishi spaces from <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}=(G_{1},V_{1},E_{1},S_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}=(G_{1},V_{1},E_{1},S_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}=(G_{2},V_{2},E_{2},S_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}=(G_{2},V_{2},E_{2},S_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth open embedding <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that 1) the vector bundle isomorphism</p>
<table id="S3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\iota_{21}:TV_{1}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{1}\to TV_{2}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\iota_{21}:TV_{1}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{1}\to TV_{2}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is normally complex and 2) the vector bundle isomorphism <math id="S3.Thmthm24.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{E}:E_{1}\to E_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{E}:E_{1}\to E_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex-linear.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">One can again discuss stabilizations (by complex vector bundles), strict embeddings, conjugations, and embeddings of normally complex Kuranishi spaces. Then one obtains a regular stratification category called the category of normally complex Kuranishi spaces, denoted by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and the corresponding rigidified category <math id="S3.SS3.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>NC</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Derived Orbifolds</h3>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we describe another regular stratification category called the category of derived orbifolds. We will consider as general as the smooth category, but not the topological category.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1. </span>Stratified orbifolds</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All orbifolds, unless declared, are assumed to be smooth and effective. They are spaces which are locally modelled by <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U/\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U/\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite group and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is an effective smooth <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold. Orbifolds with boundary and corners are locally modelled on <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U/\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U/\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold with boundary and corners. If <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a regular poset (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm4" title="Definition 2.4. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>), then one can consider the notion of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-orbifold. Without giving the detailed definition, we remind the reader that a smooth effective <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-orbifold contains charts of the form</p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="U_{\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{(\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma})},\ {\rm where\ }\alpha\leq\gamma\in A^{\max}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>where</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\alpha}\times[0,\epsilon)^{(\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma})},\ {\rm where\ }\alpha\leq\gamma\in A^{\max},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold without boundary. Here we always assume that the isotropy group acts trivially on the normal factors. For example, if <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold acted on by a compact Lie group <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with finite stabilizers, then the quotient <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X/G</annotation></semantics></math> is naturally a smooth effective <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-orbifold.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Derived orbifolds)<span id="S4.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a regular poset <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. An <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified <span id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">derived orbifold</span> is a triple <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an effective <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-orbifold, <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth orbifold vector bundle, and <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous section. A derived orbifold <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">compact</span> if the coarse space of <math id="S4.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is a compact topological space.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the case of Kuranishi spaces, we define embeddings of derived orbifolds as combinations of several more basic morphisms.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S4.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified derived orbifold.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">morphism of derived orbifolds</span> from an <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified derived orbifold <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{1}=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{1}=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to an <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified derived orbifold <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{2}=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{2}=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a morphism <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:A_{1}\to A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:A_{1}\to A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf RegPos}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a smooth stratified orbifold map <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}:{\mathcal{U}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}:{\mathcal{U}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a smooth orbibundle map <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\phi}_{21}:{\mathcal{E}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\phi}_{21}:{\mathcal{E}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> covering <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="80.64" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-60.267761830094614px" version="1.1" viewBox="36.42 60.27 130.93 80.64" width="130.93"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 36.41831886393905 80.63891030651118) translate(0,3.46) translate(36.42,0)"><g transform="translate(-11.96,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.13em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="15.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{E}}_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{E}}_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 11.963274892276791 -0.27673578005007266 L 11.963274892276791 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(16,0) translate(0,10.19) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.29em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="17.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\widehat{\phi}_{21}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\widehat{\phi}_{21}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.13,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 11.963274892276791 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.13297566579753 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.13297566579753 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.13297566579753 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.13,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.13em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="15.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{E}}_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{E}}_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 57.819493664437616 -9.685900096859001 L 58.37296522453776 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(58.1,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 57.819493664437616 -33.208800332088 L 58.37296522453776 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 57.819493664437616 -33.208800332088 L 58.37296522453776 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-12.44,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{U}}_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{U}}_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.443714556199842 -43.63264139549389 L 12.443714556199842 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(16.52,0) translate(0,-51.81) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.21em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="16.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\phi_{21}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϕ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\phi_{21}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(45.65,0) translate(0,-43.36)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.443714556199842 -43.63264139549389 L 45.65251488828785 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 45.65251488828785 -43.63264139549389 L 45.65251488828785 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-36.42,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="8" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="11.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{{\mathcal{S}}_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒮</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{{\mathcal{S}}_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-11.52,0) translate(0,-9.69)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.54 -3.56" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.28 -7.09" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 -43.355905615443824 C -22.139179107805365 -28.903908925513697 -22.139179107805365 -14.451954462756849 0 0" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(45.65,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.2em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{U}}_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{U}}_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(74.7,0) translate(0,-21.68) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.62)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="8" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="11.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{{\mathcal{S}}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">𝒮</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{{\mathcal{S}}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(69.62,0) translate(0,-9.69)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.28 -7.09" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 6.54 -3.56" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.09622944448768 -43.355905615443824 C 80.23542966587969 -28.903908925513697 80.23542966587969 -14.451954462756849 58.09622944448768 0" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Such a morphism induces an orbispace map <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{1}^{-1}(0)\to{\mathcal{S}}_{2}^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{1}^{-1}(0)\to{\mathcal{S}}_{2}^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">open embedding of derived orbifolds</span> from <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a morphism such that the poset map <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:A_{1}\to A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:A_{1}\to A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism onto an Alexandrov open subset, the orbifold map <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism onto an open subset, and the bundle map <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\phi}_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\phi}_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism over the image of <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a derived orbifold <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math>, for any open subset <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">shrinking</span> of <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is the derived orbifold <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}},{\mathcal{S}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}},{\mathcal{S}}|_{{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>. It admits a natural open embedding into <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A disk bundle over an orbifold is an open neighborhood of the zero section of an orbifold vector bundle. A <span id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stabilization</span> of a derived orbifold <math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> by a disk bundle <math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> contained in a vector bundle <math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathcal{F}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathcal{F}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the derived orbifold</p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{\mathcal{N}}{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{N}},\pi_{\mathcal{N}}^{*}{\mathcal{E}}\oplus\pi_{\mathcal{N}}^{*}{\mathcal{F}},\pi_{\mathcal{N}}^{*}{\mathcal{S}}\oplus\tau_{\mathcal{F}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{\mathcal{N}}{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{N}},\pi_{\mathcal{N}}^{*}{\mathcal{E}}\oplus\pi_{\mathcal{N}}^{*}{\mathcal{F}},\pi_{\mathcal{N}}^{*}{\mathcal{S}}\oplus\tau_{\mathcal{F}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the tautological section. We call the natural morphism</p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}\to{\rm Stab}_{\mathcal{N}}({\mathcal{D}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}\to{\rm Stab}_{\mathcal{N}}({\mathcal{D}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">the <span id="S4.I1.i4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stabilization morphism</span> by <math id="S4.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">embedding of derived orbifolds</span> from <math id="S4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{1}=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{1}=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{2}=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{2}=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is a morphism <math id="S4.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\phi}}_{21}:{\mathcal{D}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\phi}}_{21}:{\mathcal{D}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that there exists a disk bundle <math id="S4.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}_{21}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}_{21}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and an open embedding <math id="S4.I1.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}:{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{N}}_{21}}({\mathcal{D}}_{1})\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}:{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{N}}_{21}}({\mathcal{D}}_{1})\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> extending <math id="S4.I1.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The category of stratified derived orbifolds, denoted by <math id="S4.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math>, has objects being stratified derived orbifolds and morphisms being embeddings of derived orbifolds.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following is readily checked.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.4</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The category <math id="S4.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a regular stratification category (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Definition 2.10. ‣ 2.2. Regular stratification categories and presentations ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>). ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">One can see that there are functors</p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The first arrow sends <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> to the quotient <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=(V/G,E/G,S/G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=(V/G,E/G,S/G)</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that a conjugacy class of Kuranishi space embeddings induces a well-defined embedding of derived orbifolds. The second arrow is induced by passing to the zero locus <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> of a derived orbifold <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.1. </span>Rigidified embeddings</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to introduce an analogue of rigidified embeddings for orbifolds. We need to relax the triviality requirement. A flat orbifold vector bundle is an orbifold vector bundle together with a flat connection. A key property of flat vector bundles is, if <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is flat and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}\to{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}\to{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> is flat, then <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is canonically a flat bundle over <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For example, if <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a compact Lie group acting on a smooth manifold <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> with only finite stabilizers and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is a representation of <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, then the vector bundle <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V\times W)/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V\times W)/G</annotation></semantics></math> is flat. Notice that the pullback of rigid vector bundles is still rigid.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.5</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}:{\mathcal{D}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}:{\mathcal{D}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be an embedding of derived orbifolds.</p>
<ol id="S4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidification</span> of <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a disk bundle <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> contained in a flat vector bundle <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{21}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{21}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and an open embedding</p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{21}:{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{N}}_{21}}({\mathcal{D}}_{1})\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{21}:{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{N}}_{21}}({\mathcal{D}}_{1})\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which extends <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two rigidifications <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{N}}_{21}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{21},\psi_{21})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{N}}_{21}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{21},\psi_{21})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{N}}_{21}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{21}^{\prime},\psi_{21}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{N}}_{21}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{F}}_{21}^{\prime},\psi_{21}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> are equivalent if there is a flat bundle isomorphism <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:{\mathcal{F}}_{21}\cong{\mathcal{F}}_{21}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>≅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:{\mathcal{F}}_{21}\cong{\mathcal{F}}_{21}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> which identifies <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}_{21}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}_{21}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> after an appropriate shrinking such that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{21}^{\prime}=\psi_{21}\circ\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{21}^{\prime}=\psi_{21}\circ\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidified embedding</span> of derived orbifolds is an embedding together with an equivalence class of rigidifications.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">One can see that rigid derived orbifold embeddings can be composed. Therefore we can define a category of derived orbifolds with rigid embeddings as morphisms. This category is denoted by</p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that there is a quotient functor</p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Normal complex structures</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Normal complex (NC for short) structures are essential for constructing FOP transverse perturbations. We recall the definitions here.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.1. </span>Basic notions</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> acts on a set <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. A subgroup <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\subseteq G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq G</annotation></semantics></math> is called an <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-essential subgroup, denoted by</p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H\subseteq_{A}G" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq_{A}G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">if there exists <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math> whose stabilizer is <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a real representation <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> of a finite group <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">basic decomposition</span> of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is the splitting</p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=V_{\Gamma}\oplus\check{V}_{\Gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=V_{\Gamma}\oplus\check{V}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the direct sum of trivial subrepresentations and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{V}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{V}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the direct sum of nontrivial irreducible subrepresentations. An <span id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NC structure</span> on <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant complex structure on <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{V}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{V}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.2. </span>NC structures</h5>

<div id="S4.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.6</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold and <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to U</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle. An <span id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NC structure</span> on <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> consists of, for each <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>-essential subgroup <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H\subseteq_{U}\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>U</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\subseteq_{U}\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant complex structure <math id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\check{E}_{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\check{E}_{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the subbundle</p>
<table id="S4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{E}_{H}\subseteq E|_{U_{H}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{E}_{H}\subseteq E|_{U_{H}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmthm6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">satisfying the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S4.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> which conjugates <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{\prime}:=gHg^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{\prime}:=gHg^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the bundle isomorphism <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{E}_{H}\to\check{E}_{gHg^{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{E}_{H}\to\check{E}_{gHg^{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> sends <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\check{E}_{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\check{E}_{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\check{E}_{H^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\check{E}_{H^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each pair of <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>-essential subgroups <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq H\subseteq\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq H\subseteq\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, one has the <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant decomposition</p>
<table id="S4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{E}_{H}\cong\check{E}_{K}\oplus(\check{E}_{H}\cap E_{K}|_{U_{H}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{E}_{H}\cong\check{E}_{K}\oplus(\check{E}_{H}\cap E_{K}|_{U_{H}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We require that the restriction of <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\check{E}_{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\check{E}_{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\check{E}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\check{E}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with <math id="S4.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{\check{E}_{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>ˇ</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{\check{E}_{K}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.7</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an effective orbifold and <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an orbifold vector bundle. An <span id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NC structure</span> on <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of, for each bundle chart <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}=(\Gamma,U,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}=(\Gamma,U,E)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math>, an NC structure <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}^{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}^{E}</annotation></semantics></math> on the vector bundle <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, such that chart embeddings respect those complex structures. An <span id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NC structure</span> on <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is by definition an NC structure on <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S4.Thmthm7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">normally complex derived orbifold</span> is a derived orbifold <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> together with NC structures on <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmthm7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4.8</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Embeddings of NC derived orbifolds)<span id="S4.Thmthm8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">open embedding of normally complex derived orbifolds</span> from <math id="S4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an open embedding of derived orbifolds which respects normal complex structures.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A stabilization of an NC derived orbifold is a stabilization by a disk bundle which is contained in a complex orbifold vector bundle.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An embedding of NC derived orbifolds <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:{\mathcal{D}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:{\mathcal{D}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an embedding such that there exists a stabilization of <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by a disk bundle <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{N}}_{21}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{N}}_{21}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and an open embedding from <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{N}}_{21}}({\mathcal{D}}_{1})\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{{\mathcal{N}}_{21}}({\mathcal{D}}_{1})\to{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends <math id="S4.I4.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S4.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidified embedding</span> of NC derived orbifolds from <math id="S4.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a rigidified embedding whose rigidification can be represented by a disk bundle in a rigid complex vector bundle. Two rigidifications are equivalent if they (after appropriate shrinking to smaller disk bundles) differ by an isomorphism of rigid complex vector bundles.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore we obtained the category <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> of normally complex derived orbifolds with morphisms being embeddings and the category <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>NC</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> with the same objects with morphisms being rigidified embeddings. One can see that they are both regular stratification categories.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.9</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There are natural functors of regular stratification categories</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}^{\rm NC}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>NC</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>NC</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}\to\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> be a stably complex Kuranishi space. Then by definition, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> has a <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant complex structure and the vector bundle</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV/\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV/\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">has a <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant stable complex structure. This means there exists a real vector space <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and a complex structure on</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV/\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV/\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the quotient chart</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G:=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G:=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}=V/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}=V/G</annotation></semantics></math>. Given any <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in V</annotation></semantics></math> with stabilizer <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{x}\subseteq G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{x}\subseteq G</annotation></semantics></math>, one has the <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant decomposition</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{x}V\cong T_{x}V_{G_{x}}\oplus N_{x}V_{G_{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{x}V\cong T_{x}V_{G_{x}}\oplus N_{x}V_{G_{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">The stable complex structure on <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV/\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV/\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a complex structure on <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{x}V_{G_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{x}V_{G_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The collection of these complex structures forms a normal complex structure on the quotient orbifold. One can easily check that the morphisms descend to morphisms in <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>NC</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Collars</h3>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Various inductive constructions require moduli spaces, which appear as, e.g., morphism spaces of flow categories, to have compatible collars. While one can possibly discuss collars in an abstract manner, we refrain from doing so. Instead, in this section we only consider the categories with geometric meanings. More precisely, in this section, the category <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the list <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Man}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Man}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math> etc. Following an idea of Fukaya, we explain how to equip the geometric objects of interest with collars “on the outside” which facilitates inductive constructions of various sorts.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>The subcategory of collared objects</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the discussions in this section, let <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive real number. The model for collars is the space <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,\epsilon)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\epsilon)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> which is stratified by subsets of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,k\}</annotation></semantics></math>. More generally, for any finite set <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, we can form the collar <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,\epsilon)^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,\epsilon)^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> stratified by the set <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(S)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(S)}</annotation></semantics></math> (Notation <a href="#S2.Thmthm2" title="Notation 2.2. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>). These standard collars are objects of all the relevant regular stratification categories <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> listed above.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be either <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Man}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Man}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, an <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-collaring</span> of an <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a collection of open embeddings</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\to\partial^{\gamma}M,\ \alpha\leq\gamma" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\to\partial^{\gamma}M,\ \alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(called a collar embedding from <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>)
such that 1) its restriction to <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}M</annotation></semantics></math> is the inclusion of <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}M</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and 2) whenever <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.Ex2.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="70.93" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-58.05896396407353px" version="1.1" viewBox="91.40 58.06 326.82 70.93" width="326.82"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 91.39613490291399 70.92668156711593) translate(0,3.46) translate(91.4,0)"><g transform="translate(-56.3,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.54em;--ltx-fo-height:0.88em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.64" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.18)" width="104.29"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 56.2954938673983 -0.27673578005007266 L 56.2954938673983 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(161.48,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 56.2954938673983 -0.27673578005007266 L 161.47398694646594 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 161.47398694646594 -0.27673578005007266 L 161.47398694646594 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -11.069600110696001 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.069600110696001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-32.3)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -32.295933300254255 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.069600110696001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -32.295933300254255 L 0.27673578005007266 -32.295933300254255" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(161.48,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.08em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="28.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}M}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(-91.4,0) translate(0,-46.99) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.61em;--ltx-fo-height:1.01em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="17.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 14)" width="174.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\beta}}\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 91.39613490291399 -47.2660996334276 L 91.39613490291399 -46.71262807332745" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(124.61,0) translate(0,-46.99)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 91.39613490291399 -47.2660996334276 L 124.60493523500199 -46.71262807332745" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 124.60493523500199 -47.2660996334276 L 124.60493523500199 -46.71262807332745" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(124.61,0) translate(0,-46.99) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.88em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.64" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.18)" width="102.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\beta}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\beta}M\times[0,\epsilon)^{\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 179.7396674498625 -34.12164625033512 L 180.29313900996263 -34.12164625033512" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(180.02,0) translate(0,-7.61)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 2.77 -6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 179.7396674498625 -34.12164625033512 L 180.29313900996263 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 179.7396674498625 -7.610350076103501 L 180.29313900996263 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">An <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-collaring and an <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-collaring are <span id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">germ-equivalent</span> if for a certain <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime\prime}\leq\epsilon,\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime\prime}\leq\epsilon,\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the restrictions of the collar embeddings to <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon^{\prime\prime})^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}M\times[0,\epsilon^{\prime\prime})^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math> are identical. A <span id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared object</span> in <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an object together with a germ-equivalence class of <math id="S5.Thmthm1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-collarings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A morphism between two collared objects <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with underlying poset map <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:A\to A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:A\to A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared</span> if there exists a sufficiently small <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for each <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, the morphism over the strata <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\mapsto i(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\mapsto i(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> in the collared neighborhoods of the strata <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\mapsto i(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\mapsto i(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.Ex3.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="70.00" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-54.87199474275071px" version="1.1" viewBox="58.18 54.87 331.98 70.00" width="331.98"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 58.17652441446788 70.0000907039682) translate(0,3.46) translate(58.18,0)"><g transform="translate(-58.18,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.88em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.25" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.18)" width="108.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}K\times{\rm Collar}_{\epsilon}^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Collar</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\alpha}K\times{\rm Collar}_{\epsilon}^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.17654552805452 -0.27673578005007266 L 58.17654552805452 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(132.9,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.17654552805452 -0.27673578005007266 L 132.89632516166589 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 132.89632516166589 -0.27673578005007266 L 132.89632516166589 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-36.96)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -36.96076913181472 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -36.96076913181472 L 0.27673578005007266 -36.96076913181472" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(132.9,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.58em;--ltx-fo-height:1.04em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="16.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 14.44)" width="132.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{i(\alpha)}K^{\prime}\times{\rm Collar}_{\epsilon}^{\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Collar</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{i(\alpha)}K^{\prime}\times{\rm Collar}_{\epsilon}^{\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 203.0745723096764 -9.685900096859001 L 203.62804386977652 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(203.35,0) translate(0,-34.28)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 203.0745723096764 -34.28403084515964 L 203.62804386977652 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 203.0745723096764 -34.28403084515964 L 203.62804386977652 -34.28403084515964" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-17.45,0) translate(0,-47.26) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="26.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}K\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{\gamma}K\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 17.44700118155009 -47.53838044669728 L 17.44700118155009 -46.98490888659713" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(177.68,0) translate(0,-47.26)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 17.44700118155009 -47.53838044669728 L 177.68176838753547 -46.98490888659713" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 177.68176838753547 -47.53838044669728 L 177.68176838753547 -46.98490888659713" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(177.68,0) translate(0,-47.26) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.11em;--ltx-fo-height:0.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.29)" width="43.04"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\partial^{i(\gamma)}K^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\partial^{i(\gamma)}K^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the map along the collar direction is the identity map after identifying <math id="S5.Thmthm2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\cong\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}\cong\mathbb{Face}_{i(\alpha)}^{i(\gamma)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this way we obtain a subcategory</p>
<table id="S5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">of collared objects, whose morphisms are collared morphisms. Notice that the empty set and singletons are always collared. Moreover, the collar structures respect products and disjoint unions. Therefore, the category <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a regular stratification category (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Definition 2.10. ‣ 2.2. Regular stratification categories and presentations ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span>Outercollaring construction</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For manifolds with boundary, it is well-known that one can construct collars. However, it is not easy to find collars for more complicated objects, for example, smooth manifolds with corners. Here we would like to adopt the outercollaring construction from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Section 17]</cite> to avoid such discussions. Instead of finding collars in the given geometric object, we add collars outside. In general, for each category <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> listed at the beginning of this section, we would like to construct monoidal functors called the <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-outercollaring</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\cdot\}:\underline{\smash{\bf C}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mmultiscripts><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\cdot\}:\underline{\smash{\bf C}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Some care must be taken when we are in the smooth category.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.1. </span>Outercollaring of stratified spaces</h5>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first discuss the outercollaring of objects in <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a regular poset and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-space. Upon choosing a nonnegative number <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we would like to define a new <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-space denoted by <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}X</annotation></semantics></math> called <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">the outer collaring of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> of width <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span> such that the association <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\mapsto{}_{\lfloor}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\mapsto{}_{\lfloor}X</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies certain functorial properties (see Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5.2.1. Outercollaring of stratified spaces ‣ 5.2. Outercollaring construction ‣ 5. Collars ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first assume that <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique maximal element <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> has a single top stratum. Abbreviate <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}=\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}=\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}X=\left(\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in A}\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}\right)/\sim," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∼</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}X=\left(\bigsqcup_{\alpha\in A}\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}\right)/\sim,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the equivalence relation <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the following relation: if <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (which implies <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}\subseteq\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}\subseteq\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>), we identify</p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(x,(t_{i})_{i\in\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}}\big)\in\partial^{\beta}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>β</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(x,(t_{i})_{i\in\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}}\big)\in\partial^{\beta}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="S5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(y,(s_{j})_{j\in\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}\big)\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(y,(s_{j})_{j\in\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}\big)\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">if <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y\in\partial^{\alpha}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y\in\partial^{\alpha}X</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\notin\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\notin\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}=s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}=s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathbb{Face}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. We call <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}X</annotation></semantics></math> the <span id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">outer collaring</span> of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> of width <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#S5.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 5.2.1. Outercollaring of stratified spaces ‣ 5.2. Outercollaring construction ‣ 5. Collars ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="175.24" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 448.62 175.24" width="448.62"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,175.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(337.83,0) translate(0,79.57)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#BFBFBF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path d="M -314.96 78.74 L -314.96 0 L -236.22 0 L -236.22 78.74"></path></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -314.96 78.74 L -314.96 0 L -236.22 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -280.5 36.06)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.87em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="6.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="9.83"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -326.65 82.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{2}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{2}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -232.16 -4.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{1}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{1}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -333.22 -11.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="7.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.1)" width="20.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -196.85 11.81 L -100.09 11.81"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -99.26 11.81)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -4.21 5.32 C -3.44 2.13 -1.73 0.62 0 0 C -1.73 -0.62 -3.44 -2.13 -4.21 -5.32"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -11.69 82.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{2}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{2}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 82.8 -6.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{1}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{1}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#BFBFBF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path d="M 0 78.74 L 0 0 L 78.74 0 L 78.74 78.74"></path></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 78.74 L 0 0 L 78.74 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 34.46 36.06)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.87em;--ltx-fo-height:0.58em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="6.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.62)" width="9.83"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -78.74 78.74 L -78.74 -78.74 L 78.74 -78.74"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -78.74 0 L 0 0 L 0 -78.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -72.47 -42.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="10.97" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.55)" width="66.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.01 -42.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="11.31" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="64.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{1}}X\times[-\epsilon,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{1}}X\times[-\epsilon,0]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -71.73 36.14)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.71em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="11.31" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="64.73"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{2}}X\times[-\epsilon,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{2}}X\times[-\epsilon,0]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1. </span>The local picture of an outer collaring of a manifold with corners with strata <math id="S5.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\beta_{1},\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\beta_{1},\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The gray area is in the top stratum.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider the general situation when the regular poset has arbitrarily many maximal elements. For each maximal <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A^{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A^{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has the outer collaring</p>
<table id="S5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma}X)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma}X).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that if <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq\gamma_{1},\alpha\leq\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq\gamma_{1},\alpha\leq\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then there is a natural isomorphism</p>
<table id="S5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\big(\partial^{\alpha}(\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X)\big)\cong{}_{\lfloor}\big(\partial^{\alpha}(\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>≅</mo><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\big(\partial^{\alpha}(\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X)\big)\cong{}_{\lfloor}\big(\partial^{\alpha}(\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Then define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}X:=\left(\bigsqcup_{\gamma\in A^{\max}}{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma}X)\right)/\sim" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨆</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}X:=\left(\bigsqcup_{\gamma\in A^{\max}}{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma}X)\right)/\sim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> means we identify points in <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X)</annotation></semantics></math> and points in <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}(\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the above natural isomorphisms. Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5.2.1. Outercollaring of stratified spaces ‣ 5.2. Outercollaring construction ‣ 5. Collars ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> describes an example of the outer collaring of a space <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with two top strata.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.F2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="198.51" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 425.27 198.51" width="425.27"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,198.51) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(424.45,0) translate(0,99.26)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#BFBFBF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path d="M -393.7 78.74 L -393.7 -78.74 L -314.96 -78.74 L -314.96 78.74"></path></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -393.7 78.74 L -393.7 -78.74"></path></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -393.7 0 L -314.96 0"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -365.86 35.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="7.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.1)" width="23.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">γ</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -365.86 -42.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="7.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.1)" width="23.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">γ</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -405.39 82.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{1}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{1}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -310.9 -4.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{2}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{2}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -405.39 -91.06)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.78em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="8.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="23.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\beta_{3}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">β</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">3</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\beta_{3}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -419.83 -3.55)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="7.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.1)" width="20.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\alpha}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\alpha}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -255.91 0 L -139.46 0"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -138.63 0)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -4.21 5.32 C -3.44 2.13 -1.73 0.62 0 0 C -1.73 -0.62 -3.44 -2.13 -4.21 -5.32"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#BFBFBF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path d="M -78.74 98.43 L -78.74 19.69 L 0 19.69 L 0 98.43"></path></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -78.74 98.43 L -78.74 19.69 L 0 19.69"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -50.9 55.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="7.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.1)" width="23.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">γ</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\gamma_{1}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" color="#FFFFFF" fill="#BFBFBF" stroke="#FFFFFF"><path d="M -78.74 -98.43 L -78.74 -19.69 L 0 -19.69 L 0 -98.43"></path></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -78.74 -98.43 L -78.74 -19.69 L 0 -19.69"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -50.9 -62.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.03em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.19pt;" height="7.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.1)" width="23.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S5.F2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∂</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">γ</mi><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></msub></msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\gamma_{2}}X</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="1.2pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -98.43 98.43 L -98.43 -98.43"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -98.43 0 L 0 0"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="0.4pt,2.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -98.43 19.69 L -78.74 19.69 L -78.74 -19.69 L -98.43 -19.69"></path></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2. </span>The local picture of an outer collaring of a composed manifold with corners with two top strata <math id="S5.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of dimension 2, three 1-dimensional strata <math id="S5.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1},\beta_{2},\beta_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1},\beta_{2},\beta_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, and one zero-dimensional stratum <math id="S5.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following statement is straightforward from the definition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="S5.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-outer collaring is a regular stratification functor</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\{\cdot\}:\underline{\smash{\bf RegTop}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf RegTop}}.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mmultiscripts><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="bold" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\{\cdot\}:\underline{\smash{\bf RegTop}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf RegTop}}.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The outer collar construction is compatible with group actions. If <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> acts on <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, then for each <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,(t_{i})_{i\in\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}})\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,(t_{i})_{i\in\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}})\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g\cdot(x,(t_{i})_{i\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}})=(gx,(t_{i})_{i\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}})\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}\subseteq{}_{\lfloor}X." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>α</mi></msup><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕖</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\cdot(x,(t_{i})_{i\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}})=(gx,(t_{i})_{i\in{\mathbb{F}}_{\alpha}})\in\partial^{\alpha}X\times[-\epsilon,0]^{\mathbb{Face}_{\alpha}}\subseteq{}_{\lfloor}X.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">It is easy to check that this gives a <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3. </span>Category of admissible smooth manifolds and orbifolds</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The outercollaring of stratified topological manifolds is completely identical to the case of stratified spaces. However, the case with smooth manifolds is tricky.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We recall the notion of <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">admissible manifolds with corners</span> introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Chapter 25]</cite>. Let <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth manifold without boundary. For <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t=(t_{1},\ldots,t_{k})\in[0,+\infty)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=(t_{1},\ldots,t_{k})\in[0,+\infty)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote</p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}:=e^{1/t_{i}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}:=e^{1/t_{i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Consider smooth functions</p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f:V\times[0,\epsilon)^{k}\to{\mathbb{R}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:V\times[0,\epsilon)^{k}\to{\mathbb{R}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We consider the <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm stratumwise using the above coordinates <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="S5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f|_{C^{m}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f|_{C^{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">be the pointwise <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm in the above sense.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5.4</span></span><span id="S5.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Definition 25.3]</cite>) We say <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f:V\times[0,\epsilon)^{k}\to{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:V\times[0,\epsilon)^{k}\to{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">admissible</span> if for each compact <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K\subseteq V\times[0,\epsilon)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq V\times[0,\epsilon)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(m,K)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(m,K)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(m,K)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(m,K)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left|\frac{\partial f}{\partial T_{i}}\right|_{C^{m}}\leq C(m,K)e^{-\sigma(m,K)T_{i}},\ i=1,\ldots,k." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{\partial f}{\partial T_{i}}\right|_{C^{m}}\leq C(m,K)e^{-\sigma(m,K)T_{i}},\ i=1,\ldots,k.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Admissible functions are smooth (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Remark 25.5]</cite>). Using the ring of admissible functions (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Lemma 25.13]</cite>), we can consider corner charts on a smooth manifold with corners with admissible coordinate changes. In this way, one obtains a subcategory</p>
<table id="S5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}_{\rm adm}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>adm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}_{\rm adm}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that the category <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}</annotation></semantics></math> of collared smooth manifolds is automatically a subcategory of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}_{\rm adm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>adm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}_{\rm adm}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, one can consider the admissible versions of the categories <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The key feature of the admissibility is that the outercollaring is well-defined (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Section 17.3]</cite>). Indeed, for any <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist functors</p>
<table id="S5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\epsilon:\underline{\smash{\bf C}}_{\rm adm}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>adm</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\epsilon:\underline{\smash{\bf C}}_{\rm adm}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is either <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SMan}}</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each admissible object <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, let the result be called the <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-outercollaring</span> of <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, also notice that the standard collars are normally complex derived orbifolds. In fact manifolds are automatically normally complex orbifolds. Hence one has the collared versions</p>
<table id="S5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{{\rm NC}}_{\rm rig}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies</h3>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1. </span>Flow categories</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The concept of flow categories was introduced by Cohen–Jones–Segal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>. We need a variant of the original construction similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, Section 7]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, Section 7,8]</cite>. See also the formulations in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Flow categories)<span id="S6.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a regular stratification category (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Definition 2.10. ‣ 2.2. Regular stratification categories and presentations ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>). A <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>-enriched <span id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">flow category</span> <math id="S6.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the following elements.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The set of objects <math id="S6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a countable poset (not assumed to be regular).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any pair <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq q</annotation></semantics></math> of objects, a morphism space <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is an object of <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> stratified by a normal poset <math id="S6.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm5" title="Definition 2.5. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any triple <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq r\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq r\leq q</annotation></semantics></math> of objects, the composition map is defined as follows. It consists of an injective poset map homogeneous of degree <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times A_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times A_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with image</p>
<table id="S6.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}\subseteq A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}\subseteq A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">together with a morphism in <math id="S6.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}:M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}|_{A_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}:M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}|_{A_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.Thmthm1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, the following conditions must be satisfied.<span id="footnote10" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">10</span>
                  
                  
                  
                The first four conditions are usually required for flow categories. The remaining conditions are imposed in order to obtain the correct chain level information.</span></span></span></p>
<ol id="S6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq q</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a monoidal unit of <math id="S6.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S6.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=r</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=q</annotation></semantics></math>, the composition <math id="S6.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{qq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{qq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the natural isomorphism from the monoidal structure.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Associativity)</span> For any quadruple <math id="S6.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq r\leq s\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq r\leq s\leq q</annotation></semantics></math> of objects, the following diagram commutes, where the arrows are defined using composition maps:</p>
<table id="S6.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex4.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="114.98" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-102.65064780537611px" version="1.1" viewBox="37.48 102.65 332.04 114.98" width="332.04"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 37.477925322899374 114.98254480674683) translate(0,3.46) translate(37.48,0)"><g transform="translate(70.69,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.73em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="106.99"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rs}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{sq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rs}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{sq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 95.7244835042419 -11.569253138458645 L 95.7244835042419 -11.607130912885275" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(34.76,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.45 -0.3" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 5.6 4.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 95.7244835042419 -11.569253138458645 L 34.755708370628376 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 34.755708370628376 -33.17161930602039 L 34.755708370628376 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 160.97097685842803 -11.569253138458645 L 161.03131948903635 -11.637281114602791" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(222.09,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -5.6 4.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -7.45 -0.3" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 160.97097685842803 -11.569253138458645 L 222.08273320074676 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 222.0224116837251 -33.142757033087726 L 222.08273320074676 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-37.48,0) translate(0,-45.54) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.82em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="66.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{M_{ps}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{sq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{M_{ps}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{sq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 32.595007254966184 -57.10995047191738 L 32.6202379909973 -57.23730762651126" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(110.81,0) translate(0,-84.89)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -5.6 4.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -7.45 -0.3" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 32.595007254966184 -57.10995047191738 L 110.80600289333834 -84.88611939439342" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 110.80600289333834 -84.71233346278495 L 110.80600289333834 -84.88611939439342" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(219.19,0) translate(0,-45.54) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="67.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 224.22308081889096 -57.10995047191738 L 224.20722451532663 -57.10995047191738" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(145.86,0) translate(0,-84.87)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.45 -0.3" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 5.6 4.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 224.22308081889096 -57.10995047191738 L 145.85559127636597 -84.86899627563088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 145.87966076513206 -84.86899627563088 L 145.85559127636597 -84.86899627563088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(110.81,0) translate(0,-91.08) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.93em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="26.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r_{1},r_{2}&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r_{1},r_{2}&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{pr_{1}q}^{\mathbb{F}}\cap A_{pr_{2}q}^{\mathbb{F}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{pr_{1}q}^{\mathbb{F}}\cap A_{pr_{2}q}^{\mathbb{F}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, then either <math id="S6.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}\leq r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}\leq r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}\leq r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}\leq r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Maximal elements of each <math id="S6.I2.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> are true boundary strata of <math id="S6.I2.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm5" title="Definition 2.5. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Example 6.2</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">trivial flow category</span> enriched in <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{O}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is the flow category whose object set has a single element <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> with self-morphism space <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{ee}^{{\mathbb{O}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>𝕆</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{ee}^{{\mathbb{O}}}</annotation></semantics></math> being a monoidal unit of <math id="S6.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2. </span>Flow multimodules and homotopies</h4>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Flow bimodules are abstract packages of moduli spaces considered in situations such as continuation maps, PSS and SSP maps, etc. There is a more general notion of flow multimodules allowing multiple flow categories as inputs, which model situations such as the pair-of-pants product.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a regular stratification category. Let <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be flow categories <span id="footnote11" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">11</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">11</span>
                  
                  
                  
                One could consider more than one output; however, that will not be used in this paper.</span></span></span> enriched in <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">multimodule</span> over <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of the following objects.</p>
<ol id="S6.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each tuple of objects <math id="S6.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,p_{m}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,p_{m}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, an object <math id="S6.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> with underlying normal poset <math id="S6.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and a pair of objects <math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\leq q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\leq q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, an injective poset map homogeneous of degree <math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}_{p_{i}q_{i}}\times A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}_{p_{i}q_{i}}\times A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with image</p>
<table id="S6.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\subseteq A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\subseteq A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I3.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">together with a morphism in <math id="S6.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to above, for a pair of objects <math id="S6.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, an injective poset map homogeneous of degree <math id="S6.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times A_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times A_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I3.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with image</p>
<table id="S6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\subseteq A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\subseteq A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I3.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">together with a morphism in <math id="S6.I3.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.Thmthm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These objects need to satisfy the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S6.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S6.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (recall <math id="S6.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pp}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pp}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a monoidal unit), the morphism (<a href="#S6.E1" title="In item 2 ‣ Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>) is the natural isomorphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{i}p_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{i}p_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Similarly, when <math id="S6.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}=p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}=p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the morphism (<a href="#S6.E2" title="In item 3 ‣ Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>) is the natural isomorphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{p^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{p^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following associativity properties hold.</p>
<ol id="S6.I4.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I4.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S6.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}&lt;r_{i}&lt;q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}&lt;r_{i}&lt;q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.I4.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S6.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
