</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, then either <math id="S6.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\leq q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\leq q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\leq r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\leq r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the former case, one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I4.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the latter case,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i}r_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, then either <math id="S6.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.I4.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the former case, one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I4.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the latter case,</p>
<table id="S6.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cap A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}r^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S6.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}&lt;q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}&lt;q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the morphism (<a href="#S6.E1" title="In item 2 ‣ Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>) has codimension 1 and maximal elements of <math id="S6.I4.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> are true boundary strata. Similarly, when <math id="S6.I4.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the morphism (<a href="#S6.E2" title="In item 3 ‣ Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.2</span></a>) has codimension 1 and maximal elements of <math id="S6.I4.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> are true boundary strata.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A multimodule over <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is called a <span id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bimodule</span>, usually denoted by <math id="S6.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.2.1. </span>Products of multimodules</h5>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the above we only defined the situation with one output—this is the main scenario that will appear in this paper. On the other hand, there is no difficulty in extending the definition to multimodules with multiple output flow categories.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In general, let <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{n}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{n}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be flow categories enriched over <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A multimodule over <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{n}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{\prime},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{n}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of objects</p>
<table id="S6.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>Ob</mi><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">together with structural maps</p>
<table id="S6.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{i-1}^{\prime}q_{i}^{\prime}p_{i+1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{q_{i}^{\prime}p_{i}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{i-1}^{\prime}q_{i}^{\prime}p_{i+1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{q_{i}^{\prime}p_{i}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{n}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">which satisfy conditions similar to those in Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm3" title="Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>. We omit the details.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to define products of multimodules. Suppose <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a multimodule over <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a multimodule over <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for objects <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{G}}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{G}}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the collection of objects</p>
<table id="S6.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m}q_{1}\cdots q_{n};p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\times{\mathbb{Y}}}:=M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{q_{1}\cdots q_{n};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{Y}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕐</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m}q_{1}\cdots q_{n};p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\times{\mathbb{Y}}}:=M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{q_{1}\cdots q_{n};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">define a multimodule <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\times{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\times{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.2.2. </span>Homotopies of multimodules</h5>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the following definition, denote by <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> the homogeneous poset with one unique maximal element, thought as the total space of the unit interval, and two codimension <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> element, which are the boundary points <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.5</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two multimodules <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, a <span id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">homotopy</span> of multimodules from <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of the following objects.</p>
<ol id="S6.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each tuple <math id="S6.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> of objects of involved flow categories, an object <math id="S6.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{H}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> stratified by a regular poset <math id="S6.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a tuple <math id="S6.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, a morphism in <math id="S6.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\to{\mathbb{H}}}\sqcup\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}\to{\mathbb{H}}}:M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}\sqcup M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times\{0\}}\sqcup M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times\{1\}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>⊔</mo><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo>⊔</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊔</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\to{\mathbb{H}}}\sqcup\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}\to{\mathbb{H}}}:M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}\sqcup M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times\{0\}}\sqcup M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}|_{A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times\{1\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a tuple <math id="S6.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\leq q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\leq q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I5.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, injective poset maps homogeneous of degree <math id="S6.I5.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S6.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{H}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I5.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times A_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times A_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I5.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">together with morphisms in <math id="S6.I5.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> after pulling back the target to using the above poset maps (which we omit from the notations)</p>
<table id="S6.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}:M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{H}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}:M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I5.i3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}:M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times M_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}:M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times M_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These objects need to satisfy the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S6.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S6.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}=p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}=p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the morphism (<a href="#S6.E7" title="In item 3 ‣ Definition 6.5. ‣ 6.2.2. Homotopies of multimodules ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.7</span></a>) resp. (<a href="#S6.E8" title="In item 3 ‣ Definition 6.5. ‣ 6.2.2. Homotopies of multimodules ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.8</span></a>) is the natural isomorphism from the monoidal structure of <math id="S6.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Associativity H1)</span> The following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S6.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
