<p id="S6.I6.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence we have a well-defined morphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times M_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\times M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times M_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\to M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Associativity H2)</span> For <math id="S6.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0,1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math>, the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S6.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.EGx8.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
