<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3. </span>Lifts of flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The key issue of constructing Floer chain complex (and various chain maps, homotopies) is to regularize certain moduli spaces. Using the terminologies we just introduced, the associated flow categories (and multimodules, homotopies), whose morphism spaces are certain moduli spaces, are enriched in <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The regularization requires a lift to a better category which allows manipulations in differential topological or algebraic topological sense.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be two regular stratification categories (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Definition 2.10. ‣ 2.2. Regular stratification categories and presentations ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>). Let <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}:\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}:\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a covariant functor satisfying the natural compatibility conditions.</p>
<ol id="S6.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> respects the distributive monoidal structure.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The diagram <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.I7.i2.p1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="23.50" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-14.947807044924847px" version="1.1" viewBox="7.61 14.95 112.08 23.50" width="112.08"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 7.610350076103501 23.496085980200117) translate(0,3.46) translate(7.61,0)"><g transform="translate(-7.61,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.57em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.86)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.I7.i2.p1.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\underline{\hat{\bf C}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\underline{\hat{\bf C}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 7.610371189690138 -0.27673578005007266 L 7.610371189690138 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(16.15,0) translate(0,-7.47) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.32)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.48em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.65)" width="7.84"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.I7.i2.p1.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(40.82,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 7.610371189690138 -0.27673578005007266 L 40.819150408191504 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 40.819150408191504 -0.27673578005007266 L 40.819150408191504 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(13.84,0) translate(0,8.55)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 90 0 0 13.84 13.84" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 7.610371189690138 4.7044449200913245 L 7.6133059782326695 4.7044449200913245" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 7.610371189690138 4.7044449200913245 L 13.837000138370001 8.54827893527527" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(83.02,0) translate(0,-5.28)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.84 13.84 A 13.84 13.84 90 0 0 27.67 0" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 13.837000138370001 8.54827893527527 L 83.02200083022001 -5.28346392002214" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(89.25,0) translate(0,-2.91)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -7.45 0.12" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -5.48 -5.05" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 83.02200083022001 -5.28346392002214 L 89.24865089248651 -2.9059051560121767" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 89.24865089248651 -2.9059051560121767 L 89.24865089248651 -2.9059051560121767" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(40.82,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.57em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.86)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.I7.i2.p1.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\underline{\bf C}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\underline{\bf C}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 56.03987167398514 -0.27673578005007266 L 56.03987167398514 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(89.25,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 56.03987167398514 -0.27673578005007266 L 89.24865089248651 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 89.24865089248651 -0.27673578005007266 L 89.24865089248651 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(89.25,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.57em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.86)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.I7.i2.p1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\underline{\bf RegPos}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐑𝐞𝐠𝐏𝐨𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\underline{\bf RegPos}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span> commutes.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}</annotation></semantics></math> respects the pullback. Namely, if <math id="S6.I7.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="S6.I7.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object of <math id="S6.I7.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I7.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math>, then one has the natural isomorphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}(\hat{M})|_{B}\cong{\bf F}(\hat{M}|_{B})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}(\hat{M})|_{B}\cong{\bf F}(\hat{M}|_{B}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.6</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>-enriched flow category. A <span id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lift</span> of <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}:\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}:\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}</annotation></semantics></math>-enriched flow category <math id="S6.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S6.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The set of objects are identical <math id="S6.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Ob}\hat{\mathbb{F}}={\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Ob}\hat{\mathbb{F}}={\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}(M_{pq}^{\hat{\mathbb{F}}})=M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}(M_{pq}^{\hat{\mathbb{F}}})=M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}_{*}\iota_{prq}^{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}=\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}_{*}\iota_{prq}^{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}=\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.7</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>-enriched flow categories and <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a multimodule over <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are lifts of <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.</p>
<ol id="S6.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S6.I9.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lift</span> of <math id="S6.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> which <span id="S6.I9.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">extends</span> <math id="S6.I9.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a multimodule <math id="S6.I9.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.I9.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any tuple of objects <math id="S6.I9.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of the involved flow categories and <math id="S6.I9.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\leq q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\leq q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I9.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bf F}(M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}})=M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}(M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}})=M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I9.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are two such lifts of multimodules <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Let <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a homotopy from <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. A lift of <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\hat{\bf C}}}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a homotopy <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any tuple of objects <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\cdots,p_{m};p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\cdots,p_{m};p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.I9.i2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime},p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime},p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bf F}(M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{H}}})=M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}(M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{H}}})=M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S6.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}(p_{i}q_{i})p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I9.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\to\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\to{\mathbb{H}}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\to\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\to{\mathbb{H}}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}\to\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}\to{\mathbb{H}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>ι</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\bf F}_{*}\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}\to\hat{\mathbb{H}}}=\iota_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}\to{\mathbb{H}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4. </span>Outercollaring of flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies</h4>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a regular stratification category which admits the outercollaring construction. Let <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a flow category enriched in <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix an <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (the <span id="S6.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">outercollaring width</span>). Define the <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-outercollaring of <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a flow category <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as follows. The set of objects is the same as <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each pair <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the morphism space is</p>
<table id="S6.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{pq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{}_{\epsilon}{\mathbb{F}}}:={}_{\lfloor}M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{}_{\epsilon}{\mathbb{F}}}:={}_{\lfloor}M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S6.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq r\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq r\leq q</annotation></semantics></math>, the composition is the outercollaring</p>
<table id="S6.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\iota_{prq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}:={}_{\lfloor}{}_{\epsilon}\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}:{}_{\lfloor}(M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}})\cong{}_{\lfloor}M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times{}_{\lfloor}M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\cong M_{pr}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}\times M_{rq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}\to{}_{\lfloor}M_{pq}^{{\mathbb{F}}}\cong M_{pq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>≅</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>≅</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>≅</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{prq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}:={}_{\lfloor}{}_{\epsilon}\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}:{}_{\lfloor}(M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}})\cong{}_{\lfloor}M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times{}_{\lfloor}M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\cong M_{pr}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}\times M_{rq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}\to{}_{\lfloor}M_{pq}^{{\mathbb{F}}}\cong M_{pq}^{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to check that this set of data satisfies the definition of flow categories.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The case of outercollaring of multimodules and homotopies are similar. We omit the details. We remark that one must choose the same outercollaring width of involved flow categories to obtain a corresponding outercollaring of multimodules and homotopies.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.5. </span>Multimodule concatenations</h4>

<section id="S6.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.5.1. </span>Bimodule concatenations</h5>

<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before we discuss the more general multimodule concatenation, we first consider the bimodule case, which was discussed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Section 5]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first describe the intuitive picture. Suppose <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are flow categories enriched in <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a bimodule over <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a bimodule over <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are bimodules corresponding to continuation maps. We would like to define a bimodule <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> which characterizes the features of compositions of continuation maps. Then given a pair of objects <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the space <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> should be the quotient</p>
<table id="S6.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the equivalence relation is generated by viewing the images of points of</p>
<table id="S6.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\times M_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\times M_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">in either <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> the same point.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, this construction does not work for any category <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For example, when <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}=\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}=\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, because of the symmetry groups, there is no obvious way to construct the above quotient in <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To rigorously define the notion of concatenations, one needs some preparations. Let <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{F},\mathbb{F}^{\prime},\mathbb{F}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F},\mathbb{F}^{\prime},\mathbb{F}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be flow categories. Let <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be a bimodule over <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be a bimodule over <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. For each pair of objects <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the set</p>
<table id="S6.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}\circ{\mathbb{B}}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝔹</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}\circ{\mathbb{B}}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the equivalence relation <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as follows. For any <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime},q^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime},q^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> images of the two maps</p>
<table id="S6.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
