<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">are identified. The equivalence relation <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by this identification.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.8</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Two pairs <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are equivalent if and only if one of the following conditions holds: 1) <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and there exists <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in A_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in A_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ b^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(a^{\prime},v),\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ b^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(a^{\prime},v),\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ a^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime\prime});" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ a^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime\prime});</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">2) <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and there exists <math id="S6.Thmthm8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in A_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in A_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S6.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ a^{\prime}=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(b^{\prime},w),\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ a^{\prime}=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(b^{\prime},w),\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ b^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,a^{\prime\prime})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ b^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,a^{\prime\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first check that the relation defined in the statement of this lemma, denoted by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math>, is an equivalence relation. The only non-obvious condition is the transitivity. Suppose we have three elements <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c^{\prime},c^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;r^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c^{\prime},c^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;r^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\approx(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\approx(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})\approx(c^{\prime},c^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b^{\prime},b^{\prime\prime})\approx(c^{\prime},c^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, we may assume one of the following holds.</span></p>
<ol id="S6.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, there exists <math id="S6.I10.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in A_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in A_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I10.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in A_{q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in A_{q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ b^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a^{\prime},v),\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ b^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a^{\prime},v),\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ a^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ a^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ c^{\prime}=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(b^{\prime},w),\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ c^{\prime}=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(b^{\prime},w),\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ b^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{q^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,c^{\prime\prime})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ b^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{q^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,c^{\prime\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then by the associativity conditions for the bimodules, one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(b^{\prime},w)=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a^{\prime},v),w)=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a^{\prime},\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(v,w))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(b^{\prime},w)=\iota_{p;q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a^{\prime},v),w)=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a^{\prime},\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(v,w))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime\prime})=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,\iota_{q^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,c^{\prime\prime}))=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(v,w),c^{\prime\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime\prime})=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,\iota_{q^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,c^{\prime\prime}))=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(v,w),c^{\prime\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="S6.I10.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\approx(c^{\prime},c^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a^{\prime},a^{\prime\prime})\approx(c^{\prime},c^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, there exists <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in A_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in A_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in A_{r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in A_{r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a,v),\ a^{\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a,v),\ a^{\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S6.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\iota_{p;r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(c,w),\ c^{\prime}=\iota_{r^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,b^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\iota_{p;r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(c,w),\ c^{\prime}=\iota_{r^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,b^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then we see</p>
<table id="S6.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\partial^{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\cap\partial^{p;r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\neq\emptyset." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">∩</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\partial^{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\cap\partial^{p;r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}A_{p;q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\neq\emptyset.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Then by the condition for bimodule/multimodules (see (3) and (4) of Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm3" title="Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>), either <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, assume that <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in A_{p;p^{\prime}r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in A_{p;p^{\prime}r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">As the poset maps underlying the structural maps are all injective (see Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm1" title="Definition 6.1 (Flow categories). ‣ 6.1. Flow categories ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> and Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm3" title="Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>), it follows that there exists <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in A_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in A_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a,u),\ v=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(u,w)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(a,u),\ v=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(u,w).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Then by using the associativity of the bimodules, one can conclude that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime})=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(u,w),b^{\prime})=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(u,\iota_{r^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,b^{\prime}))=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(u,c^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,b^{\prime})=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}(u,w),b^{\prime})=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(u,\iota_{r^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,b^{\prime}))=\iota_{p^{\prime}r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(u,c^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I10.i2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">which implies <math id="S6.I10.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,a^{\prime})\approx(c,c^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,a^{\prime})\approx(c,c^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math> is an equivalence relation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then one can see that the two relations <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math> contain each other. Hence the lemma is proved.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The following corollary is an obvious consequence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.9</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The natural map</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is injective.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Denote the image of the above map by</p>
<table id="S6.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">More generally, assume <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\prime}&lt;\cdots&lt;p_{l}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\prime}&lt;\cdots&lt;p_{l}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote</p>
<table id="S6.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p;(p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{l}^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}=\bigcap_{i=1}^{l}A_{p;p_{i}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;(p_{1}^{\prime}\cdots p_{l}^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}=\bigcap_{i=1}^{l}A_{p;p_{i}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The following corollary is also obvious.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6.10</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="S6.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\cap A_{p;q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\cap A_{p;q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, then either <math id="S6.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We define a partial order between two elements <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. We denote <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq y</annotation></semantics></math> if there exist <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime},y^{\prime}\in A_{p^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime},y^{\prime}\in A_{p^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime\prime},y^{\prime\prime}\in A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime\prime},y^{\prime\prime}\in A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{\prime},x^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{\prime},x^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{\prime},y^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{\prime},y^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.11</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This is a partial order. Moreover, the map <math id="S6.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a poset map.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The only non-obvious condition is the transitivity. Suppose <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq y\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq y\leq z</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{\prime},x^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{\prime},x^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{\prime},y^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{\prime},y^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. There also exists <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{y}^{\prime},\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{y}^{\prime},\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{z}^{\prime},\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{z}^{\prime},\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime})\in A_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{\prime},y^{\prime\prime})\approx(\tilde{y}^{\prime},\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{\prime},y^{\prime\prime})\approx(\tilde{y}^{\prime},\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, by Lemma <a href="#S6.Thmthm8" title="Lemma 6.8. ‣ 6.5.1. Bimodule concatenations ‣ 6.5. Multimodule concatenations ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.8</span></a>, either <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq\tilde{p}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq\tilde{p}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p11.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq\tilde{p}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq\tilde{p}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in A_{p^{\prime}\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in A_{p^{\prime}\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \tilde{y}^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(y^{\prime},v),\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \tilde{y}^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(y^{\prime},v),\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ y^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}\tilde{p}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ y^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}\tilde{p}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I11.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(x^{\prime},v)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime}=\iota_{p;p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}(x^{\prime},v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I11.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then as <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, as <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(v,\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. It then follows that <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x^{\prime},x^{\prime\prime})\approx(\tilde{x}^{\prime},\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x^{\prime},x^{\prime\prime})\approx(\tilde{x}^{\prime},\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S6.I11.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}^{\prime}\leq p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the argument is similar. There exists <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S6.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ y^{\prime}=\iota_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(\tilde{y}^{\prime},w),\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ y^{\prime}=\iota_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(\tilde{y}^{\prime},w),\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,y^{\prime\prime})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,y^{\prime\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I11.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then define <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,x^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,x^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then since <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime\prime}\leq y^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="S6.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,x^{\prime\prime})\leq\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,y^{\prime\prime})=\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime\prime}=\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,x^{\prime\prime})\leq\iota_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}(w,y^{\prime\prime})=\tilde{y}^{\prime\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I11.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, as <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}=\iota_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(\tilde{y}^{\prime},w)\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}\leq y^{\prime}=\iota_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(\tilde{y}^{\prime},w)\in A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime}\in A_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime}\in A_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in A_{\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}=\iota_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(\tilde{x}^{\prime},u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}=\iota_{p;\tilde{p}^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}(\tilde{x}^{\prime},u)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{y}^{\prime}\leq\tilde{z}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S6.I11.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Lastly, it follows immediately from the definition of the partial order that the map <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a poset map.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6.12</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The poset <math id="S6.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a normal poset.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first verify that this poset is homogeneous (see Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm3" title="Definition 2.3. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>). Let <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary element. Notice that each <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\cong A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\cong A_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous. Hence if <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the depth of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in this subset is well-defined, denoted by <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. As maximal elements of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are exactly maximal elements of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all possible <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we only need to show that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\cap A_{p;q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\cap A_{p;q^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, we can assume <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leq q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We need to show that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p^{\prime}}(x)=d_{q^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p^{\prime}}(x)=d_{q^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Claim.</span><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p14.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Maximal elements of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> have depth <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of the claim.</span><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.1.2" class="ltx_text"> The depth is clearly at least one. If the depth is bigger than <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists a non-maximal element <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&lt;y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;y</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> different from <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime},q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime},q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in A_{p;r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in A_{p;r^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by the definition of the equivalence relation, the three elements <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime},q^{\prime},r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime},q^{\prime},r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are totally ordered. In either case, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be a maximal element of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.  </span><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">End of the proof of the claim.</span><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p15.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, both <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{q^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{q^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are 1 higher than the depth of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in the subset <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;(p^{\prime}q^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p^{\prime}}(x)=d_{q^{\prime}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p^{\prime}}(x)=d_{q^{\prime}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a homogeneous poset.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we need to show that the poset is regular (see Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm4" title="Definition 2.4. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>). Given any <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the three conditions for <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm4" title="Definition 2.4. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> are about elements below <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We may assume that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a regular poset. Hence all three conditions for <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Therefore, <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is regular.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Lastly, we verify that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is normal (Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm5" title="Definition 2.5. ‣ 2.1.1. Partially ordered sets ‣ 2.1. Regular posets ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>), i.e., there are only fake boundaries or true boundaries. Let <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> be an element of depth <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Claim. There exist at most two distinct </span><math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p19.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose it is not the case, then there exists three distinct <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\prime},p_{2}^{\prime},p_{3}^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\prime},p_{2}^{\prime},p_{3}^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is representable in <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p_{i}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p_{i}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p_{i}^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times A_{p_{i}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the three elements <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\prime},p_{2}^{\prime},p_{3}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\prime},p_{2}^{\prime},p_{3}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are totally ordered; we may assume <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\prime}&lt;p_{2}^{\prime}&lt;p_{3}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\prime}&lt;p_{2}^{\prime}&lt;p_{3}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it is easy to find an increasing path starting from <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> of length <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. This contradicts the condition that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> has depth <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we discuss in two cases. First, suppose there exists a unique <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A_{p;p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a normal poset. Hence <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to at most two maximal elements. Second, suppose <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A_{p;p_{i}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A_{p;p_{i}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\prime}\neq p_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\prime}\neq p_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we may assume <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\prime}&lt;p_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\prime}&lt;p_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in A_{p;(p_{1}^{\prime}p_{2}^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in A_{p;(p_{1}^{\prime}p_{2}^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> has depth 1, it is a maximal element of <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;(p_{1}^{\prime}p_{2}^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;(p_{1}^{\prime}p_{2}^{\prime});p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence by the properties of bimodule/multimodules (see (2) of Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm3" title="Definition 6.3. ‣ 6.2. Flow multimodules and homotopies ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a>), it is a true boundary in both <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p_{1}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p_{1}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p_{2}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p_{2}^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to exactly two maximal elements in <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This finishes the proof that <math id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p21.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is normal.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">The above technical results allow us to do the following construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.SSS1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="S6.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> be either <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐨𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Top}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If we define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I12.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">as topological spaces, then it is naturally stratified by <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}\circ{\mathbb{B}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>𝔹</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}\circ{\mathbb{B}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, if <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}=\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}=\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stratified pseudomanifold. Moreover, one obtains a bimodule over <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. If the flow categories and bimodules are enriched in the collared version of <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.I12.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is also collared.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}=\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}=\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the underlying stratified orbifolds in <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Then define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times{\mathcal{U}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{p^{\prime}\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}}\times{\mathcal{U}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\right)/\sim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I12.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">in the similar way. Then it is a stratified orbifold. Moreover, the obstruction bundles <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{p^{\prime};p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> induce orbifold vector bundles <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with induced Kuranishi sections</p>
<table id="S6.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}:{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}:{\mathcal{U}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.I12.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then one obtains objects <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p;p^{\prime\prime}}^{{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math> together with structural maps making a bimodule <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Lastly, if the flow categories and bimodules are enriched in <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so is the concatenation <math id="S6.I12.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}\circ{\mathbb{B}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">6.5.2. </span>General concatenations</h5>

<div id="S6.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we consider concatenations in a general regular stratification category <math id="S6.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. There is no canonical construction. We characterize the notion of concatenations in an axiomatic way.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6.13</span></span><span id="S6.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n},{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n},{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be flow categories enriched in <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a multimodule over <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{G}}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{G}}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> resp. over <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then a <span id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">concatenation</span> of <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{G}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{G}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of the following objects.</p>
<ol id="S6.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A multimodule over <math id="S6.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{i-1},{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{i+1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{i-1},{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{i+1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each two tuples <math id="S6.I13.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I13.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{1},\ldots,r_{n};r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{1},\ldots,r_{n};r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> of objects, a codimension zero morphism</p>
<table id="S6.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r_{i}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{Y}}\to M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}p_{1}\cdots p_{m}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕐</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r_{i}}^{\mathbb{X}}\times M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{Y}}\to M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}p_{1}\cdots p_{m}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S6.Thmthm13.p1.2" class="ltx_p">They are required to satisfy the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S6.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each tuple <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{1},\cdots,r_{i-1},p_{1},\cdots,p_{m},r_{i+1},\cdots,r_{n};r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{1},\cdots,r_{i-1},p_{1},\cdots,p_{m},r_{i+1},\cdots,r_{n};r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, the object <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}p_{1}\cdots p_{m}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}p_{1}\cdots p_{m}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is stratified by <math id="S6.I14.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}p_{1}\cdots p_{m}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}p_{1}\cdots p_{m}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The underlying poset maps of the structural maps of <math id="S6.I14.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as the previously discussed special cases.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S6.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.Ex63.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="116.81" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-104.48185028798257px" version="1.1" viewBox="99.16 104.48 654.39 116.81" width="654.39"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 99.1611420011329 116.8137472893533) translate(0,3.46) translate(99.16,0)"><g transform="translate(132.37,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:17.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.42em;font-size:10pt;" height="17.43" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="239.12"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S6.Ex63.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r_{i}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}\times M_{r_{i}s_{i}}^{{\mathbb{G}}_{i}}\times M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}s_{i}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{Y}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕐</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};r_{i}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}\times M_{r_{i}s_{i}}^{{\mathbb{G}}_{i}}\times M_{r_{1}\cdots r_{i-1}s_{i}r_{i+1}\cdots r_{n};r^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{Y}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 323.1613477994846 -13.400455621065102 L 323.2266310093659 -13.475493307972707" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(422.39,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.24 4.07" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -7.33 -1.36" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 323.1613477994846 -13.400455621065102 L 422.38441595022357 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 422.31915385392887 -33.13082785663787 L 422.38441595022357 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 180.7291979147749 -13.400455621065102 L 180.72607310395261 -13.41890889578577" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(69.34,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.3 -1.51" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 6.33 3.94" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 180.7291979147749 -13.400455621065102 L 69.34282475196096 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><pa