<li id="S7.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The category of Novikov groups admits finite products, denoted by</p>
<table id="S7.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{\Pi},\lambda,\mu)\oplus(\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime},\lambda^{\prime},\mu^{\prime})=(\mathbb{\Pi}\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime},\lambda\oplus\lambda^{\prime},\mu+\mu^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{\Pi},\lambda,\mu)\oplus(\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime},\lambda^{\prime},\mu^{\prime})=(\mathbb{\Pi}\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime},\lambda\oplus\lambda^{\prime},\mu+\mu^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S7.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S7.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">twisted Novikov group</span>, denoted by <math id="S7.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of a Novikov group <math id="S7.I7.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> together with a finite group <math id="S7.I7.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> acting on <math id="S7.I7.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> by isomorphisms of Novikov groups. Notice that the semi-direct product <math id="S7.I7.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math> is a not necessarily abelian.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Example 7.22</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S7.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> be a symplectic manifold. Then</p>
<table id="S7.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi=\frac{\pi_{2}(X)}{{\rm ker}\omega\cap{\rm ker}c_{1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi=\frac{\pi_{2}(X)}{{\rm ker}\omega\cap{\rm ker}c_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I8.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">together with the symplectic area <math id="S7.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(a)=\omega(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(a)=\omega(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and twice the Chern number <math id="S7.I8.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(a)=2c_{1}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(a)=2c_{1}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is a Novikov group.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> with the inclusion <math id="S7.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:{\mathbb{Z}}\hookrightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:{\mathbb{Z}}\hookrightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the multiplication by two <math id="S7.I8.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:{\mathbb{Z}}\to 2{\mathbb{Z}}\hookrightarrow{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↪</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:{\mathbb{Z}}\to 2{\mathbb{Z}}\hookrightarrow{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Novikov group.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S7.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Any finite group is a twisted Novikov group.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.3.2. </span>Novikov rings</h5>

<div id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be a commutative ring with unit, typically <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf F}_{\sf p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mi>𝗉</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf F}_{\sf p}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{\Pi},\lambda,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{\Pi},\lambda,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> be a Novikov group. We define the Novikov ring <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. Define</p>
<table id="S7.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}:=\left\{f:\mathbb{\Pi}\to R\ \left|\ \begin{array}[]{l}\forall\alpha=1,\ldots,k,\ \displaystyle\inf\{\lambda_{\alpha}(a)\ |\ f(a)\neq 0\}&gt;-\infty,\\
\forall c&gt;0,\ \#\big\{a\in\mathbb{\Pi}\ |\ f(a)\neq 0,\ \lambda_{\alpha}(a)&lt;c,\ \alpha=1,\ldots,k\big\}&lt;\infty\end{array}\right.\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>R</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">|</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.389em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>#</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}:=\left\{f:\mathbb{\Pi}\to R\ \left|\ \begin{array}[]{l}\forall\alpha=1,\ldots,k,\ \displaystyle\inf\{\lambda_{\alpha}(a)\ |\ f(a)\neq 0\}&gt;-\infty,\\
\forall c&gt;0,\ \#\big\{a\in\mathbb{\Pi}\ |\ f(a)\neq 0,\ \lambda_{\alpha}(a)&lt;c,\ \alpha=1,\ldots,k\big\}&lt;\infty\end{array}\right.\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7.23</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.Thmthm23.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.Thmthm23.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a graded unital commutative ring.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can grade <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> by dualizing the grading on <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by the morphism <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:{\mathbb{\Pi}}\to{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:{\mathbb{\Pi}}\to{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The product structure is defined as follows. Choose <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime},f^{\prime\prime}\in\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime},f^{\prime\prime}\in\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define formally <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}:\mathbb{\Pi}\to R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}:\mathbb{\Pi}\to R</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S7.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}(a)=\sum_{a^{\prime}+a^{\prime\prime}=a}f^{\prime}(a^{\prime})f^{\prime\prime}(a^{\prime\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}(a)=\sum_{a^{\prime}+a^{\prime\prime}=a}f^{\prime}(a^{\prime})f^{\prime\prime}(a^{\prime\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is commutative in <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that this is a finite sum. If not, then there is a sequence <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{i}^{\prime},a_{i}^{\prime\prime})\in\mathbb{\Pi}\times\mathbb{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{i}^{\prime},a_{i}^{\prime\prime})\in\mathbb{\Pi}\times\mathbb{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\prime}+a_{i}^{\prime\prime}=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\prime}+a_{i}^{\prime\prime}=a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(a_{i}^{\prime}),f^{\prime\prime}(a_{i}^{\prime\prime})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(a_{i}^{\prime}),f^{\prime\prime}(a_{i}^{\prime\prime})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime})+\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime\prime})=\lambda_{\alpha}(a)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime})+\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime\prime})=\lambda_{\alpha}(a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is independent of <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{i}\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime\prime})=\lambda_{\alpha}(a)-\inf_{i}\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime})&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{i}\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime\prime})=\lambda_{\alpha}(a)-\inf_{i}\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i}^{\prime})&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">The finiteness condition in the definition of <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> shows that there are only finitely many distinct <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in this sequence. As <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\prime}=a-a_{i}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\prime}=a-a_{i}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are also only finitely many distinct <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in this sequence. Hence the sum (<a href="#S7.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ 7.3.2. Novikov rings ‣ 7.3. Symmetries on flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>) is indeed finite. Therefore, <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined. It is also straightforward to check that <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}f^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the definition of <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this definition, one can easily see that the unit is given by the map which assigns the identity element of <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the multiplicative unit in <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We also define the subring</p>
<table id="S7.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda_{R,0}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}:=\left\{f\in\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}\ |\ f(a)\neq 0\Longrightarrow\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i})\geq 0,\ \alpha=1,\ldots,k\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R,0}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}:=\left\{f\in\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}\ |\ f(a)\neq 0\Longrightarrow\lambda_{\alpha}(a_{i})\geq 0,\ \alpha=1,\ldots,k\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we consider the tensor product of Novikov rings. If <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are two Novikov groups, then the Novikov ring</p>
<table id="S7.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">is a certain completion of the tensor product <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}}\otimes_{R}\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>R</mi></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}}\otimes_{R}\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the completed tensor product by <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\otimes}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\otimes}</annotation></semantics></math>. More generally, if <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}_{1},\ldots,\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}_{1},\ldots,\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> are Novikov groups, then there is a natural identification</p>
<table id="S7.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}}_{R}\widehat{\underset{R}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{R}{\otimes}}\Lambda^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}_{R}\cong\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑅</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑅</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}}_{R}\widehat{\underset{R}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{R}{\otimes}}\Lambda^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}_{R}\cong\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly, suppose one has a morphism of Novikov groups <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is a natural ring map</p>
<table id="S7.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}\to\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}\to\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">making the latter an algebra over <math id="S7.SS3.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{R}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.3.3. </span>Symmetries on flow categories</h5>

<div id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the concepts related to symmetries on flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies which appear everywhere in the Floer-theoretic setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7.24</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm24.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math> be a twisted Novikov group of rank <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a (weak) flow category enriched in <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with a filtration <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(free) <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{\Pi}}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{\Pi}}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>-action</span> on <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a (free) <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{\Pi}}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{\Pi}}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> together with <math id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>-isomorphisms</p>
<table id="S7.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{a}^{\mathbb{F}}:M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{ap\ aq}^{\mathbb{F}},\ \forall a\in{\mathbb{\Pi}}\rtimes G" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{a}^{\mathbb{F}}:M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to M_{ap\ aq}^{\mathbb{F}},\ \forall a\in{\mathbb{\Pi}}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm24.p1.2" class="ltx_p">such that</p>
<ol id="S7.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{0}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{0}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity morphism and for all <math id="S7.I9.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b\in\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b\in\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S7.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{a+b}^{\mathbb{F}}=T_{a}^{\mathbb{F}}\circ T_{b}^{\mathbb{F}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{a+b}^{\mathbb{F}}=T_{a}^{\mathbb{F}}\circ T_{b}^{\mathbb{F}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S7.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I9.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q,r\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q,r\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote <math id="S7.I9.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}=ap" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}=ap</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.I9.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}=ar" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}=ar</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.I9.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}=aq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}=aq</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S7.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S7.Ex86.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="77.07" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-61.86449793309811px" version="1.1" viewBox="46.36 61.86 210.53 77.07" width="210.53"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 46.35705416077513 77.06596360787887) translate(0,3.46) translate(46.36,0)"><g transform="translate(-37.69,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.6" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="67.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex86.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{M_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\times M_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 37.69094029847923 -0.27673578005007266 L 37.69094029847923 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(66.72,0) translate(0,7.6) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-0.72)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="6.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="19.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_