pan class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S7.Ex102.m1.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{M_{ap;\rho(a)q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times M_{\rho(a)q^{\prime}\ \rho(a)p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{M_{ap;\rho(a)q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\times M_{\rho(a)q^{\prime}\ \rho(a)p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 281.33051877399856 -47.218066223828615 L 281.33051877399856 -46.664594663728465" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(206.61,0) translate(0,-46.94)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 206.61071802680053 -47.218066223828615 L 281.33051877399856 -46.664594663728465" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 206.61071802680053 -47.218066223828615 L 206.61071802680053 -46.664594663728465" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I12.i1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S7.I12.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}=\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}=\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I12.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity, we simply say that <math id="S7.I12.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S7.I12.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose in addition that <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⋊</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}\rtimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">⋊</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}\rtimes</annotation></semantics></math> are twisted Novikov groups and <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is an equivariant morphism of Novikov groups. Suppose <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔹</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant Novikov bimodules. Then a <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant Novikov homotopy is a <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant homotopy <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies, in addition, that for all constants <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the set</p>
<table id="S7.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{(p,p^{\prime})\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}\times{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}\ \left|\ \begin{array}[]{c}M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\neq\emptyset,\\
{\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p)+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{k}(p)-{\mathcal{A}}_{1}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})-\cdots-{\mathcal{A}}_{k^{\prime}}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})&lt;C\end{array}\right.\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Ob</mi><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Ob</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em">|</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{(p,p^{\prime})\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}\times{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}\ \left|\ \begin{array}[]{c}M_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\neq\emptyset,\\
{\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p)+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{k}(p)-{\mathcal{A}}_{1}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})-\cdots-{\mathcal{A}}_{k^{\prime}}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})&lt;C\end{array}\right.\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.I12.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">consists of finitely many <math id="S7.I12.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>-orbits.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that incorporating <math id="S7.SS3.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-symmetry for flow multimodules and bimodule homotopies is straightforward. We do not spell out the details because they are not needed for this paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.4. </span>Algebraic structures with symmetry</h4>

<div id="S7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the previous two subsections, we provide separate treatments of convergence of structural maps of chain complexes and Novikov rings with geometric origin. As usual, in the concrete setting of Floer theory, the two structures interact with each other in the form that recapping of periodic orbits corresponds to multiplication by Novikov variables. Abstractly, equivariance under Novikov groups of flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies leads to linearity of differentials and chain maps under Novikov rings, and local finiteness of orbits under the Novikov group action is compatible with the convergence assumption. We record these classical observations here formally.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.4.1. </span>Flow categories and bimodules</h5>

<div id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded, oriented, unobstructed, Novikov flow category enriched in <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have obtained previously the complex <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> as a free abelian group.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.30</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G,\lambda,\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G,\lambda,\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> be a twisted Novikov group. If <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⋊</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant, then <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> has the structure of a <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math>-module with a <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action and the differential is <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant and <math id="S7.Thmthm30.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math>-linear.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS4.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariance condition on <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> has a natural <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math>-module structure. Moreover, the <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariance on the flow category implies that <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}}</annotation></semantics></math>-module map. In the presence of the finite group <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows from definition that the chain complex <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following proposition is straightforward.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.31</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm31.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math> be twisted Novikov groups with a <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant morphism <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant resp. <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded, oriented, unobstructed flow categories enriched in <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant graded, oriented, and unobstructed bimodule over <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the chain map</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{B}}:C({\mathbb{F}})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝔹</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{B}}:C({\mathbb{F}})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">extends to a <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{{\mathbb{\Pi}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{{\mathbb{\Pi}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>-linear chain map</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{B}}:C({\mathbb{F}})\underset{\Lambda^{\mathbb{\Pi}}}{\otimes}\Lambda^{{\mathbb{\Pi}}^{\prime}}\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝔹</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mo>⊗</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathsize="0.710em" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{B}}:C({\mathbb{F}})\underset{\Lambda^{\mathbb{\Pi}}}{\otimes}\Lambda^{{\mathbb{\Pi}}^{\prime}}\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which is equivariant with respect to the <math id="S7.Thmthm31.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-actions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.4.2. </span>Multimodules and homotopies</h5>

<div id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that by Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmthm18" title="Proposition 7.18. ‣ 7.2.3. Chain maps and homotopies ‣ 7.2. Algebraic structures without symmetry ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.18</span></a>, given a <math id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded, oriented, unobstructed multimodule, and locally finite <math id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has obtained a chain map</p>
<table id="S7.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{X}}:C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{X}}:C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To obtain a chain map as modules over the Novikov ring, one needs to make use of the equivariance condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm32" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.32</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm32.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{i},{\mathcal{A}}_{i}),i=1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{i},{\mathcal{A}}_{i}),i=1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math> is equivariant with respect to the action of an (untwisted) Novikov group <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{\Pi}_{i},\lambda_{i},\mu_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{\Pi}_{i},\lambda_{i},\mu_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the tensor product</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is a differential graded module over</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}}\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}\cong\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ℤ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}}\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}\cong\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivariant with respect to a Novikov group morphism <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}\to\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the chain map <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>-linear chain map</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{X}}:\left(C_{*}({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}C_{*}({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\right)\underset{\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}}{\otimes}\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}}\to C_{*}({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">ℤ</mo><mo>^</mo></munderover><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">ℤ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathsize="0.710em" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.710em">⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.710em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo mathsize="0.710em">⊕</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathsize="0.710em" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup></munder><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\Phi}^{\mathbb{X}}:\left(C_{*}({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}\cdots\widehat{\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\otimes}}C_{*}({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\right)\underset{\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}}}{\otimes}\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}}\to C_{*}({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In addition, if <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are two such multimodules and there exists a <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant unobstructed and oriented homotopy from <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the corresponding chain maps <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> are homotopic as <math id="S7.Thmthm32.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{{\mathbb{\Pi}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ℤ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\mathbb{Z}}^{{\mathbb{\Pi}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>-linear chain maps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS4.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from the same reasoning as in Lemma <a href="#S7.Thmthm30" title="Proposition 7.30. ‣ 7.4.1. Flow categories and bimodules ‣ 7.4. Algebraic structures with symmetry ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.30</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm33" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm33.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 7.33</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm33.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm33.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a specific case corresponding to the equivariant pair-of-pants product which we would like to address in Section <a href="#S24" title="24. Quantum Steenrod Operations—Proof of Theorem ‣ Part IV EQUIVARIANT FLOER THEORY AND STEENROD OPERATIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> and Section <a href="#S26" title="26. The Equivariant Pair-of-Pants—Proof of Theorem ‣ Part IV EQUIVARIANT FLOER THEORY AND STEENROD OPERATIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> in a more concrete setting rather than the current abstract setting.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.5. </span>Quantitative theories</h4>

<section id="S7.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.5.1. </span>Nonarchimedean linear algebra</h5>

<div id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall some basic notions about nonarchimedean linear algebra systematically used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>. Let <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Pi,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Pi,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> be an ungraded Novikov group; the relevant discussion is insensitive to <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>-grading so we only consider a <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded theory. Let <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf K}</annotation></semantics></math> be a field. Then on the Novikov field <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> there is the standard valuation</p>
<table id="S7.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{v}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}c_{i}T^{a_{i}}\right):=\inf\Big\{\lambda(a_{i})\ |\ c_{i}\neq 0\Big\}\in{\mathbb{R}}\cup\{+\infty\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{v}}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}c_{i}T^{a_{i}}\right):=\inf\Big\{\lambda(a_{i})\ |\ c_{i}\neq 0\Big\}\in{\mathbb{R}}\cup\{+\infty\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is a nonarchimedean field. Notice that in the setting of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite> one requires <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We slightly relax this setting to better fit our discussion. To translate to the setting of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>, denote</p>
<table id="S7.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Pi|:=\lambda(\Pi)\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Pi|:=\lambda(\Pi)\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}</annotation></semantics></math> is an algebra over <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{{\bf K}}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{{\bf K}}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nonarchimedean normed vector space</span> of <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Definition 2.2]</cite>) is a pair <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>-vector space and <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:C\to\{-\infty\}\cup{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:C\to\{-\infty\}\cup{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a function satisfying</p>
<ol id="S7.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(x)=-\infty\Longrightarrow x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(x)=-\infty\Longrightarrow x=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.I13.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\lambda x)=\ell(x)-{\mathfrak{v}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\lambda x)=\ell(x)-{\mathfrak{v}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S7.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.I13.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(x+y)\leq\max\{\ell(x),\ \ell(y)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(x+y)\leq\max\{\ell(x),\ \ell(y)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">There is a notion called <span id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">orthogonalizability</span> on nonarchimedean normed vector spaces (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Definition 2.10]</cite>) over <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{{\bf K}}^{|\Pi|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{{\bf K}}^{|\Pi|}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is satisfied by all concrete cases considered in Floer theory. Finally, Usher–Zhang defined the notion called <span id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Floer-type complex</span> which is crucial in their abstract discussion on barcodes. As the consideration does not necessarily involve grading, we slightly modify the original definition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm34" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm34.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7.34</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm34.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm34.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(cf.<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Definition 4.1]</cite>) Let <math id="S7.Thmthm34.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Pi,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Pi,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> be an ungraded Novikov group and <math id="S7.Thmthm34.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf K}</annotation></semantics></math> be a field.</p>
<ol id="S7.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A nonarchimedean normed vector space <math id="S7.I14.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\ell_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\ell_{C})</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S7.I14.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S7.I14.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">orthogonalizable</span> if the tensor product <math id="S7.I14.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonalizable over <math id="S7.I14.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S7.I14.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Floer-type complex</span> over <math id="S7.I14.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a <math id="S7.I14.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-graded orthogonalizable <math id="S7.I14.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>-space <math id="S7.I14.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> together with an odd <math id="S7.I14.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>-differential <math id="S7.I14.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{C}:C\to C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{C}:C\to C</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="S7.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{C}(d_{C}x)\leq\ell_{C}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{C}(d_{C}x)\leq\ell_{C}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm35" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm35.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 7.35</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm35.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm35.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm35.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is another notion called Floer–Novikov complex defined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite>. It requires that the differential strictly decreases the nonarchimedean norm. On the other hand, that notion allows one to consider Novikov rings with coefficients in a general Noetherian ring and the exponents <math id="S7.Thmthm35.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to be a general finite-rank free abelian group. In the Floer setup, the Floer complex can be made both a Floer–Novikov complex and a Floer-type complex with appropriate Novikov coefficients.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next we have two notions about chain maps and chain homotopies.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm36" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm36.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7.36</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm36.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm36.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm36.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Definition 4.5]</cite>)
Let <math id="S7.Thmthm36.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm36.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be two Floer-type complexes over <math id="S7.Thmthm36.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="S7.I15" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I15.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I15.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I15.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A linear map <math id="S7.I15.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:C\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:C\to D</annotation></semantics></math> is said to <span id="S7.I15.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">preserve the filtration</span> if</p>
<table id="S7.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{D}(\Phi(x))\leq\ell_{C}(x)\ \forall x\in C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{D}(\Phi(x))\leq\ell_{C}(x)\ \forall x\in C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I15.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I15.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I15.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.I15.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I15.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> are said to be <span id="S7.I15.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">filtered isomorphic</span> if there is an isomorphism <math id="S7.I15.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:C\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:C\to D</annotation></semantics></math> of chain complexes such that</p>
<table id="S7.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{D}(\Phi(x))=\ell_{C}(x)\ \forall x\in C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{D}(\Phi(x))=\ell_{C}(x)\ \forall x\in C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I15.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S7.I15.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I15.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two chain maps <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi,\Psi:C\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi,\Psi:C\to D</annotation></semantics></math> are said to be <span id="S7.I15.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">filtered chain homotopic</span> if 1) both <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> preserve the filtration and 2) there exists a homotopy <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:C\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:C\to D</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> which also preserves the filtration. Two Floer-type complexes are <span id="S7.I15.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">filtered chain homotopy equivalent</span> if there exists a filtered chain homotopy <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:C\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:C\to D</annotation></semantics></math> and a filtered homotopy inverse <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi:D\to C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi:D\to C</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi\circ\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi\circ\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> is filtered chain homotopic to <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Id}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Id}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi\circ\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi\circ\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is filtered chain homotopic to <math id="S7.I15.i3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Id}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Id}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">One uses the following notion to compare Floer type complexes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm37" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm37.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7.37</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm37.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\ell_{C},d_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\ell_{C},d_{C})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,\ell_{D},d_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,\ell_{D},d_{C})</annotation></semantics></math> be two Floer-type complexes and <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. A <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-quasiequivalence</span> between <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is a quadruple <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Phi,\Psi,K_{C},K_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Phi,\Psi,K_{C},K_{D})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi:C\to D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi:C\to D</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi:D\to C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi:D\to C</annotation></semantics></math> are chain maps, <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are chain homotopies as</p>
<table id="S7.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \Psi\circ\Phi-{\rm Id}_{C}=d_{C}\circ K_{C}+K_{C}\circ d_{C},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \Psi\circ\Phi-{\rm Id}_{C}=d_{C}\circ K_{C}+K_{C}\circ d_{C},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex114.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \Phi\circ\Psi-{\rm Id}_{D}=d_{D}\circ K_{D}+K_{D}\circ d_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \Phi\circ\Psi-{\rm Id}_{D}=d_{D}\circ K_{D}+K_{D}\circ d_{D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.2" class="ltx_p">satisfying for all <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in D</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S7.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \ell_{D}(\Phi(x))\leq\ell_{C}(x)+\delta,\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \ell_{D}(\Phi(x))\leq\ell_{C}(x)+\delta,\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex115.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \ell_{C}(\Psi(y))\leq\ell_{D}(y)+\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \ell_{C}(\Psi(y))\leq\ell_{D}(y)+\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S7.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \ell_{C}(K_{C}(x))\leq\ell_{C}(x)+2\delta,\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \ell_{C}(K_{C}(x))\leq\ell_{C}(x)+2\delta,\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex116.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \ell_{D}(K_{D}(y))\leq\ell_{D}(y)+2\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \ell_{D}(K_{D}(y))\leq\ell_{D}(y)+2\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">quasiequivalence distance</span> between two Floer-type complexes is the infimum of <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for which there exists a <math id="S7.Thmthm37.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-quasiequivalence between them.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Below we show that the complex obtained from a Novikov flow category is indeed a Floer-type complex, once we use field coefficients.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm38" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm38.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.38</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm38.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm38.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> be a finitely generated Novikov group and let <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}},{\mathcal{A}})</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant Novikov flow category enriched in <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying in addition</span></p>
<ol id="S7.I16" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I16.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I16.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I16.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I16.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The action </span><math id="S7.I16.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I16.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on </span><math id="S7.I16.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I16.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S7.I16.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I16.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-valued and </span><math id="S7.I16.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I16.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S7.I16.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I16.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-valued.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I16.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I16.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I16.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.I16.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}/\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}/\Pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I16.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is finite.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then these data together with the differential on the chain complex <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> define a filtered Floer–Novikov complex in the sense of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>, Definition 1.1]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm38.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm38.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm38.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for any field <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bf K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf K}</annotation></semantics></math>, the complex</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}})\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}})\otimes\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm38.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm38.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">together with the norm <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:={\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:={\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a Floer-type complex over <math id="S7.Thmthm38.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> in the sense of Definition <a href="#S7.Thmthm34" title="Definition 7.34. ‣ 7.5.1. Nonarchimedean linear algebra ‣ 7.5. Quantitative theories ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.34</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first claim is straightforward where we take <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Ob}(\mathring{\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Ob}(\mathring{\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> under the <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>-action equipped with the action <math id="S7.SS5.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we use the incidence coefficients of the differential. For the second, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Section 12]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.5.2. </span>Filtration and spectral invariants</h5>

<div id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any Floer-type complex <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\ell_{C},d_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\ell_{C},d_{C})</annotation></semantics></math>, one can consider the filtration defined by</p>
<table id="S7.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ C^{\leq\tau}=\Big\{x\in C\ |\ \ell_{C}(x)\leq\tau\Big\},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ C^{\leq\tau}=\Big\{x\in C\ |\ \ell_{C}(x)\leq\tau\Big\},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex118.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ C^{&lt;\tau}:=\Big\{x\in C\ |\ \ell_{C}(x)&lt;\tau\Big\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ C^{&lt;\tau}:=\Big\{x\in C\ |\ \ell_{C}(x)&lt;\tau\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> respects the norm, <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\leq\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\leq\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> is a subcomplex. Then for any interval <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\subseteq{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has a corresponding complex defined in a typical way. For example, when <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is the quotient complex</p>
<table id="S7.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{I}:=C^{\leq b}/C^{&lt;a}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{I}:=C^{\leq b}/C^{&lt;a}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in H(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in H(C)</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <span id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">spectral number</span> to be</p>
<table id="S7.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(x):=\inf\Big\{\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}\ |\ x\in{\rm Im}\Big(H(C^{&lt;\tau})\to H(C)\Big)\Big\}\in{\mathbb{R}}\cup\{-\infty\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.500em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(x):=\inf\Big\{\tau\in{\mathbb{R}}\ |\ x\in{\rm Im}\Big(H(C^{&lt;\tau})\to H(C)\Big)\Big\}\in{\mathbb{R}}\cup\{-\infty\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">When the complex <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> comes from a flow category <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denote the spectral number by</p>
<table id="S7.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{{\mathbb{F}}}(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{{\mathbb{F}}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the coefficient ring is understood from the context.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Usher <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite> provided an abstract argument showing the finiteness of spectral numbers and existence of spectral carriers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm39" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm39.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 7.39</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm39.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite>)<span id="S7.Thmthm39.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm39.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmthm39.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm39.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the assumption of Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmthm38" title="Proposition 7.38. ‣ 7.5.1. Nonarchimedean linear algebra ‣ 7.5. Quantitative theories ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.38</span></a>, for any Noetherian ring <math id="S7.Thmthm39.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S7.Thmthm39.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in H_{*}({\mathbb{F}})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in H_{*}({\mathbb{F}})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmthm39.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(a):=c_{\mathbb{F}}(a)&gt;-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(a):=c_{\mathbb{F}}(a)&gt;-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="S7.Thmthm39.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by a cycle contained in <math id="S7.Thmthm39.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{*}({\mathbb{F}})^{\leq\tau(a)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{*}({\mathbb{F}})^{\leq\tau(a)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The theorem follows from Proposition <a href="#S7.Thmthm38" title="Proposition 7.38. ‣ 7.5.1. Nonarchimedean linear algebra ‣ 7.5. Quantitative theories ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.38</span></a> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>, Theorem 1.3]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.5.3. </span>Barcodes</h5>

<div id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the nonarchimedean Gram–Schmidt process established in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Definition 6.3]</cite>, given a Floer-type complex <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\ell_{C},d_{C})=(C,\ell,d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\ell_{C},d_{C})=(C,\ell,d)</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d:C\to C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d:C\to C</annotation></semantics></math> of the ungraded complex factors through <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to\ker(d)\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to\ker(d)\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math>, so we can find an orthogonal basis <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1},\ldots,y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},\ldots,y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and an orthogonal basis of <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\ldots,x_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm ker}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm ker}(d)</annotation></semantics></math> such that one can write <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d:C\to\ker(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d:C\to\ker(d)</annotation></semantics></math> in the block-matrix form</p>
<table id="S7.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}I_{r}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{array}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}I_{r}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0\end{array}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> is the rank of <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and such that</p>
<table id="S7.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(y_{1})-\ell(x_{1})\geq\cdots\geq\ell(y_{r})-\ell(x_{r})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(y_{1})-\ell(x_{1})\geq\cdots\geq\ell(y_{r})-\ell(x_{r}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">verbose barcode</span> of <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,d,\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,d,\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> is the multiset of elements <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{R}}/\Gamma)\times[0,+\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{R}}/\Gamma)\times[0,+\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of</p>
<ol id="S7.I17" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I17.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I17.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I17.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">a pair <math id="S7.I17.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell(x_{i})\ {\rm mod}\ \Gamma,\ell(y_{i})-\ell(x_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>mod</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell(x_{i})\ {\rm mod}\ \Gamma,\ell(y_{i})-\ell(x_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S7.I17.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,r</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I17.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I17.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I17.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">a pair <math id="S7.I17.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\ell(x_{i})\ {\rm mod}\ \Gamma,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>mod</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\ell(x_{i})\ {\rm mod}\ \Gamma,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S7.I17.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=r+1,\ldots,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=r+1,\ldots,m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Each element of this multiset is called a bar while the second variable is called the bar-length. The <span id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">concise barcode</span> is the submultiset obtained by removing bars of length zero. It was proved (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Theorem 7.1]</cite>) that the verbose barcode of a Floer-type complex does not depend on the choice of the singular value decomposition, hence is well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm40" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm40.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 7.40</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm40.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm40.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm40.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm40.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm40.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmthm40.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be two Floer-type complexes over <math id="S7.Thmthm40.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S7.I18" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I18.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I18.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I18.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I18.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S7.I18.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I18.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S7.I18.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I18.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are filtered isomorphic, then they have identical verbose barcodes.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I18.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I18.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I18.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I18.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S7.I18.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I18.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S7.I18.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S7.I18.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are filtered homotopy equivalent, then they have identical concise barcodes.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, Theorem A, B]</cite>, this is true if the Novikov group <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In our setting, the conclusion holds after tensoring with <math id="S7.SS5.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\bf K}^{|\Pi|}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS5.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">7.5.4. </span>Continuity</h5>

<div id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we consider the case of tensor product and discuss quantitative aspects of chain maps. Let <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},{\mathcal{A}}_{1}),\ldots,({\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathcal{A}}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},{\mathcal{A}}_{1}),\ldots,({\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathcal{A}}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> be locally finite flow categories enriched in <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌𝐚𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{{\bf\Psi}{\bf Man}}}</annotation></semantics></math> so there are the associated chain complexes <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that one can consider the completed tensor product (over <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
<table id="S7.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">whose elements are formal sums</p>
<table id="S7.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}\big(p_{i_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes p_{i_{m}}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}a_{i}\big(p_{i_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes p_{i_{m}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\in R</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S7.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{i\to\infty}\big({\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p_{i_{1}})+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{m}(p_{i_{m}})\big)=-\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{i\to\infty}\big({\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p_{i_{1}})+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{m}(p_{i_{m}})\big)=-\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Then there is a similar filtration on the tensor product and for <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{m}\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{m}\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, an inclusion</p>
<table id="S7.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C^{\leq\tau_{1}}({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C^{\leq\tau_{m}}({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to\big(C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\big)^{\leq\tau_{1}+\cdots+\tau_{m}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\leq\tau_{1}}({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C^{\leq\tau_{m}}({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to\big(C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\big)^{\leq\tau_{1}+\cdots+\tau_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm41" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm41.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7.41</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm41.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm41.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm41.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.Thmthm41.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be Novikov flow categories with <math id="S7.Thmthm41.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued actions <math id="S7.Thmthm41.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathcal{A}}_{m},{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathcal{A}}_{m},{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm41.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S7.I19" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S7.I19.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S7.I19.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I19.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.I19.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Novikov multimodule over <math id="S7.I19.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. The <span id="S7.I19.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">threshold</span> of <math id="S7.I19.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number</p>
<table id="S7.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathbb{X}}:=\inf\Big\{{\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p_{1})+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{m}(p_{m})-{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})\ |\ M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\neq\emptyset\Big\}\in[-\infty,\infty]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathbb{X}}:=\inf\Big\{{\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p_{1})+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{m}(p_{m})-{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})\ |\ M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\neq\emptyset\Big\}\in[-\infty,\infty].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I19.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S7.I19.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.I19.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.I19.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.I19.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be two Novikov multimodules over <math id="S7.I19.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S7.I19.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Novikov homotopy from <math id="S7.I19.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S7.I19.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <span id="S7.I19.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">threshold</span> of <math id="S7.I19.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number</p>
<table id="S7.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta^{\mathbb{H}}:=\inf\Big\{{\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p_{1})+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{m}(p_{m})-{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})\ |\ M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\neq\emptyset\Big\}\in[-\infty,+\infty]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\mathbb{H}}:=\inf\Big\{{\mathcal{A}}_{1}(p_{1})+\cdots+{\mathcal{A}}_{m}(p_{m})-{\mathcal{A}}^{\prime}(p^{\prime})\ |\ M_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}\neq\emptyset\Big\}\in[-\infty,+\infty].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By the Novikov property of multimodules (see Definition <a href="#S7.Thmthm2" title="Definition 7.2. ‣ 7.1.2. Convergence ‣ 7.1. Unobstructedness, local finiteness, grading, and orientations ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>), <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathbb{X}}\neq-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathbb{X}}\neq-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\mathbb{H}}\neq-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\mathbb{H}}\neq-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmthm42" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmthm42.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7.42</span></span><span id="S7.Thmthm42.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmthm42.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the situation of Definition <a href="#S7.Thmthm41" title="Definition 7.41. ‣ 7.5.4. Continuity ‣ 7.5. Quantitative theories ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.41</span></a>, the chain map</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex130" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi^{\mathbb{X}}:C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathbb{X}}:C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex131" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi^{\mathbb{X}}\left(\big(C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\big)^{\leq\tau}\right)\subseteq C_{*}^{\leq\tau-\epsilon^{\mathbb{X}}}({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathbb{X}}\left(\big(C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\big)^{\leq\tau}\right)\subseteq C_{*}^{\leq\tau-\epsilon^{\mathbb{X}}}({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The chain homotopy</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi^{\mathbb{H}}:C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathbb{H}}:C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\to C({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmthm42.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Phi^{\mathbb{H}}\left(\big(C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\big)^{\leq\tau}\right)\subseteq C_{*}^{\leq\tau-\delta^{\mathbb{H}}}({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathbb{H}}\left(\big(C({\mathbb{F}}_{1})\widehat{\otimes}\cdots\widehat{\otimes}C({\mathbb{F}}_{m})\big)^{\leq\tau}\right)\subseteq C_{*}^{\leq\tau-\delta^{\mathbb{H}}}({\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS5.SSS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Straightforward check.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8. </span>FOP Perturbations</h3>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we review the technique of FOP perturbations. The original idea was proposed by Fukaya–Ono in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>, and further explored by Parker <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> the authors rigorously established this technique and defined integer-valued Gromov–Witten invariants for general compact symplectic manifolds. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> the authors further proved the integral Arnold conjecture; see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> for another application.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.1. </span>FOP perturbations</h4>

<div id="S8.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8.1</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Perturbations on derived orbifolds)<span id="S8.Thmthm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a derived orbifold <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math>, a <span id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">perturbation</span> of <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> (or of <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>) is a smooth section <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that if <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, then <math id="S8.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> is also compact.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We recall the main “black-box” type theorem proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 8.2</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a><span id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Theorem 1.1]</span></cite><span id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Suppose <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an NC orbifold without boundary<span id="footnote14" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">14</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">14</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">14</span></span>
                    
                    
                    
                  <span id="footnote14.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">When discussing FOP transverse sections for orbifolds with boundaries and corners, the behavior near boundary and corner strata are predetermined.</span></span></span></span> and <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an NC vector bundle. Let <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})</annotation></semantics></math> be the space of smooth sections. Then there is a <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-dense subset <math id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})\subseteq\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>FOP</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})\subseteq\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})</annotation></semantics></math> whose elements are called <em id="S8.Thmthm2.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">FOP transverse sections</em> satisfying the following properties.</span></p>
<ol id="S8.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Classical transversality)</span><span id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a manifold, FOP transversality is equivalent to classical transversality.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Locality Property)</span><span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> The restrictions of FOP transverse sections to open subsets are still FOP transverse.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Extension Property)</span><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For any pair of closed subsets </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Y}}\subseteq{\mathcal{Y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Y}}\subseteq{\mathcal{Y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and open neighborhoods </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}^{\prime}\subseteq{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, if </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}\in\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{V}},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{V}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>FOP</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}\in\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{V}},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{V}}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then there exists </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}\in\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{V}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{V}}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>FOP</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}\in\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{V}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}|_{{\mathcal{V}}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> which agrees with </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> near </span><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Product Property)</span><span id="S8.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Let </span><math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be another normally complex orbifold and </span><math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{E}}^{\prime}\to{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{E}}^{\prime}\to{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a normally complex vector bundle. Then the product map</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})\times\Gamma({\mathcal{U}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}^{\prime})\to\Gamma({\mathcal{U}}\times{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}\boxplus{\mathcal{E}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⊞</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})\times\Gamma({\mathcal{U}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}^{\prime})\to\Gamma({\mathcal{U}}\times{\mathcal{U}}^{\prime},{\mathcal{E}}\boxplus{\mathcal{E}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sends products of FOP transverse sections to FOP transverse sections.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Stabilization Property)</span><span id="S8.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="S8.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathcal{F}}\to{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathcal{F}}\to{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is rigid complex vector bundle</span><span id="footnote15" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">15</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">15</sup>
                        <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">15</span>
                        
                        
                        
                      This condition was stated in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> for more general normally complex vector bundles. When <math id="footnote15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a rigid bundle, the total space <math id="footnote15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> carries a canonical NC structure.</span></span></span><span id="S8.I1.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then the stabilization map</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})\to\Gamma({\mathcal{F}},\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{E}}\oplus\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{F}}),\quad\quad{\mathcal{S}}\mapsto\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{S}}\oplus\tau_{\mathcal{F}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})\to\Gamma({\mathcal{F}},\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{E}}\oplus\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{F}}),\quad\quad{\mathcal{S}}\mapsto\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{S}}\oplus\tau_{\mathcal{F}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.I1.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="S8.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathcal{F}}\to\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathcal{F}}\to\pi_{\mathcal{F}}^{*}{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the tautological section, sends FOP transverse sections to FOP transverse sections.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Main stratum)</span><span id="S8.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> For each </span><math id="S8.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}\in\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>FOP</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}\in\Gamma^{\rm FOP}({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the closure</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)\cap{\mathcal{U}}_{\rm free}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>free</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathcal{S}}^{-1}(0)\cap{\mathcal{U}}_{\rm free}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.I1.i6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I1.i6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is a pseudomanifold (whose dimension is </span><math id="S8.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm dim}{\mathcal{U}}-{\rm rank}{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dim</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm dim}{\mathcal{U}}-{\rm rank}{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I1.i6.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8.3</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>FOP</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>FOP</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> be the category whose objects are</p>
<table id="S8.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{D}}:=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}},{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{D}}:=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}},{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}:=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}:=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> is an NC derived orbifold and <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an FOP transverse perturbation. The morphism from <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{D}}_{1}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{D}}_{1}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{D}}_{2}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{D}}_{2}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is an embedding of underlying stratified orbifolds covered by a bundle embedding <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\iota}}_{21}=(\iota_{21},\widehat{\iota}_{21}):({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1})\to({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜾</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>21</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\iota}}_{21}=(\iota_{21},\widehat{\iota}_{21}):({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1})\to({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> such that it induces both a morphism of <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>NC</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{1}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{1}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{1},{\mathcal{E}}_{1},{\mathcal{S}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}_{2}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}_{2}:=({\mathcal{U}}_{2},{\mathcal{E}}_{2},{\mathcal{S}}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and a morphism with <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="S8.Thmthm3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that there are natural forgetful functors

by forgetting the perturbation part <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. taking the closure of <math id="S8.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})^{-1}(0)\cap{\mathcal{U}}_{\rm free}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>free</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})^{-1}(0)\cap{\mathcal{U}}_{\rm free}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By using Theorem <a href="#S8.Thmthm2" title="Theorem 8.2. ‣ 8.1. FOP perturbations ‣ 8. FOP Perturbations ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8.2</span></a> inductively, one can construct FOP transverse perturbations on stratified derived orbifolds which respect collars.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8.4</span></span><span id="S8.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a regular poset and <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{D}}=({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object of <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}\subseteq A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}\subseteq A</annotation></semantics></math> be an Alexandrov closed subset and</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{A^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{A^{\prime}}{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be the corresponding <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified derived orbifold. Suppose <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{A^{\prime}}:\partial^{A^{\prime}}{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{A^{\prime}}:\partial^{A^{\prime}}{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an FOP transverse perturbation so that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\partial^{A^{\prime}}{\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}},{\mathcal{S}}_{A^{\prime}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\partial^{A^{\prime}}{\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}},{\mathcal{S}}_{A^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is an <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified object of <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>FOP</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists an FOP transverse perturbation <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime}:{\mathcal{U}}\to{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> which extends <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}_{A^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}_{A^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}},{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{U}},{\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{S}},{\mathcal{S}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is an object of <math id="S8.Thmthm4.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>FOP</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm FOP}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8.2. </span>FOP perturbations on flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies</h4>

<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we prove a major result of this paper stating the general procedure of constructing FOP perturbations on flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem N</span></span><span id="Thmthma14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthma14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies in this proposition are assumed to be unobstructed (Definition <a href="#S7.Thmthm1" title="Definition 7.1. ‣ 7.1.1. Unobstructedness ‣ 7.1. Unobstructedness, local finiteness, grading, and orientations ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.1</span></a>) and locally compact (Definition <a href="#S7.Thmthm2" title="Definition 7.2. ‣ 7.1.2. Convergence ‣ 7.1. Unobstructedness, local finiteness, grading, and orientations ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.2</span></a>, <a href="#S7.Thmthm5" title="Definition 7.5. ‣ 7.1.2. Convergence ‣ 7.1. Unobstructedness, local finiteness, grading, and orientations ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.5</span></a>, <a href="#S7.Thmthm6" title="Definition 7.6. ‣ 7.1.2. Convergence ‣ 7.1. Unobstructedness, local finiteness, grading, and orientations ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.6</span></a>, and <a href="#S7.Thmthm8" title="Definition 7.8. ‣ 7.1.2. Convergence ‣ 7.1. Unobstructedness, local finiteness, grading, and orientations ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.8</span></a>). We also assume that all charts have compact zero locus.</span></p>
<ol id="S8.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(FOP perturbation for equivariant flow categories)</span><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Let </span><math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a twisted Novikov group (Definition </span><a href="#S7.Thmthm21" title="Definition 7.21 (Novikov groups). ‣ 7.3.1. Twisted Novikov groups ‣ 7.3. Symmetries on flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.21</span></a><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) and let </span><math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a free </span><math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-equivariant flow category enriched in </span><math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a </span><math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋊</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}\rtimes G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-equivariant FOP perturbation </span><math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on </span><math id="S8.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(FOP perturbation for equivariant multimodules)</span><span id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Let </span><math id="S8.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}_{1},\ldots,\mathbb{\Pi}_{m};\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}_{1},\ldots,\mathbb{\Pi}_{m};\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be Novikov groups and </span><math id="S8.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a finite group acting on </span><math id="S8.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}_{1}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{\Pi}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and on </span><math id="S8.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Pi}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Let</span></p>
