<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S12.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I2.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be two compatible sets of integral actions. Let </span><math id="S12.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{(s)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I2.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be an AMS lift subject to the fixed outercollaring width and one set of integral actions. Let </span><math id="S12.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{F}_{j}\mathbb{F}_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>01</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{F}_{j}\mathbb{F}_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I2.i1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(10)}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(10)}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I2.i1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the lift provided by Proposition </span><a href="#S12.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 12.2. ‣ 12.1. Main statements for Floer flow categories ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12.2</span></a><span id="S12.I2.i1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a lift of the outercollaring of </span><math id="S12.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I2.i1.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as a homotopy from</span></p>
