<div id="S12.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S12.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Section <a href="#S20" title="20. Comparing Non-homotopic Choices ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now we state the corresponding results for homotopies of multimodules from varying Floer data on smooth domains.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem Q</span></span><span id="Thmthma17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthma17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationh1" title="Situation Homotopy(i). ‣ 11.1. Homotopies from varying Floer data ‣ 11. Homotopies of Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(i)</span></a>, fix an outercollaring width and a compatible set of integral actions on involved Floer flow categories <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\tilde{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\tilde{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be AMS lifts of these flow categories subject to the fixed outercollaring width and the integral actions. Let <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be AMS lifts of <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the same outercollaring width and the integral actions. Then there exists a lift of the outercollaring of <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, called an AMS lift subject to the outercollaring width and integral actions as a homotopy from <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmthma17.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S12.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Section <a href="#S18" title="18. Proofs of the Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">To establish algebraic relation such as the associativity of pair-of-pants product, one needs to consider the homotopy of multimodules corresponding to gluing of Floer domains. Recall the following setup. Let <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Floer domain with <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> negative ends and one positive end, defining a multimodule <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{G}}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{G}}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>𝕐</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Floer domain with <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> negative ends and one positive ends defining a multimodule <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Here the source and target flow categories are all Floer flow categories associated to the limiting Hamiltonians on the two Floer domains. Recall that the concatenation <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a multimodule over <math id="S12.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{i-1},{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{i+1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{i-1},{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{i+1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n};{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S12.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S12.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 12.4</span></span><span id="S12.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S12.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a common outercollaring width. In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationc1" title="Situation Concatenation(i). ‣ 10.4. Concatenations ‣ 10. Geometric Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Concatenation(i)</span></a>, choose integral actions on the involved flow categories which are compatible with respect to <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{n},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{n},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be AMS lifts of <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n},{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔾</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m},{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{G}}_{n},{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively subject to the fixed outercollaring width and the integral actions. Let <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an AMS lift to <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the fixed outercollaring width and the chosen integral actions provided by Theorem <a href="#Thmthma16" title="Theorem P. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">P</span></a>. Let <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be their descendants to <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math> which, by the discussion in Subsection <a href="#S10.SS4" title="10.4. Concatenations ‣ 10. Geometric Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.4</span></a>, admit a natural concatenation <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\circ\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\circ\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists a concatenation <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm13" title="Definition 6.13. ‣ 6.5.2. General concatenations ‣ 6.5. Multimodule concatenations ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.13</span></a>) which is a lift of <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}_{0}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S12.Thmthm4.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="footnote18" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">18</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">18</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">18</span></span>
                    
                    
                    
                  <span id="footnote18.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">For the purpose of this paper, we do not need to prove that the concatenation </span><math id="footnote18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote18.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> is well-defined up to homotopy.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S12.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Section <a href="#S19" title="19. Concatenation and Gluing—Proof of Theorem ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, let <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S}{\mathbb{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S}{\mathbb{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the family of Floer domains obtained from gluing along positive end of <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> matched with the negative end of <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>𝕐</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, each of which defines a multimodule <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S}{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S}{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall (see Subsection <a href="#S11.SS2" title="11.2. Homotopies from gluing ‣ 11. Homotopies of Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11.2</span></a>) that there is a homotopy <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{W}}:={\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S_{0}}{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕎</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{W}}:={\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S_{0}}{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S12.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}\gg 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≫</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}\gg 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem R</span></span><span id="Thmthma18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmthma18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a common outercollaring width. In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationg1" title="Situation Glue(i). ‣ 11.2. Homotopies from gluing ‣ 11. Homotopies of Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Glue(i)</span></a>, choose integral actions on involved flow categories which are compatible with respect to the homotopy <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{l},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{l},\tilde{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are AMS lifts of the involved Floer flow categories subject to the fixed outercollaring width and the integral actions. Let <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be AMS lifts of the outercollaring of <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> as multimodules over <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> resp. over <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{l};\tilde{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{\mathbb{G}}_{l};\tilde{\mathbb{G}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the fixed outercollaring width and the chosen integral actions. Let <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a concatenation provided by Theorem <a href="#S12.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 12.4. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12.4</span></a>. Let <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an AMS lift of the multimodule associated to the smooth domain <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S}{\mathbb{Y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></msub><mi>𝕐</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{S}{\mathbb{Y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the same outercollaring width and the chosen integral actions. Then there exists a class of lifts of the outercollaring of <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}^{\rm NC}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> as a homotopy from <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{X}}\circ_{i}\tilde{\mathbb{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each lift in this class is called an AMS lift of <math id="Thmthma18.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S12.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Section <a href="#S19" title="19. Concatenation and Gluing—Proof of Theorem ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S12.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 12.5</span></span><span id="S12.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S12.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We do not discuss comparing non-homotopic choices in the constructions of lifts of homotopies. We only use homotopies to ensure well-defineness of operations induced by flow multimodules, so we stop our discussion on non-homotopic choices at multimodules.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S12.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">12.3. </span>Bimodules and homotopies associated to PSS type maps</h4>

<div id="S12.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We state the main technical theorem towards the definition of the PSS and SSP maps (cf. Theorem <a href="#Thmthma5" title="Theorem E (PSS and SSP maps). ‣ 1.1.4. PSS map and isomorphism ‣ 1.1. Main results on Floer complexes ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem S</span></span><span id="Thmthma19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma19.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthma19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> be Floer flow category on <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a Hamiltonian <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and a time-independent almost complex structure <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Morse flow category on <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a Morse–Smale pair <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,g)</annotation></semantics></math> with the standard behavior near critical points. Let <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="Thmthma19.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Morse-to-Floer resp. Floer-to-Morse bimodule associated to certain Floer data on the infinite cylinder. Fix an outercollaring width.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma19.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S12.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S12.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S12.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Choose an integral action </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}\to{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝔽</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}\to{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> which is compatible with respect to </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. to </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Let </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be an AMS lift of </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> subject to the outercollaring width and the integral action. Then there exists a lift of the outercollaring of </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as a bimodule over </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}};\tilde{\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝕄</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}};\tilde{\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. over </span><math id="S12.I3.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\tilde{\mathbb{F}};{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝕄</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mathbb{F}};{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S12.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S12.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega_{(s)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝔽</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega_{(s)}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0,1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be two integral actions which are compatible with respect to </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Let </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}_{(s)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be AMS lifts of </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> subject to </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega_{(s)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝔽</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega_{(s)}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and let </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(s)}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(s)}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(s)}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(s)}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be AMS lift of </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> subject to </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}}^{\Omega_{(s)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝔽</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}}^{\Omega_{(s)}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Let </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{FF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>01</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{FF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the AMS lift provided by Proposition </span><a href="#S12.Thmthm2" title="Proposition 12.2. ‣ 12.1. Main statements for Floer flow categories ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12.2</span></a><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a homotopy from </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(1)}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(1)}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to the composition </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(0)}^{\mathbb{MF}}\circ\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{FF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>01</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(0)}^{\mathbb{MF}}\circ\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{FF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. there exists a homotopy from </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(0)}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(0)}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to the composition </span><math id="S12.I3.i2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{FF}}\circ\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(1)}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>01</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}_{(01)}^{\mathbb{FF}}\circ\tilde{\mathbb{B}}_{(1)}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I3.i2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S12.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Subsection <a href="#S21.SS5" title="21.5. Morse-to-Floer and Floer-to-Morse bimodules ‣ 21. AMS Construction for Other Flow categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21.5</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S12.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 12.6</span></span><span id="S12.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S12.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathbb{M}}^{\prime},\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{M}^{\prime}\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},{\mathbb{M}}^{\prime},\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{M}^{\prime}\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}\mathbb{M}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}\mathbb{M}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be another set of Floer flow category, Morse flow category, Morse-to-Floer and Floer-to-Morse as in Theorem <a href="#Thmthma19" title="Theorem S. ‣ 12.3. Bimodules and homotopies associated to PSS type maps ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S</span></a>. Let <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FF}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FF}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a bimodule over <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{F};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{F};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a Floer datum on the infinite cylinder. Let <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MM}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MM}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a bimodule over <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{M};{\mathbb{M}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{M};{\mathbb{M}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a one-parameter family of Morse data. Let <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a homotopy from <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FF}^{\prime}}\circ\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}\mathbb{M}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FF}^{\prime}}\circ\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}\mathbb{M}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}\circ\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MM^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}\circ\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MM^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math> by gluing the Floer/Morse data and varying in a one-parameter family. Then there exist AMS lifts <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and AMS lifts <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math> (as a bimodule over <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\tilde{\mathbb{F}};{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝕄</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mathbb{F}};{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}{\mathbb{M}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}{\mathbb{M}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (as a bimodule over <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{M}^{\prime};\tilde{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝕄</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{M}^{\prime};\tilde{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, an AMS lift <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FF}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FF}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a lift of the outercollaring of <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S12.Thmthm6.p1.m20" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S12.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Subsection <a href="#S21.SS5" title="21.5. Morse-to-Floer and Floer-to-Morse bimodules ‣ 21. AMS Construction for Other Flow categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21.5</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S12.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">12.3.1. </span>PSS maps and pearly flow category</h5>

<div id="S12.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we consider the pearly flow category and its diagonal bimodule.</p>
</div>
<div id="S12.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S12.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 12.7</span></span><span id="S12.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S12.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S12.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact symplectic manifold.</span></p>
<ol id="S12.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S12.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S12.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the pearly flow category associated to a Morse–Smale pair </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f,g)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a compatible almost complex structure </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then upon choosing an integral symplectic form </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> which is tamed by </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, any outercollaring of </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> admits a set of lifts </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S12.I4.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Each individual lift is called an </span><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AMS lift</span><span id="S12.I4.i1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (subject to the outercollaring width and the integral symplectic form).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S12.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S12.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="S12.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the diagonal bimodule over </span><math id="S12.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{P}};{\mathbb{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{P}};{\mathbb{P}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Let </span><math id="S12.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{0},\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{0},\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be AMS lifts of </span><math id="S12.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> subject to the same outercollaring width and an integral symplectic form. Then there exists a lift of the outercollaring of </span><math id="S12.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S12.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as a bimodule over </span><math id="S12.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{0};\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{0};\tilde{\mathbb{P}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I4.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S12.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S12.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S12.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Section <a href="#S21.SS1" title="21.1. Pearly flow category ‣ 21. AMS Construction for Other Flow categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S12.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">12.3.2. </span>The triangle of Morse, Floer and pearly flow categories</h5>

<div id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that in Subsection <a href="#S10.SS3" title="10.3. PSS type bimodules ‣ 10. Geometric Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10.3</span></a>, besides the Morse-to-Floer and Floer-to-Morse bimodules, we also described a few other bimodules, namely the Pearly-to-Floer bimodule <math id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{PF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{PF}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Floer-to-Pearly bimodule <math id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FP}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Pearly-to-Morse bimodule <math id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{PM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{PM}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the Morse-to-Pearly bimodule <math id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MP}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, one has the diagonal bimodules <math id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{FF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{FF}}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is a special case for the continuation map bimodule), <math id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S12.SS3.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{MM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{MM}}</annotation></semantics></math> (a deformation of the diagonal bimodule of the classical Morse flow category). These bimodules are related by a triangle which commutes up to homotopies of bimodules.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmthma20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmthma20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem T</span></span><span id="Thmthma20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmthma20.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmthma20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a common outercollaring width and an integral action <math id="Thmthma20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝔽</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> compatible with all involved bimodules and homotopy. There exist the following objects.</span></p>
<ol id="S12.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S12.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S12.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An AMS lift </span><math id="S12.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S12.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (subject to the outercollaring width and the integral action).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S12.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S12.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">An AMS lift </span><math id="S12.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S12.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (subject to the outercollaring width and the integral symplectic form).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S12.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S12.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lifts of the outercollaring of </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FP}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{FP}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{MP}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{PM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{B}^{\mathbb{PM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{FF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{FF}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{PP}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{MM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{\Delta}^{\mathbb{MM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by</span></p>
<table id="S12.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S12.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FM}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{PM}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{FF}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{PP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{MM}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FM}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{FP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{PM}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{FF}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{PP}},\ \tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{MM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S12.I5.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which are bimodules over two of the three flow categories </span><math id="S12.I5.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}},\tilde{\mathbb{P}},{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}},\tilde{\mathbb{P}},{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S12.I5.i3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="Thmthma20.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmthma20.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the following diagram commutes in the following sense.</span></p>
<table id="S12.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S12.E1.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="196.42" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-151.707369607894px" version="1.1" viewBox="47.33 151.71 371.43 196.42" width="371.43"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 47.33429651826484 196.42043545877223) translate(0,3.54) translate(47.33,0)"><g transform="translate(124.23,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.66em;font-size:10pt;" height="18.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="19.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S12.E1.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{M}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(73.87,0) translate(0,-75.46) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.99" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="22.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S12.E1.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MF}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(8,0) translate(0,-110.85)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.43 0.6" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 4.97 5.55" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 138.1393987904516 0 C 101.99112269959873 -50.1684154797115 55.94464939825264 -88.41236283938485 0 -114.73182096543344" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(121.57,0) translate(0,35.57) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.99" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="24.83"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S12.E1.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{MM}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_double-struck" mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="double-struck">Δ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝕄</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\tilde{\mathbb{\Delta}}^{\mathbb{MM}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(130.22,0) translate(0,10.07)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -0.88 7.4" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -5.74 4.75" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 138.1393987904516 0 C 173.36268865074115 35.22328986028954 102.91610893016207 35.22328986028954 138.1393987904516 0" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(211.99,0) translate(0,-39.28) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.65em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.99" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="22.83"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S12.E1.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MP}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔹</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝕄</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">ℙ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\tilde{\mathbb{B}}^{\mathbb{MP}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(268.36,0) translate(0,-104.13)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -2.09 7.15" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.44 3.74" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 138.1393987904516 0 C 194.08404818870426 -26.319415898875313 240.13052149005034 -64.56336325854868 276.2787975809032 -114.73182096543344" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-7.99,0) translate(0,-114.73) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.56em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.99" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="7.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><m