<div id="S14.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS1.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Again, a monotone homotopy induces an ordinary homotopy <math id="S14.SS1.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S14.SS1.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S14.SS1.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with</p>
<table id="S14.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="M_{a_{1}\cdots a_{m};a^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}:=\left\{\begin{array}[]{cl}M_{a_{1}+\cdots+a_{m}-a^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{h}},&amp;\ a_{1}+\cdots+a_{m}\geq a^{\prime},\\
\emptyset,&amp;\ {\rm otherwise}.\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕙</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>otherwise</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{a_{1}\cdots a_{m};a^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}:=\left\{\begin{array}[]{cl}M_{a_{1}+\cdots+a_{m}-a^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{h}},&amp;\ a_{1}+\cdots+a_{m}\geq a^{\prime},\\
\emptyset,&amp;\ {\rm otherwise}.\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">14.2. </span>The category of curves</h4>

<div id="S14.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following definition may not be the most canonical one. However, as we will consider only very concrete objects, the <span id="S14.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ad hoc</span> description suffices our purpose. We should remind the reader that the following definition goes beyond the algebro-geometric situation as the base <math id="S14.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is typically only a stratified smooth manifold.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14.6</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">equivariant families of curves</span> is a triple <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a (not necessarily reductive) complex Lie group containing a maximal compact subgroup <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> are stratified smooth <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>-manifolds, with a <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant map <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to B</annotation></semantics></math>, and the structure of a prestable genus zero complex curve on each fiber <math id="S14.Thmthm6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\phi}\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\phi}\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math>. This triple needs to satisfy the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S14.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S14.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S14.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="S14.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="S14.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:C_{\phi}\to C_{g\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:C_{\phi}\to C_{g\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism of complex curves.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S14.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S14.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{C}\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{C}\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math> be the complement of fiberwise nodes. Then <math id="S14.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stratified <math id="S14.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold and the map <math id="S14.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{C}\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{C}\to B</annotation></semantics></math> is a submersion.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each object <math id="S14.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce</p>
<table id="S14.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S14.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S14.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ P_{\mathcal{C}}={\mathcal{G}}/G,\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ P_{\mathcal{C}}={\mathcal{G}}/G,\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S14.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ Q_{\mathcal{C}}={\rm Lie}({\mathcal{G}})/{\rm Lie}G." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Lie</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>Lie</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ Q_{\mathcal{C}}={\rm Lie}({\mathcal{G}})/{\rm Lie}G.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can also add additional structures to an equivariant family of curves, such as a collection of marked points, which are precisely <math id="S14.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant sections of <math id="S14.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\to B</annotation></semantics></math> avoiding nodes and each other. Another structure we will use all the time is the cylindrical ends around markings and nodes, which are choices of germs of cylindrical coordinates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We define morphisms of the category of equivariant families of curves.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14.7</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S14.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> be an equivariant family of curves.</p>
<ol id="S14.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S14.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S14.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S14.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">group enlargement</span> of <math id="S14.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> is an equivariant family of curves <math id="S14.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}^{\prime}=({\mathcal{G}}^{\prime},B^{\prime},C^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}^{\prime}=({\mathcal{G}}^{\prime},B^{\prime},C^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S14.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}\to{\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}\to{\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a complex Lie group embedding which sends the compact group <math id="S14.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S14.I5.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S14.I5.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\prime}={\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}\times_{\mathcal{G}}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\prime}={\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}\times_{\mathcal{G}}B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.I5.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}={\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}\times_{\mathcal{G}}C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}={\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}\times_{\mathcal{G}}C</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the group enlargement as such by</p>
<table id="S14.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}\times_{\mathcal{G}}{\mathcal{C}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}^{\prime}\times_{\mathcal{G}}{\mathcal{C}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S14.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S14.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict morphism</span> from <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{1}=({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{1}=({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{2}=({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{2}=({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}:{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}:{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, consists of a complex Lie group embedding <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{{\mathcal{G}}}:{\mathcal{G}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{{\mathcal{G}}}:{\mathcal{G}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> which restricts to a group map <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{G}:G_{1}\to G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{G}:G_{1}\to G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and an equivariant commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S14.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S14.Ex23.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="81.53" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-62.444847088987046px" version="1.1" viewBox="12.85 62.44 84.61 81.53" width="84.61"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 12.849686600054483 81.53378856253028) translate(0,3.46) translate(12.85,0)"><g transform="translate(-12.69,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.09"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex23.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{C_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{C_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.694501738273143 -0.27673578005007266 L 12.694501738273143 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(17.73,0) translate(0,9.54) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.79" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.9)" width="15.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex23.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\zeta_{21}^{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ζ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\zeta_{21}^{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.21,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.694501738273143 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.21369290751046 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.21369290751046 -0.27673578005007266 L 46.21369290751046 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.21,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.09"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex23.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{C_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{C_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.631437752146894 -9.685900096859001 L 59.18490931224704 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(58.91,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.631437752146894 -33.208800332088 L 59.18490931224704 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 58.631437752146894 -33.208800332088 L 59.18490931224704 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-12.85,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex23.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{B_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{B_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.849686600054483 -43.63264139549389 L 12.849686600054483 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(17.73,0) translate(0,-52.9) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.09em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.79" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.9)" width="15.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex23.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\zeta_{21}^{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ζ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\zeta_{21}^{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(46.06,0) translate(0,-43.36)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 12.849686600054483 -43.63264139549389 L 46.058486932142486 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 46.058486932142486 -43.63264139549389 L 46.058486932142486 -43.07916983539375" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(46.06,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="17.4"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex23.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{B_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{B_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.I5.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">satisfying 1) the map <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{B}:B_{1}\to B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{B}:B_{1}\to B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stratified smooth map; 2) the map <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{C}:C_{1}\to C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{C}:C_{1}\to C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous such that the restricted map <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{C}_{1}\to\mathring{C}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{C}_{1}\to\mathring{C}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and such that for each <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}\in B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}\in B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sent to <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{2}\in B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{2}\in B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the induced map <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{C}_{\phi_{1}}\to\mathring{C}_{\phi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{C}_{\phi_{1}}\to\mathring{C}_{\phi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism (of complex curves together with extra structures such as germs of cylindrical ends and marked points). Notice that a strict morphism <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a strict morphism from <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}{\mathcal{C}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}{\mathcal{C}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S14.I5.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S14.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A strict morphism is called a <span id="S14.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict embedding</span> if the induced map <math id="S14.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S14.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S14.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">unitary conjugation</span> of <math id="S14.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> is a strict morphism induced from an element <math id="S14.I5.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math> which lifts the conjugation action of <math id="S14.I5.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S14.I5.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I5.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S14.I5.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I5.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S14.I5.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">embedding</span> of equivariant families of curves is a unitary conjugacy class of strict embeddings, where we declare that two strict embeddings <math id="S14.I5.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are equivalent if one can be taken to another via a unitary conjugation of <math id="S14.I5.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I5.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="S14.I5.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I5.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The category of equivariant families of curves, denoted by <math id="S14.I5.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is the category whose objects are equivariant families of curves and whose morphisms are embeddings.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that the category <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> is monoidal: given two object <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{i}=({\mathcal{G}}_{i},B_{i},C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{i}=({\mathcal{G}}_{i},B_{i},C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, the product <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{1}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{1}\times B_{2},C_{1}\sqcup C_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{1}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{1}\times B_{2},C_{1}\sqcup C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> where the fiber of <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\sqcup C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\sqcup C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\in B_{1}\times B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{1},\phi_{2})\in B_{1}\times B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the disjoint union <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\phi_{1}}\sqcup C_{\phi_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\phi_{1}}\sqcup C_{\phi_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The initial object, which is <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified (see Definition <a href="#S2.Thmthm10" title="Definition 2.10. ‣ 2.2. Regular stratification categories and presentations ‣ 2. Regular Stratification Categories ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.10</span></a>), is the object with <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> being the trivial group, <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> being the singleton, and <math id="S14.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> being empty.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that the category <math id="S14.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> also allows outercollaring.</p>
</div>
<section id="S14.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.2.1. </span>Lateral lines</h5>

<div id="S14.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the notation of lateral lines, which are used for gluing domains of solutions to Floer equations in various flow-category constructions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14.8</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S14.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S14.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S14.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth genus zero curve with cylindrical ends. A <span id="S14.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lateral line</span> in <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a real curve <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}\cong\ell\subseteq\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>≅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}\cong\ell\subseteq\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying: near <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in a cylindrical end of <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and in cylindrical coordinates, is parametrized by <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,0)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, for domains of Floer trajectories, this amounts to an <math id="S14.I6.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>-orbit of the translation action on the cylinder.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S14.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S14.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> be an equivariant family of curves equipped with marked points and cylindrical ends. A family of lateral lines is a collection of lateral lines <math id="S14.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\phi}\subseteq C_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\phi}\subseteq C_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S14.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{g\phi}=g(\ell_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{g\phi}=g(\ell_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S14.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.I6.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By abuse of notations, we use <math id="S14.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the category of equivariant family of curves equipped with cylindrical ends and lateral lines. It is easy to see that lateral lines can be concatenated (as we always require the angular coordinate to be <math id="S14.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\in S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\in S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>), which also guarantees their existence by induction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.2.2. </span>Rigidifications</h5>

<div id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To fit into the construction of Kuranishi charts and FOP perturbations, we need to introduce the more refined category <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>. Comparing to other “rigidified” morphisms in categories such as <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the difference between the domain and target of an embedding in <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> is caused typically by the enlargement of the complex Lie group. So the rigidification becomes more specific.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14.9</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> be a strict embedding in <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidification</span> of <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of an orthogonal representation <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
a germ of <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant maps</p>
<table id="S14.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\to B_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\to B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(where <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> acts diagonally on the domain) whose restriction to <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}\times\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}\times\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the map</p>
<table id="S14.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}(B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon})\to&amp;\ B_{2},\\
[g_{2},(b_{1},\eta_{21})]\mapsto&amp;\ g_{2}\theta_{21}(b_{1},\eta_{21})\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}(B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon})\to&amp;\ B_{2},\\
[g_{2},(b_{1},\eta_{21})]\mapsto&amp;\ g_{2}\theta_{21}(b_{1},\eta_{21})\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">is a diffeomorphism onto an open neighborhood of the image of <math id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S14.Thmthm9.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict rigidified embedding</span> is a strict embedding together with a rigidification.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that the group embedding <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{\mathcal{G}}:{\mathcal{G}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{\mathcal{G}}:{\mathcal{G}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a linear injection</p>
<table id="S14.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{{\mathcal{C}}_{1}}\to Q_{{\mathcal{C}}_{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{{\mathcal{C}}_{1}}\to Q_{{\mathcal{C}}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> is necessarily isomorphic to its cokernel.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Each group element <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{2}\in G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{2}\in G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a strict rigidified embedding from <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to itself.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 14.10</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Strict rigidified embeddings can be composed.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{i}=({\mathcal{G}}_{i},B_{i},C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{i}=({\mathcal{G}}_{i},B_{i},C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math> are three equivariant families. Let <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}:{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}:{\mathcal{C}}_{1}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{32}:{\mathcal{C}}_{2}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{32}:{\mathcal{C}}_{2}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be strict embeddings with rigidifications</span></p>
<table id="S14.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S14.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S14.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S14.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \theta_{32}:B_{2}\times Q_{32}^{\epsilon}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>32</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \theta_{32}:B_{2}\times Q_{32}^{\epsilon}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The composed rigidification consists of the representation <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{21}\oplus Q_{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{21}\oplus Q_{32}</annotation></semantics></math>, the neighborhood <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\oplus Q_{32}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>32</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\oplus Q_{32}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the map</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\theta_{31}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\times Q_{32}^{\epsilon}\to&amp;\ {\mathcal{G}}_{3},\\
(b_{1},\eta_{21},\eta_{32})\mapsto&amp;\ \theta_{32}\Big(\theta_{21}(b_{1},\eta_{21}),\eta_{32}\Big).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>31</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>32</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>32</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\theta_{31}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\times Q_{32}^{\epsilon}\to&amp;\ {\mathcal{G}}_{3},\\
(b_{1},\eta_{21},\eta_{32})\mapsto&amp;\ \theta_{32}\Big(\theta_{21}(b_{1},\eta_{21}),\eta_{32}\Big).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The property that the induced map is a diffeomorphism onto a neighborhood of <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{31}^{B}(B_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>31</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{31}^{B}(B_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> is an obvious consequence of the corresponding properties for the two rigidified embeddings.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14.11</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S14.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> has morphisms being conjugacy classes of strict rigidified embeddings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that we can naturally define the collared version of <math id="S14.SS2.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by</p>
<table id="S14.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.2.3. </span>Stable complex structure</h5>

<div id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to define a category <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>ℂ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> of equivariant families of curves whose bases have equivariant stable complex structures.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14.12</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stable complex structure</span> on an equivariant family of curves <math id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant stable complex structure of the tangent bundle <math id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TB</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm17" title="Definition 3.17. ‣ 3.3.2. Stable complex structures ‣ 3.3. Stable complex structures and normal complex structures ‣ 3. Kuranishi Spaces ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.17</span></a>). Recall that it consists of a <math id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant complex vector bundle <math id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\to B</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S14.Thmthm12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant stable isomorphism</p>
<table id="S14.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:TB\overset{s}{\to}I." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑠</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:TB\overset{s}{\to}I.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To define morphisms of stably complex objects, note the following fact. Let <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> be a strict embedding of equivariant families of curves. Notice that there are <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundles</p>
<table id="S14.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S14.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S14.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}TB_{1},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}TB_{1},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S14.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \pi^{*}T({\mathcal{G}}_{2}/{\mathcal{G}}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \pi^{*}T({\mathcal{G}}_{2}/{\mathcal{G}}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}B_{1}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}/{\mathcal{G}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}B_{1}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}/{\mathcal{G}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> temporarily denotes the natural projection.
Via <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can see that there is a <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant bundle isomorphism</p>
<table id="S14.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TB_{2}\cong\pi^{*}T({\mathcal{G}}_{2}/{\mathcal{G}}_{1})\oplus({\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}TB_{1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TB_{2}\cong\pi^{*}T({\mathcal{G}}_{2}/{\mathcal{G}}_{1})\oplus({\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{1}}TB_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the first summand is complex. Hence a stable complex structure on <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> naturally induces a stable complex structure on <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> via the strict embedding <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can see that the induced one is invariant under unitary conjugations of strict embeddings. Hence one can make the following definition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14.13</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A strict embedding of equivariant families of curves with stably complex structures from <math id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1},I_{1},\tau_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1},I_{1},\tau_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2},I_{2},\tau_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2},I_{2},\tau_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is a strict embedding <math id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> such that the bundle isomorphism (<a href="#S14.E2" title="In 14.2.3. Stable complex structure ‣ 14.2. The category of curves ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.2</span></a>) respects the <math id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant stable complex structures. The category <math id="S14.Thmthm13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>ℂ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of objects being equivariant families of curves with stable complex structures whose morphisms are unitary conjugacy classes of strict embeddings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">One can also define rigidifications for strict embeddings in <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>ℂ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, suppose</p>
<table id="S14.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1},I_{1},\tau_{1}),\ ({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2},I_{2},\tau_{2})\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>ℂ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1},I_{1},\tau_{1}),\ ({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2},I_{2},\tau_{2})\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S14.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">is a strict embedding. Suppose</p>
<table id="S14.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">is a rigidification of <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> as a strict embedding in <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the image</p>
<table id="S14.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}^{\epsilon}:={\rm Im}(G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}(B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon})\to B_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}^{\epsilon}:={\rm Im}(G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}(B_{1}\times Q_{21}^{\epsilon})\to B_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">which is a <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant open subset of <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. There is a projection</p>
<table id="S14.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}^{\epsilon}\to G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}B_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}^{\epsilon}\to G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}B_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p">We say that the rigidification <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> respects the stable complex structure if over <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, the stable complex structure on <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is pulled back from its restriction to <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{2}\times_{G_{1}}B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> via the above projection. This provides a category <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>rig</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. One also has the corresponding collared version <math id="S14.SS2.SSS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">14.3. </span>Construction of the domain flow categories</h4>

<div id="S14.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The purpose of the rest of this section is to construct monotone flow categories (Definition <a href="#S14.Thmthm1" title="Definition 14.1. ‣ 14.1.1. Monotone flow category ‣ 14.1. Monotone flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.1</span></a>) enriched in the category <math id="S14.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as monotone flow bimodules and homotopies.</p>
</div>
<section id="S14.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.3.1. </span>Some Lie groups and homogeneous spaces</h5>

<div id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will consider variants of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(d)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="GL(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">GL(d)</annotation></semantics></math>. Inside <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PGL(d+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PGL(d+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, there are two complex subgroups</p>
<table id="S14.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d}^{-}:=PGL^{-}(d+1)=\left\{\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}1&amp;*\\
0&amp;*\end{array}\right]\in PGL(d+1)\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d}^{-}:=PGL^{-}(d+1)=\left\{\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}1&amp;*\\
0&amp;*\end{array}\right]\in PGL(d+1)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S14.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d}^{+}:=PGL^{+}(d+1)=\left\{\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}*&amp;0\\
&amp;1\end{array}\right]\in PGL(d+1)\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>G</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mo>∗</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d}^{+}:=PGL^{+}(d+1)=\left\{\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}*&amp;0\\
&amp;1\end{array}\right]\in PGL(d+1)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In this paper we will use exclusively the positive version<span id="footnote19" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">19</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">19</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">19</span>
                  
                  
                  
                This preference is due to the fact that the domains of multimodules always have a unique output. However, for Floer flow categories, using the negative version is also possible.</span></span></span>, hence we simply denote <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d}={\mathcal{G}}_{d}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d}={\mathcal{G}}_{d}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. The unitary group <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}:=U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}:=U(d)</annotation></semantics></math> embeds into <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="S14.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(d)\ni g\mapsto\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}g&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{array}\right]\in{\mathcal{G}}_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∋</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(d)\ni g\mapsto\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}g&amp;0\\
0&amp;1\end{array}\right]\in{\mathcal{G}}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">One needs to consider certain specific group embeddings for different <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>’s. The embedding</p>
<table id="S14.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d_{1}}\times G_{d_{2}}=U(d_{1})\times U(d_{2})\to G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}=U(d_{1}+d_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d_{1}}\times G_{d_{2}}=U(d_{1})\times U(d_{2})\to G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}=U(d_{1}+d_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">is obvious. For the corresponding complex Lie group <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are corresponding embeddings. For example, for <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}=d_{2}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}=d_{2}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the embedding <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{2}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> reads</p>
<table id="S14.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}a_{11}&amp;a_{12}&amp;0\\
a_{21}&amp;a_{22}&amp;0\\
a_{31}&amp;a_{32}&amp;1\end{array}\right],\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}b_{11}&amp;b_{12}&amp;0\\
b_{21}&amp;b_{22}&amp;0\\
b_{31}&amp;b_{32}&amp;1\end{array}\right]\right)\mapsto\left[\begin{array}[]{ccccc}a_{11}&amp;a_{12}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
a_{21}&amp;a_{22}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;b_{11}&amp;b_{12}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;b_{21}&amp;b_{22}&amp;0\\
a_{31}&amp;a_{32}&amp;b_{31}&amp;b_{32}&amp;1\end{array}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>22</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>22</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>22</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>22</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>31</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>32</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}a_{11}&amp;a_{12}&amp;0\\
a_{21}&amp;a_{22}&amp;0\\
a_{31}&amp;a_{32}&amp;1\end{array}\right],\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}b_{11}&amp;b_{12}&amp;0\\
b_{21}&amp;b_{22}&amp;0\\
b_{31}&amp;b_{32}&amp;1\end{array}\right]\right)\mapsto\left[\begin{array}[]{ccccc}a_{11}&amp;a_{12}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
a_{21}&amp;a_{22}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;b_{11}&amp;b_{12}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;b_{21}&amp;b_{22}&amp;0\\
a_{31}&amp;a_{32}&amp;b_{31}&amp;b_{32}&amp;1\end{array}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We set up the following notations for later purposes. Denote</p>
<table id="S14.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{d}:={\mathcal{G}}_{d}/G_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{d}:={\mathcal{G}}_{d}/G_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The tangent space at the identity coset is the quotient of Lie algebras</p>
<table id="S14.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d}:={\mathfrak{g}}_{d}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d}:={\mathfrak{g}}_{d}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">There are canonical <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant metrics on <math id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> making the linear embeddings</p>
<table id="S14.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d_{1}}\oplus Q_{d_{2}}\to Q_{d_{1}+d_{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d_{1}}\oplus Q_{d_{2}}\to Q_{d_{1}+d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">isometric. Denote</p>
<table id="S14.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}:=Q_{d_{1}+d_{2}}/(Q_{d_{1}}\oplus Q_{d_{2}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}:=Q_{d_{1}+d_{2}}/(Q_{d_{1}}\oplus Q_{d_{2}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.3.2. </span>Moduli spaces of cylinders in projective spaces</h5>

<div id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we will describe an object <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{d}=({\mathcal{G}}_{d},B_{d},C_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{d}=({\mathcal{G}}_{d},B_{d},C_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the moduli space of holomorphic maps</p>
<table id="S14.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to\mathbb{P}^{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to\mathbb{P}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">of degree <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, modulo the translation in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>-direction (but not the <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-rotation). Let</p>
<table id="S14.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{P}^{d},d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{P}^{d},d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">be the natural compactification of this moduli space (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Definition 5.14]</cite> for an explanation of this notation). Then the group <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PU(d+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PU(d+1)</annotation></semantics></math> acts on <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{P}^{d},d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{P}^{d},d)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="S14.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{{\mathbb{R}},+}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)\subseteq\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{{\mathbb{R}},+}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)\subseteq\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">be the subset satisfying the constraint:</p>
<table id="S14.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(z_{+})=[0,\ldots,0,1]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(z_{+})=[0,\ldots,0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which is invariant under <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}=U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}=U(d)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{+}=\{\infty\}\in\mathbb{P}^{1}\supseteq{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{+}=\{\infty\}\in\mathbb{P}^{1}\supseteq{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="S14.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{d}\subseteq\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{{\mathbb{R}},+}(\mathbb{P}^{d},d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}\subseteq\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{{\mathbb{R}},+}(\mathbb{P}^{d},d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">be the open subset of curves <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> whose image is not contained in any hyperplane of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is easy to calculate the dimension of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is</p>
<table id="S14.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm dim}_{\mathbb{R}}B_{d}=2d(d+1)-1={\rm dim}_{\mathbb{R}}{\mathcal{G}}_{d}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>dim</mi><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>dim</mi><mi>ℝ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm dim}_{\mathbb{R}}B_{d}=2d(d+1)-1={\rm dim}_{\mathbb{R}}{\mathcal{G}}_{d}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Further, let <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{d}\to B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{d}\to B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the universal curve; notice that fibers also carry canonical germs of cylindrical ends.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The moduli space <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is stratified by the poset <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. the notations introduced in Section <a href="#S14.SS1.SSS1" title="14.1.1. Monotone flow category ‣ 14.1. Monotone flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.1.1</span></a>): for any <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau=(d_{0}\cdots d_{r})\in A_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(d_{0}\cdots d_{r})\in A_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the stratum <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\tau}B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mi>τ</mi></msup><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\tau}B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subspace of curves in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> which breaks into <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+1</annotation></semantics></math> stable cylinders such that the <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th one has degree <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, one obtains an object</p>
<table id="S14.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{d}=({\mathcal{G}}_{d},B_{d},C_{d})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{d}=({\mathcal{G}}_{d},B_{d},C_{d})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">in the category <math id="S14.SS3.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 14.14</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.Thmthm14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a refinement of the above stratification, namely, the stratification by combinatorial types, and each stratum is preserved by the <math id="S14.Thmthm14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>-action.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.3.3. </span>Orientations</h5>

<div id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The smooth part of the moduli space <math id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,2}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,2}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)</annotation></semantics></math> is a complex manifold, which is canonically oriented. The interior of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> has a natural <math id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-action by reparametrizing the cylinders so that the quotient <math id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Int}B_{d}/S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Int}B_{d}/S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is identified with an open subset of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,2}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{0,2}({\mathbb{P}}^{d},d)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence we can orient <math id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by regarding the infinitesimal <math id="S14.SS3.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-direction as positively oriented.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.3.4. </span>Concatenation of cylinders</h5>

<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to define the structural maps, i.e., morphisms</p>
<table id="S14.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}:{\mathcal{C}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}},\ d,d^{\prime}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}:{\mathcal{C}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}},\ d,d^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">in the category <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that they satisfy associativity. In this way, one obtains a monotone flow category enriched in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We describe the definition as follows. Given two points <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}\in B_{d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}\in B_{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> represented by maps <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\Sigma\to{\mathbb{P}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\Sigma\to{\mathbb{P}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}:\Sigma^{\prime}\to{\mathbb{P}}^{d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}:\Sigma^{\prime}\to{\mathbb{P}}^{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the prestable cylinder obtained by identifying the output of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> with the input <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. The map <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented by sections</p>
<table id="S14.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},\ldots,h_{d}\in H^{0}(\Sigma,u^{*}{\mathcal{O}}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{d}}(1))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},\ldots,h_{d}\in H^{0}(\Sigma,u^{*}{\mathcal{O}}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{d}}(1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We abbreviate <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{u}:=u^{*}{\mathcal{O}}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{d}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{u}:=u^{*}{\mathcal{O}}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{d}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and extend it by trivial bundle to <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0},\ldots,h_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0},\ldots,h_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are sections over <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, the map <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented by sections <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}^{\prime},\ldots,h_{d^{\prime}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}^{\prime},\ldots,h_{d^{\prime}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of the pullback bundle <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{u^{\prime}}\to\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{u^{\prime}}\to\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> which can be extended to the whole of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}\in B_{d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}\in B_{d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we choose the lateral line, a (broken) real curve</p>
<table id="S14.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\phi^{\prime}}\subseteq C_{\phi^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\phi^{\prime}}\subseteq C_{\phi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which is parametrized by <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,0)</annotation></semantics></math> in the cylindrical coordinates in all cylindrical components. Along <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\phi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\phi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the parallel transport with respect to the Chern connection on <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{u^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{u^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> sends the (nonzero) vector <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{d^{\prime}}(z_{+})\in L_{u^{\prime}}|_{z_{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{d^{\prime}}(z_{+})\in L_{u^{\prime}}|_{z_{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> to a nonzero vector <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{u^{\prime}}\in L_{u^{\prime}}|_{z_{-}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{u^{\prime}}\in L_{u^{\prime}}|_{z_{-}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then consider <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+d+d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+d+d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> sections of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{u}\otimes L_{u^{\prime}}\to\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{u}\otimes L_{u^{\prime}}\to\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> given by</p>
<table id="S14.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}\otimes\tau_{u^{\prime}},\ldots,h_{d-1}\otimes\tau_{u^{\prime}},h_{d}\otimes h_{0}^{\prime},\ldots,h_{d}\otimes h_{d^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}\otimes\tau_{u^{\prime}},\ldots,h_{d-1}\otimes\tau_{u^{\prime}},h_{d}\otimes h_{0}^{\prime},\ldots,h_{d}\otimes h_{d^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">It is easy to check that it is base-point-free, hence defines a map</p>
<table id="S14.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi\#\phi^{\prime}):\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}\to\mathbb{P}^{d+d^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi\#\phi^{\prime}):\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}\to\mathbb{P}^{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">which represents a point in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, it is straightforward to see that the equivalence class of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\#u^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\#u^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of the choice of the representatives <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, one obtains a well-defined map</p>
<table id="S14.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}:B_{d}\times B_{d^{\prime}}\to B_{d+d^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}:B_{d}\times B_{d^{\prime}}\to B_{d+d^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 14.15</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm15.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The map <math id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}:B_{d}\times B_{d^{\prime}}\to B_{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}:B_{d}\times B_{d^{\prime}}\to B_{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and equivariant with respect to the group embedding</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{G}}:{\mathcal{G}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{d+d^{\prime}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{\mathcal{G}}:{\mathcal{G}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{d+d^{\prime}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and satisfying the associativity, i.e., the following diagram commutes.</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S14.Ex57.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="64.50" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-54.425505726139825px" version="1.1" viewBox="52.55 54.43 226.19 64.50" width="226.19"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 52.55116818603414 64.49575755413727) translate(0,3.54) translate(52.55,0)"><g transform="translate(-52.55,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="96.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex57.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}\times B_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}\times B_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 52.55118929962078 -0.27673578005007266 L 52.55118929962078 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(85.76,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 52.55118929962078 -0.27673578005007266 L 85.75996851812215 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 85.75996851812215 -0.27673578005007266 L 85.75996851812215 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -11.14645356605438 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(85.76,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="79.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex57.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{B_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times B_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{B_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times B_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 129.42235895718747 -11.14645356605438 L 129.9758305172876 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(129.7,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 129.42235895718747 -33.208800332088 L 129.9758305172876 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 129.42235895718747 -33.208800332088 L 129.9758305172876 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-43.94,0) translate(0,-43.28) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="79.58"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex57.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}+d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}+d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 43.93912621911538 -43.55578794013552 L 43.93912621911538 -43.002316380035374" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(94.37,0) translate(0,-43.28)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 43.93912621911538 -43.55578794013552 L 94.37203159862754 -43.002316380035374" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 94.37203159862754 -43.55578794013552 L 94.37203159862754 -43.002316380035374" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(94.37,0) translate(0,-43.28) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.51em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="62.35"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex57.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{B_{d_{1}+d_{2}+d_{3}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{B_{d_{1}+d_{2}+d_{3}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore, the maps <math id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> can be lifted canonically to a strict morphism</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}:{\mathcal{C}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}:{\mathcal{C}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d^{\prime}}\to{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in the category <math id="S14.Thmthm15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following diagram commutes.</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S14.Ex59.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="64.50" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-54.425505726139825px" version="1.1" viewBox="47.68 54.43 210.98 64.50" width="210.98"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 47.681889495068404 64.49575755413727) translate(0,3.54) translate(47.68,0)"><g transform="translate(-47.68,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.29em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="87.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex59.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 47.681889495068404 -0.27673578005007266 L 47.681889495068404 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(80.89,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 47.681889495068404 -0.27673578005007266 L 80.89068982715641 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 80.89068982715641 -0.27673578005007266 L 80.89068982715641 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -11.14645356605438 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(80.89,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="74.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex59.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 121.8193564092336 -11.14645356605438 L 122.37282796933376 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(122.1,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 121.8193564092336 -33.208800332088 L 122.37282796933376 -11.14645356605438" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 121.8193564092336 -33.208800332088 L 122.37282796933376 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-41.21,0) translate(0,-43.28) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="74.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex59.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}+d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}+d_{3}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 41.205402362127266 -43.55578794013552 L 41.205402362127266 -43.002316380035374" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(87.37,0) translate(0,-43.28)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 41.205402362127266 -43.55578794013552 L 87.36717696009755 -43.002316380035374" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 87.36717696009755 -43.55578794013552 L 87.36717696009755 -43.002316380035374" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(87.37,0) translate(0,-43.28) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="61.16"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex59.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}+d_{3}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}+d_{3}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">All elements in the definition depend smoothly on the variables <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the explicit definition of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\#u^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\#u^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> given above, the equivariance follows immediately. The associativity can also be checked directly. See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, §5.2.4]</cite> for more details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We need to prove that the morphisms are strict embeddings into the corresponding stratum.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 14.16</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.Thmthm16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The morphism <math id="S14.Thmthm16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a strict embedding into the stratum <math id="S14.Thmthm16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{d,d^{\prime}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{d,d^{\prime}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">What we need to show is that the induced strict morphism</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d+d^{\prime}}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d^{\prime}}}\left({\mathcal{C}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d^{\prime}}\right)\to\partial^{d,d^{\prime}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d+d^{\prime}}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d^{\prime}}}\left({\mathcal{C}}_{d}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d^{\prime}}\right)\to\partial^{d,d^{\prime}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">is an isomorphism. Indeed, given any curve in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{d,d^{\prime}}B_{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{d,d^{\prime}}B_{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is represented by a holomorphic map <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}\to\mathbb{P}^{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\Sigma\#\Sigma^{\prime}\to\mathbb{P}^{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the restriction of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has degree <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. After applying a transformation in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can make <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> be contained in the special <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{d}\subseteq{\mathbb{P}}^{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{d}\subseteq{\mathbb{P}}^{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> with last <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates vanish, and make <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\Sigma^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\Sigma^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> be contained in a <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{d^{\prime}}\subseteq{\mathbb{P}}^{d+d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{d^{\prime}}\subseteq{\mathbb{P}}^{d+d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> which is spanned by the last <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates as well as a line contained in the special <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such curves are exactly in the image of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS4.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S14.SS3.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">14.3.5. </span>Rigidification</h5>

<div id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lastly we construct the rigidifications (see Definition <a href="#S14.Thmthm9" title="Definition 14.9. ‣ 14.2.2. Rigidifications ‣ 14.2. The category of curves ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 14.17</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S14.Thmthm17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The monotone flow category <math id="S14.Thmthm17.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}</annotation></semantics></math> by taking the outer-collaring of the monotone flow category which has objects <math id="S14.Thmthm17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and morphisms <math id="S14.Thmthm17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d,d^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a lift to <math id="S14.Thmthm17.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first explain why a single embedding <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d_{1},d_{2}}:{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}}\to\partial^{d_{1},d_{2}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d_{1},d_{2}}:{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}}\to\partial^{d_{1},d_{2}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be rigidified (before outer-collaring). (See Definition <a href="#S14.Thmthm9" title="Definition 14.9. ‣ 14.2.2. Rigidifications ‣ 14.2. The category of curves ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.9</span></a>) the representation of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}=G_{d_{1}}\times G_{d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}=G_{d_{1}}\times G_{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> given by (<a href="#S14.E3" title="In 14.3.1. Some Lie groups and homogeneous spaces ‣ 14.3. Construction of the domain flow categories ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.3</span></a>). Roughly, <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normal direction to <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}({\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}({\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To be more specific, one can choose a <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant germ of maps</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}:Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}:Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">sending <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to the identity (such as the restriction of an exponential map) which is orthogonal to <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}({\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}({\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of embeddings in <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is an isomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{2}}}({\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}})\to\partial^{d_{1},d_{2}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times_{{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{2}}}({\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}}\times{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{2}})\to\partial^{d_{1},d_{2}}{\mathcal{C}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then the map</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}\times(B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}})&amp;\ \to\partial^{d_{1},d_{2}}B_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\\
(v,x_{1},x_{2})&amp;\ \mapsto\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}(v)(\zeta_{d_{1},d_{2}}^{B}(x_{1},x_{2}))\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}\times(B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}})&amp;\ \to\partial^{d_{1},d_{2}}B_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\\
(v,x_{1},x_{2})&amp;\ \mapsto\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}(v)(\zeta_{d_{1},d_{2}}^{B}(x_{1},x_{2}))\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">is a local diffeomorphism after equivariantize by <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d_{1}+d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We need to choose rigidifications for all such embeddings so that they satisfy the requirement for flow categories. For this one can allow <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> to depend on <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{1},x_{2})\in B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{1},x_{2})\in B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{d_{1},d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a germ of equivariant bundle maps</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}\times B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d_{1},d_{2}}\times B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{d_{1}+d_{2}}\times B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">over <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{d_{1}}\times B_{d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. All such rigidifications of the embedding <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{d_{1},d_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{d_{1},d_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are equivariantly homotopic. The collaring region allows us to connect different choices.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We choose such a lift of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> and still denote it by <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}</annotation></semantics></math>. The effect of such a lift to later constructions needs to be addressed in the following way. Roughly, the resulting Kuranishi spaces of the AMS construction have symmetry groups being compact Lie groups <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> while the domains we constructed here have symmetry groups being corresponding complex Lie groups <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This redundance will be removed by using a notion called <span id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">group reduction</span> (see Definition <a href="#S15.Thmthm7" title="Definition 15.7 (The category of families of reduced framed maps). ‣ 15.2.2. Group reductions ‣ 15.2. Framed maps ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.7</span></a>), which later becomes part of the Kuranishi section.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a strict embedding</p>
<table id="S14.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}:{\mathcal{C}}_{1}=({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}=({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}:{\mathcal{C}}_{1}=({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to{\mathcal{C}}_{2}=({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p">of equivariant families of curves. Denote by</p>
<table id="S14.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{P}:P_{1}={\mathcal{G}}_{1}/G_{1}\to P_{2}={\mathcal{G}}_{2}/G_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{P}:P_{1}={\mathcal{G}}_{1}/G_{1}\to P_{2}={\mathcal{G}}_{2}/G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p6.3" class="ltx_p">the induced embedding of homogeneous spaces and</p>
<table id="S14.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{Q}:Q_{1}={\mathfrak{g}}_{1}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{1}\to Q_{2}={\mathfrak{g}}_{2}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔤</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔤</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{Q}:Q_{1}={\mathfrak{g}}_{1}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{1}\to Q_{2}={\mathfrak{g}}_{2}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p6.4" class="ltx_p">the linearization of <math id="S14.SS3.SSS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>P</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S14.Thmthm18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S14.Thmthm18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 14.18</span></span><span id="S14.Thmthm18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S14.Thmthm18.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}</annotation></semantics></math> be the monotone flow category enriched in <math id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> we constructed above. There exist a collection of germs of <math id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}\times G_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}\times G_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant maps</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S14.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{d}:{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times Q_{d}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times P_{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{d}:{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times Q_{d}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times P_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">as bundle maps over <math id="S14.Thmthm18.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following conditions.</span></p>
<ol id="S14.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S14.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S14.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="S14.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\phi\in{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S14.I7.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the restriction of </span><math id="S14.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S14.I7.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S14.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi\}\times Q_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi\}\times Q_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S14.I7.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a local diffeomorphism onto an open neighborhood of </span><math id="S14.I7.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1]\in P_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1]\in P_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S14.I7.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S14.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S14.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S14.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is collared, i.e., </span><math id="S14.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S14.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is determined over the collar neighborhood by its restriction to the boundary strata via the projections.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S14.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S14.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S14.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S14.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each decomposition </span><math id="S14.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{1}+d_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{1}+d_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S14.I7.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the following diagram commutes.</span></p>
<table id="S14.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S14.Ex69.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="83.07" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-64.49653875684282px" version="1.1" viewBox="88.69 64.50 429.21 83.07" width="429.21"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 88.68945755040775 83.06880965179406) translate(0,3.54) translate(88.69,0)"><g transform="translate(-88.69,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.22em;--ltx-fo-height:0.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.66em;font-size:10pt;" height="21.52" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 12.45)" width="169.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex69.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\big({}_{\lfloor}B_{d_{1}}\times Q_{d_{1}}\big)\times\big({}_{\lfloor}B_{d_{2}}\times Q_{d_{2}}\big)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\big({}_{\lfloor}B_{d_{1}}\times Q_{d_{1}}\big)\times\big({}_{\lfloor}B_{d_{2}}\times Q_{d_{2}}\big)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 88.68945755040775 -0.27673578005007266 L 88.68945755040775 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(99.8,0) translate(0,9.29) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.26em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.27" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="44.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S14.Ex69.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lambda_{d_{1}}\times\lambda_{d_{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">λ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">λ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.710em">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lambda_{d_{1}}\times\lambda_{d_{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(163.41,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 88.68945755040775 -0.27673578005007266 L 163.40925829760576 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 163.40925829760576 -0.27673578005007266 L 163.40925829760576 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -16.758128190347396 L 0.27673578005007266 -16.758128190347396" fil