gnorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 74.95215pt\raise-16.06139pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.2222pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\Lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 74.95215pt\raise-24.78947pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-24.2566pt\raise-32.12279pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{P_{pr}\times P_{rq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 33.59668pt\raise-39.32613pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.23114pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\zeta_{prq}^{P}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 63.77829pt\raise-32.12279pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 63.77829pt\raise-32.12279pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{P_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">The compatibility assumption and the <math id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariance imply that one obtains a group reduction on the boundary of <math id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> which is collared. We also have a group reduction in <math id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> (viewed as a subset away from boundary) given by (<a href="#S15.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 15.2.6. Group reductions ‣ 15.2. Framed maps ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.6</span></a>). Then using the product structure on the collar region (where the actions by the complex Lie groups fix the collar coordinates) and choosing a homotopy, one can interpolate over the collar region to get a continuous group reduction on the whole of <math id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS2.SSS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The constructions for the cases of multimodules and homotopies are completely the same and we omit the details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS2.SSS7" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.2.7. </span>Linearizing the group reduction</h5>

<div id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to regard the group reduction as a section of a vector bundle rather than a nonlinear fiber bundle. This requires linearizing the homogeneous space <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}/G</annotation></semantics></math>, which has a contractible set of choices.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that we have constructed a collection of germs of maps</p>
<table id="S15.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{d}:{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times Q_{d}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times P_{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{d}:{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times Q_{d}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{d}\times P_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By abuse of notation, let <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d}^{\epsilon}\subseteq Q_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d}^{\epsilon}\subseteq Q_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant disk bundle over which <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined and <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{d}^{\epsilon}\subseteq P_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{d}^{\epsilon}\subseteq P_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> the image of <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{d}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{d}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote</p>
<table id="S15.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{pq}:{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times Q_{pq}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times P_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{pq}:{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times Q_{pq}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times P_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.3" class="ltx_p">the pullback of <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then define</p>
<table id="S15.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{{\mathbb{F}},\epsilon}:=(\Lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}})^{-1}(P_{pq}^{\epsilon})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{{\mathbb{F}},\epsilon}:=(\Lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}})^{-1}(P_{pq}^{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and define the composition</p>
<table id="S15.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{pq}:=\left(\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 15.11443pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-15.11443pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F},\epsilon}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 17.54204pt\raise 7.19441pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.2222pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\Lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 39.11443pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 39.11443pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{P_{pq}^{\epsilon}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 64.27847pt\raise 7.10612pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.13391pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\lambda_{pq}^{-1}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 85.46214pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 85.46214pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Q_{pq}^{\epsilon}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 131.90636pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 131.90636pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Q_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-16.681274734989017px" height="36.59" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="20.91 16.68 234.49 36.59" width="234.49"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 20.913830993745243 36.59109134338894) translate(0,3.46) translate(20.91,0)"> <g transform="translate(-20.91,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.66em;font-size:10pt;" height="20.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.64)" width="33.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 20.91385210733188 -0.27673578005007266 L 20.91385210733188 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(24.27,0) translate(0,9.96) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.07)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.31em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.88)" width="18.19"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">q</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">𝔽</mi></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(54.12,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 20.91385210733188 -0.27673578005007266 L 54.12263132583325 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 54.12263132583325 -0.27673578005007266 L 54.12263132583325 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(54.12,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="22.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 85.04516804252931 -0.27673578005007266 L 85.04516804252931 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(88.94,0) translate(0,9.83) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-2.95)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.62em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.63)" width="17.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">λ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(118.26,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 85.04516804252931 -0.27673578005007266 L 118.25396837461732 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 118.25396837461732 -0.27673578005007266 L 118.25396837461732 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(118.26,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.64em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="22.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 149.3100485267919 -0.27673578005007266 L 149.3100485267919 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(182.52,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 149.3100485267919 -0.27673578005007266 L 182.51882774529327 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 182.51882774529327 -0.27673578005007266 L 182.51882774529327 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(182.52,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.64em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="22.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{pq}:=\left(\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 15.11443pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-15.11443pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{{}_{\lfloor}Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F},\epsilon}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 17.54204pt\raise 7.19441pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.2222pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\Lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 39.11443pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 39.11443pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{P_{pq}^{\epsilon}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 64.27847pt\raise 7.10612pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.13391pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\lambda_{pq}^{-1}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 85.46214pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 85.46214pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Q_{pq}^{\epsilon}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 131.90636pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 131.90636pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Q_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Viewing this as a section of a certain trivial vector bundle, this map will become part of the Kuranishi sections. We call such a section <math id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> a <span id="S15.SS2.SSS7.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">linearized group reduction</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">15.3. </span>The topological Kuranishi lifts</h4>

<section id="S15.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.3.1. </span>Thickening data</h5>

<div id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given an equivariant family <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> and an almost complex manifold <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,J)</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{C}\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{C}\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math> is the complement of nodes and markings. Consider the vector bundle</p>
<table id="S15.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{0,1}_{\mathring{C}/B}\otimes TX\to\mathring{C}\times X." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{0,1}_{\mathring{C}/B}\otimes TX\to\mathring{C}\times X.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.10</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">thickening datum</span> on an equivariant family of curves <math id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}=({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a pair <math id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite-dimensional complex unitary representation<span id="footnote22" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">22</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">22</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">22</span>
                    
                    
                    
                  We restrict to complex representation in order to simplify the discussion of normal complex structures.</span></span></span> of the maximal compact subgroup <math id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S15.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu:W\to\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}\times X,\Lambda^{0,1}_{\mathring{C}/B}\otimes TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu:W\to\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}\times X,\Lambda^{0,1}_{\mathring{C}/B}\otimes TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is a <math id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant linear map. Here <math id="S15.Thmthm10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> stands for smooth sections with compact support.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that given a thickening datum <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for each <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in B</annotation></semantics></math> and a smooth map <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:C_{\phi}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:C_{\phi}\to X</annotation></semantics></math>, there is an induced linear map</p>
<table id="S15.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\phi,u}:W\to\Omega^{0,1}_{c}(\mathring{C}_{\phi},u^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\phi,u}:W\to\Omega^{0,1}_{c}(\mathring{C}_{\phi},u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">given by restricting <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(e)</annotation></semantics></math> to the graph of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{C}_{\phi}\times X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{C}_{\phi}\times X</annotation></semantics></math>. These maps will be used to thicken up the moduli space of Floer equation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.11</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">category of curves-with-thickening data</span>, denoted by <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as follows. The objects are tuples</p>
<table id="S15.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}},B,C,W,\nu)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}},B,C,W,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> is an equivariant family of curves and <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> is a thickening datum on <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm11.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict embedding of perturbations</span> consists of a strict embedding</p>
<table id="S15.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}=(\zeta_{21}^{\mathcal{G}},\zeta_{21}^{B},\zeta_{21}^{C}):({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}=(\zeta_{21}^{\mathcal{G}},\zeta_{21}^{B},\zeta_{21}^{C}):({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.2" class="ltx_p">(see Definition <a href="#S14.Thmthm7" title="Definition 14.7. ‣ 14.2. The category of curves ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.7</span></a>) and a <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant isometric linear embedding <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}^{W}:W_{1}\to W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}^{W}:W_{1}\to W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that 1) the following diagram commutes;</p>
<table id="S15.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="74.32" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-60.461563441834876px" version="1.1" viewBox="24.08 60.46 235.96 74.32" width="235.96"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 24.0804044903768 74.31777694404447) translate(0,3.46) translate(24.08,0)"><g transform="translate(-14.75,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="21.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 14.749888283790387 -0.27673578005007266 L 14.749888283790387 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(21.73,0) translate(0,6.93) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\nu_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\nu_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(47.96,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 14.749888283790387 -0.27673578005007266 L 47.95866750229175 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 47.95866750229175 -0.27673578005007266 L 47.95866750229175 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-24.08,0) translate(0,-22.58) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.14em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="10.79" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.9)" width="15.78"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\zeta_{21}^{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ζ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">21</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">W</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\zeta_{21}^{W}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(0,-35.02)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -35.01688343732704 L 0.27673578005007266 -9.685900096859001" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -35.01688343732704 L 0.27673578005007266 -35.01688343732704" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(47.96,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.25em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.56em;font-size:10pt;" height="18.95" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="155.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{1}\times X,\Lambda_{\mathring{C}_{1}/B_{1}}^{0,1}\otimes TX)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{1}\times X,\Lambda_{\mathring{C}_{1}/B_{1}}^{0,1}\otimes TX)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 129.6434815500359 -15.297574721152017 L 130.19695311013604 -15.297574721152017" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(129.92,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 129.6434815500359 -33.20877921850137 L 130.19695311013604 -15.297574721152017" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 129.6434815500359 -33.20877921850137 L 130.19695311013604 -33.20877921850137" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-14.75,0) translate(0,-45.16) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.53em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="21.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{2}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 14.749888283790387 -45.44072450073293 L 14.749888283790387 -44.887252940632784" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(21.73,0) translate(0,-52.09) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-1.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.79em;--ltx-fo-height:0.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.1em;font-size:10pt;" height="5.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.17)" width="10.95"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\nu_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\nu_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(47.96,0) translate(0,-45.16)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 14.749888283790387 -45.44072450073293 L 47.95866750229175 -44.887252940632784" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 47.95866750229175 -45.44072450073293 L 47.95866750229175 -44.887252940632784" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(47.96,0) translate(0,-45.16) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.25em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.56em;font-size:10pt;" height="18.95" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="155.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex67.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{2}\times X,\Lambda_{\mathring{C}_{2}/B_{2}}^{0,1}\otimes TX)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{2}\times X,\Lambda_{\mathring{C}_{2}/B_{2}}^{0,1}\otimes TX)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.3" class="ltx_p">(here the right vertical arrow is induced from the morphism <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math>) and 2) the restriction of <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to the orthogonal complement <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}^{\bot}\subseteq W_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊥</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}^{\bot}\subseteq W_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm11.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm11.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The conjugation of <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}},B,C,W,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}},B,C,W,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> is a strict embedding induced by <math id="S15.Thmthm11.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G</annotation></semantics></math>. An <span id="S15.Thmthm11.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">embedding</span> of curvs-with-thickening-datum is a conjugacy class of strict embeddings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The category <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a regular stratification category with a forgetful functor <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Curv}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Curv}}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can easily formulate the category <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}</annotation></semantics></math> of collared curves-with-thickening-datum, together with forgetful functor</p>
<table id="S15.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We need to consider the rigidified version. Recall that for a strict embedding</p>
<table id="S15.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}:({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1})\to({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">a rigidification is a germ of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant map <math id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying an appropriate condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.12</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\zeta_{21},\zeta_{21}^{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\zeta_{21},\zeta_{21}^{W})</annotation></semantics></math> be a strict embedding in <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1},W_{1},\nu_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{1},B_{1},C_{1},W_{1},\nu_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2},W_{2},\nu_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{2},B_{2},C_{2},W_{2},\nu_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidification</span> of <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\zeta_{21},\zeta_{21}^{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>W</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\zeta_{21},\zeta_{21}^{W})</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a rigidification <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{21}:B_{1}\times Q_{21}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following condition. Fix <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}\in B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}\in B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The rigidification induces identifications</p>
<table id="S15.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\zeta_{21}^{B}(b_{1})}\cong C_{\theta_{21}(b_{1},q)(\zeta_{21}^{B}(b_{1}))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\zeta_{21}^{B}(b_{1})}\cong C_{\theta_{21}(b_{1},q)(\zeta_{21}^{B}(b_{1}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in Q_{21}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>21</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in Q_{21}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficient close to the origin. Then we can regard <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as a family of linear maps</p>
<table id="S15.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}(b_{1},q):W_{2}\to\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{\zeta_{21}(b_{1})}\times X,\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}(b_{1},q):W_{2}\to\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{\zeta_{21}(b_{1})}\times X,\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We require that these family only depends on <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, for <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> close to the origin, <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes on the orthogonal complement of <math id="S15.Thmthm12.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.13</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">thickening datum</span> on a flow category/multimodule/homotopy enriched in <math id="S15.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lift in <math id="S15.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If the flow category/multimodule/homotopy is enriched in <math id="S15.Thmthm13.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>, then a perturbation is called <span id="S15.Thmthm13.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared and rigidified</span> if it is a lift in <math id="S15.Thmthm13.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the following steps, one needs to choose perturbations satisfying additional properties. The construction of such perturbations will be provided in due course.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now we can describe the AMS lift of the Floer flow categories, bimodules, and homotopies to the category of topological Kuranishi spaces.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.3.2. </span>The thickenings</h5>

<div id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We describe the thickened moduli spaces as candidates of the Kuranishi regularizations of the moduli spaces. We first consider the flow category case. Return to the domain flow category <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> whose morphism spaces are equivariant families of curves <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{C}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{C}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A thickening datum of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> which consists of thickening data</p>
<table id="S15.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}:W_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times X,\Lambda_{\mathring{C}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}/B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}}^{0,1}\otimes TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}:W_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to\Gamma_{c}(\mathring{C}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\times X,\Lambda_{\mathring{C}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}/B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}}^{0,1}\otimes TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.14</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given any collared and rigidified thickening datum <math id="S15.Thmthm14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the flow category <math id="S15.Thmthm14.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the flow category <math id="S15.Thmthm14.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}}^{\mathbb{fr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}}^{\mathbb{fr}}</annotation></semantics></math> of reduced framed maps, for each pair <math id="S15.Thmthm14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> of objects in the Floer flow category <math id="S15.Thmthm14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the following items.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm14.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S15.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">thickened moduli space</span> is</p>
<table id="S15.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{pq}:=V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}:=\left\{(\phi,u,F,e)\ \left|\ \begin{array}[]{c}(\phi,u,F)\in Y_{pq}^{{\mathbb{F}},\epsilon},\ e\in W_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}},\\
\overline{\partial}_{H}u+\nu_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(e)=0,\ \phi=\phi_{F}\in{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}.\end{array}\right.\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em">|</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∂</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msub><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}:=V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}:=\left\{(\phi,u,F,e)\ \left|\ \begin{array}[]{c}(\phi,u,F)\in Y_{pq}^{{\mathbb{F}},\epsilon},\ e\in W_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}},\\
\overline{\partial}_{H}u+\nu_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(e)=0,\ \phi=\phi_{F}\in{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}.\end{array}\right.\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="S15.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S15.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is the product of the diagonal <math id="S15.I10.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S15.I10.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F},\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F},\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> space of framed maps and the action on <math id="S15.I10.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.I10.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">obstruction bundle</span> is the trivial bundle</p>
<table id="S15.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}:=E_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}:=\underline{\smash{Q}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to V_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}:=E_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}:=\underline{\smash{Q}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to V_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I10.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S15.I10.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I10.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.I10.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kuranishi section</span> is (given by) the equivariant map</p>
<table id="S15.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi,u,F,e)=(\lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi,u,F),e)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi,u,F,e)=(\lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi,u,F),e).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 15.15</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm15.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.Thmthm15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The natural “footprint” map</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(S_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}})^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}})^{-1}(0)/G_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\to{}_{\lfloor}\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm15.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.Thmthm15.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which sends the orbit of <math id="S15.Thmthm15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi,u,F,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi,u,F,0)</annotation></semantics></math> to the equivalence class of the stable Floer trajectory <math id="S15.Thmthm15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:C_{\phi}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:C_{\phi}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism of orbispaces.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We drop <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the notations for simplification. We also assume <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We prove that the footprint map is surjective. Given any point of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> represented by a stable Floer trajectory <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:\Sigma\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:\Sigma\to X</annotation></semantics></math> (assume that this point is not in the outer collar; the case that it is in the outer collar can be deduced similarly). Then <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> determines a unitary line bundle <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{u}\to\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{u}\to\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> whose Chern connection has curvature <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> be a frame of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the negative (or positive) constraint, which determines a holomorphic map <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{F}:\Sigma\to{\mathbb{P}}^{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{F}:\Sigma\to{\mathbb{P}}^{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence can be identified with a point <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{F}\in B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{F}\in B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. The domain <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> can be then identified with <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\phi_{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\phi_{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{F}:\mathring{C}_{\phi_{F}}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{F}:\mathring{C}_{\phi_{F}}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> be the pullback map. As two different frames <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> differ by an element of the group <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{pq,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{pq,R}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains a <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-orbit (where we regard <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> as the diagonal of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{pq,L}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{pq,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{pq,L}\times{\mathcal{G}}_{pq,R}</annotation></semantics></math>) of framed maps</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)\in Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)\in Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of a structural group reduction scheme, there is a unique <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-orbit (for the diagonal action) of framed maps such that</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)=[1]\in P_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)=[1]\in P_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)\in Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F},\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)\in Y_{pq}^{\mathbb{F},\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(\phi_{F},u_{F},F)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. This <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-orbit is then sent by the footprint map to the given point of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore the footprint map is surjective.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove that the footprint map is injective. Suppose <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi,u,F,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi,u,F,0)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi^{\prime},u^{\prime},F^{\prime},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi^{\prime},u^{\prime},F^{\prime},0)</annotation></semantics></math> are sent to the same point of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition, there is a domain isomorphism <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\phi}\cong C_{\phi^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\phi}\cong C_{\phi^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which must be given by an element <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=\phi_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=\phi_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}=\phi_{F^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}=\phi_{F^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\phi,u,F,0)=(\phi^{\prime},u^{\prime},F^{\prime},0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\phi,u,F,0)=(\phi^{\prime},u^{\prime},F^{\prime},0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">As in the same <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-orbit there can only be one normalized <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-oribt, it follows that <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that the footprint map is injective.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now we turn to the case of multimodules <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}:=\mathbb{X}^{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>𝕏</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}:=\mathbb{X}^{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a connected Floer domain <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Previously one has constructed a multimodule <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{Dom}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{Dom}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with the group reductions</p>
<table id="S15.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:{}_{\lfloor}Y_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}/G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:{}_{\lfloor}Y_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}\to{\mathcal{G}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}/G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which extends the group reductions on the involved flow categories of framed maps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.16</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm16.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm16.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a thickening datum <math id="S15.Thmthm16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> on the multimodule <math id="S15.Thmthm16.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> (as a multimodule over the flow categories equipped with thickening data, enriched in <math id="S15.Thmthm16.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>), for objects <math id="S15.Thmthm16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the following objects.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm16.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S15.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.I11.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">thickened moduli space</span> is</p>
<table id="S15.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}:=V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:=\left\{(\phi,u,F,e)\ \left|\begin{array}[]{l}(\phi,u,F)\in{}_{\lfloor}Y_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}},\epsilon},\ e\in W_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},\\
\overline{\partial}_{\sigma}u+\nu_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}(e)=0,\ \phi=\phi_{F}\in{}_{\lfloor}B_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.\end{array}\right.\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>∂</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>σ</mi></msub><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}:=V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:=\left\{(\phi,u,F,e)\ \left|\begin{array}[]{l}(\phi,u,F)\in{}_{\lfloor}Y_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{X}},\epsilon},\ e\in W_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},\\
\overline{\partial}_{\sigma}u+\nu_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}(e)=0,\ \phi=\phi_{F}\in{}_{\lfloor}B_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.\end{array}\right.\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="S15.I11.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>-action on <math id="S15.I11.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of the diagonal action on <math id="S15.I11.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}Y_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X},\epsilon}\times W_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}Y_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X},\epsilon}\times W_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I11.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I11.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I11.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.I11.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">obstruction bundle</span> is the trivial bundle</p>
<table id="S15.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}:=E_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:=\underline{\smash{Q}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}:=E_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:=\underline{\smash{Q}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I11.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S15.I11.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I11.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.I11.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kuranishi section</span> is (equivalent to) the map</p>
<table id="S15.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}(\phi,u,F,e)\mapsto(\lambda_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}(\phi,u,F),e)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}(\phi,u,F,e)\mapsto(\lambda_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}(\phi,u,F),e)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.I11.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S15.I11.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the linearized group reduction.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The case of homotopies is the same. We omit the detailed discussions. We will use <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to indicate the relationship with a multimodule homotopy <math id="S15.SS3.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> coming from the Floer theory background.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.3.3. </span>Transversality</h5>

<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next we deal with transversality. For this we need to set up a certain Fredholm problem. For each pair of objects <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S15.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}:=\Big\{(\phi,u,e)|\ \phi\in{}_{\lfloor}B^{\mathbb{F}}_{pq},e\in W_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}},u:C_{\phi}\to X\text{ satisfies }\overline{\partial}_{H}u+\nu_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(e)=0\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi><mtext> satisfies </mtext><msub><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}:=\Big\{(\phi,u,e)|\ \phi\in{}_{\lfloor}B^{\mathbb{F}}_{pq},e\in W_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}},u:C_{\phi}\to X\text{ satisfies }\overline{\partial}_{H}u+\nu_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}(e)=0\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15.17</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.Thmthm17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is a canonical <math id="S15.Thmthm17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant isomorphism <math id="S15.Thmthm17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}\cong V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}\cong V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show the natural map <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\to V_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\to V_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is bijective. Indeed, given any <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi,u,e)\in V_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi,u,e)\in V_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the set of all frames <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> on it are related by an element of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> which linearly transforms the frame. Each frame <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> induces a map <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{F}:C_{\phi}\to\mathbb{P}^{\bf d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝐝</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{F}:C_{\phi}\to\mathbb{P}^{\bf d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The condition that <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{F}=\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{F}=\phi</annotation></semantics></math> specifies a unique frame. Hence the map <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\to V_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\to V_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective. As it is obviously injective and <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant, the lemma follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)\subseteq V_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)\subseteq V_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be the preimage of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the zero locus of a smooth Fredholm section defined on a certain Banach manifold of maps from <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>; the concrete choice of the Banach manifold depends on certain Sobolev parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.18</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm18.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We say that <math id="S15.Thmthm18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi,u,e)\in V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi,u,e)\in V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="S15.Thmthm18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">transverse</span> if the linearization of the corresponding Fredholm section is surjective (which is independent of the Sobolev parameters). We say that the perturbation <math id="S15.Thmthm18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="S15.Thmthm18.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">transverse</span> if all points of <math id="S15.Thmthm18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S15.Thmthm18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> are transverse.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can choose the thicikening data appropriately so that transversality holds.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 15.19</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm19.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.Thmthm19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We omit the dependence on <math id="S15.Thmthm19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> from the notations.</span></p>
<ol id="S15.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I12.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given any integral modification of the topological energy, there exists a transverse thickening datum </span><math id="S15.I12.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on the flow category </span><math id="S15.I12.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, i.e., a transverse lift to </span><math id="S15.I12.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the multimodule </span><math id="S15.I12.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> over </span><math id="S15.I12.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\cdots{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝔻</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕠</mi><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝔻</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕠</mi><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo>;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝔻</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕠</mi><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\cdots{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Suppose </span><math id="S15.I12.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S15.I12.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S15.I12.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are transverse thickening data on these flow categories. Then there exists a transverse thickening datum </span><math id="S15.I12.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{W}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{W}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> which is a multimodule over </span><math id="S15.I12.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\cdots\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\cdots\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I12.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I12.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are two transverse thickening data on </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as multimodules over </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\cdots,\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\cdots,\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a lift of </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{H}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\mathbb{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐓𝐡𝐢𝐜𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Thick}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{H}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>ℍ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, as a homotopy from </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I12.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{X}}_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I12.i3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Subsubsection <a href="#S15.SS3.SSS6" title="15.3.6. Proof of Proposition ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.3.6</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Transversality implies the regularity of the thickened moduli spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 15.20</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm20.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.Thmthm20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose we choose transverse thickening data as claimed in Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm19" title="Proposition 15.19. ‣ 15.3.3. Transversality ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.19</span></a>.</span></p>
<ol id="S15.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="S15.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the thickened moduli space </span><math id="S15.I13.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is an </span><math id="S15.I13.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-stratified topological </span><math id="S15.I13.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-manifold near </span><math id="S15.I13.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}})^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}})^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Each thickened moduli space </span><math id="S15.I13.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is an </span><math id="S15.I13.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-stratified topological </span><math id="S15.I13.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-manifold near </span><math id="S15.I13.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}})^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}})^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I13.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Each thickened moduli space </span><math id="S15.I13.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is an </span><math id="S15.I13.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-stratified topological </span><math id="S15.I13.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-manifold near </span><math id="S15.I13.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}})^{-1}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>ℍ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{H}})^{-1}(0)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I13.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We only discuss the flow category case. By definition, transversality implies that each <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)\cong V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}(\phi)\cong V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is a topological manifold near where <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. The gluing argument implies that <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a stratified manifold. Since the thickening datum is collared, <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is also collared. Finally the canonical identification <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{\prime}\cong V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{\prime}\cong V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> shows <math id="S15.SS3.SSS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is a collared manifold.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.3.4. </span>The topological AMS lifts</h5>

<div id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now assuming transversality, by abuse of notations, the “regular locus” of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is still denoted by <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> (similar treatment for thickenings for multimodules and homotopies). Then one obtains topological Kuranishi spaces</p>
<table id="S15.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq}),\ p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq}),\ p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Together with the structural maps, one obtains a lift of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the category <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15.21</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.Thmthm21.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The topological AMS lift <math id="S15.Thmthm21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be canonically lifted to <math id="S15.Thmthm21.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We only need to construct rigidifications of the embeddings</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{prq}:K_{pr}\times K_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}K_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{prq}:K_{pr}\times K_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}K_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, one needs to find an orthogonal representation <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}\times G_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}\times G_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> and a germ of open embedding</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}\times_{G_{pr}\times G_{rq}}(K_{pr}\times K_{rq}\times N_{prq})\to\partial^{prq}K_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}\times_{G_{pr}\times G_{rq}}(K_{pr}\times K_{rq}\times N_{prq})\to\partial^{prq}K_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which extends <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{prq}\subseteq W_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{prq}\subseteq W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">be the orthogonal complement of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pr}\oplus W_{rq}\subseteq W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pr}\oplus W_{rq}\subseteq W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the underlying strict embedding in <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also rigidified via a representation <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{prq}\subseteq Q_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{prq}\subseteq Q_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{prq}:=W_{prq}\oplus Q_{prq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{prq}:=W_{prq}\oplus Q_{prq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Then one can check that there is a natural strict open embedding</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}\times_{G_{prq}}\left({\rm Stab}_{N_{prq}^{\epsilon}}(K_{pr}\times K_{rq})\right)\to\partial^{prq}K_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}\times_{G_{prq}}\left({\rm Stab}_{N_{prq}^{\epsilon}}(K_{pr}\times K_{rq})\right)\to\partial^{prq}K_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">(for a sufficiently small ball <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{prq}^{\epsilon}\subseteq N_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{prq}^{\epsilon}\subseteq N_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math>) which extends <math id="S15.SS3.SSS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{prq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS3.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.3.5. </span>Multimodules and homotopies</h5>

<div id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, for the flow multimodule <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> induced from a Floer domain <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, choose integral modifications</p>
<table id="S15.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S15.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S15.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}^{\Omega}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{i}\to{\mathbb{Z}}^{k},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}^{\Omega}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}_{i}\to{\mathbb{Z}}^{k},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S15.Ex91.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}^{\Omega}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}\to{\mathbb{Z}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}^{\Omega}:{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}\to{\mathbb{Z}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(and the constant <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathbb{X}}\in{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathbb{X}}\in{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>, see Definition <a href="#S15.Thmthm2" title="Definition 15.2. ‣ 15.1. Integral modification of topological energy ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.2</span></a>). Make choices for</p>
<table id="S15.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S15.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S15.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}^{\mathbb{fr}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}^{\mathbb{fr}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S15.Ex92.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}}^{\mathbb{fr}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}}^{\mathbb{fr}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">namely group reductions, by Lemma <a href="#S15.Thmthm9" title="Proposition 15.9. ‣ 15.2.6. Group reductions ‣ 15.2. Framed maps ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.9</span></a>, one can find a multimodule</p>
<table id="S15.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{X}}}^{\mathbb{fr}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{X}}}^{\mathbb{fr}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">over <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{\mathbb{F}_{1}}^{\mathbb{fr}},\cdots{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}}^{\mathbb{fr}};{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{fr}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝕞</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><mmultiscripts><mo>,</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝕞</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><mmultiscripts><mo>;</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mmultiscripts><mi>𝕞</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{\mathbb{F}_{1}}^{\mathbb{fr}},\cdots{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}}^{\mathbb{fr}};{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{fr}})</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in the category <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf map}}{}_{\rm rig}^{\rm fr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐦𝐚𝐩</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>fr</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf map}}{}_{\rm rig}^{\rm fr}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In parallel, choose collared and rigidified thickening data <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\bm{\Omega}},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{{\bm{\Omega}},{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, by Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm19" title="Proposition 15.19. ‣ 15.3.3. Transversality ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.19</span></a>, one can find a thickening datum <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{W}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{W}}^{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a multimodule over <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\ldots,\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}},\ldots,\mathbb{W}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{m}};\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{F}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the data <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{\mathbb{X}}^{\mathbb{fr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{map}}{}_{\mathbb{X}}^{\mathbb{fr}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{W}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> induce the collection of topological Kuranishi spaces</p>
<table id="S15.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=(G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},E_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=(G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},E_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}},S_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This provides a lift of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and called a <span id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">topological AMS lift</span> of the multimodule <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is a multimodule over <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\widehat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\widehat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\widehat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\widehat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to Lemma <a href="#S15.Thmthm21" title="Lemma 15.21. ‣ 15.3.4. The topological AMS lifts ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.21</span></a>, this lift can be further lifted (in a natural way) to <math id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p2.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}{}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}{}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The case of homotopies is similar and omited.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS3.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.3.6. </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm19" title="Proposition 15.19. ‣ 15.3.3. Transversality ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.19</span></a></h5>

<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The existence of a transverse thickening datum for a single moduli space was (essentially) given in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>, Section 4.1]</cite>. To construct a transverse thickening datum on a flow category, one needs a more systematic treatment.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All the constructions towards the proof is <span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ad hoc</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.22</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm22.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm22.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S15.Thmthm22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a Lie group.</p>
<ol id="S15.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I14.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-representation</span> of a Lie group <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a direct system of complex representations <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{\mu})_{\mu\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{\mu})_{\mu\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu}\to W_{\mu+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu}\to W_{\mu+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is an embedding. A <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation is said to be <span id="S15.I14.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">exhaustive</span> if any finite-dimensional representation <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> can be embedded into <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S15.I14.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A single representation <math id="S15.I14.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is regarded as a <math id="S15.I14.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation with <math id="S15.I14.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu}\equiv W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu}\equiv W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <math id="S15.I14.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation is called <span id="S15.I14.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">finite-dimensional</span> if all <math id="S15.I14.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> are finite-dimensional; is called <span id="S15.I14.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">unitary</span> if all <math id="S15.I14.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> are equipped with <math id="S15.I14.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant Hermitian inner products and the embeddings <math id="S15.I14.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu}\to W_{\mu+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu}\to W_{\mu+1}</annotation></semantics></math> are isometric.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I14.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S15.I14.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I14.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.I14.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict embedding</span> of <math id="S15.I14.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representations from <math id="S15.I14.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.I14.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{\mu}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{\mu}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of <math id="S15.I14.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant linear isometric embeddings <math id="S15.I14.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu}\to W_{\mu}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu}\to W_{\mu}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S15.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S15.Ex95.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="66.97" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-55.87231425043457px" version="1.1" viewBox="22.36 55.87 122.65 66.97" width="122.65"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 22.361082903359364 66.96657503032249) translate(0,3.46) translate(22.36,0)"><g transform="translate(-15.36,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="22.41"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex95.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{\mu}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{\mu}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 15.356080469722913 -0.27673578005007266 L 15.356080469722913 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(62.58,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 15.356080469722913 -0.27673578005007266 L 62.57490678267045 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 62.57490678267045 -0.27673578005007266 L 62.57490678267045 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-34.16)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -34.15595582862011 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -34.15595582862011 L 0.27673578005007266 -34.15595582862011" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(62.58,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="22.41"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex95.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{\mu}^{\prime}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{\mu}^{\prime}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 77.65423035875666 -11.569253138458645 L 78.2077019188568 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(77.93,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 77.65423035875666 -33.208800332088 L 78.2077019188568 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 77.65423035875666 -33.208800332088 L 78.2077019188568 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-22.36,0) translate(0,-44.3) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="36.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex95.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{\mu+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{\mu+1}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 22.361082903359364 -44.579796892025996 L 22.361082903359364 -44.026325331925854" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(55.57,0) translate(0,-44.3)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 22.361082903359364 -44.579796892025996 L 55.56988323544737 -44.026325331925854" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 55.56988323544737 -44.579796892025996 L 55.56988323544737 -44.026325331925854" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(55.57,0) translate(0,-44.3) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="36.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S15.Ex95.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{W_{\mu+1}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{W_{\mu+1}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
