</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the definition of the category <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can define another category <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> whose objects are <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}},B,C,(W_{\mu}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}},B,C,(W_{\mu}))</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}},B,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}},B,C)</annotation></semantics></math> is an object of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite-dimensional, exhaustive, and unitary <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\subseteq{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\subseteq{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can similarly define strict embeddings; the morphisms are conjugacy classes of strict embeddings. Then there is an obvious forgetful functor</p>
<table id="S15.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 15.23</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S15.I15" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I15.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I15.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I15.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I15.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist a lift of the monotone flow category </span><math id="S15.I15.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I15.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by </span><math id="S15.I15.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I15.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I15.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each smooth Floer domain </span><math id="S15.I15.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with </span><math id="S15.I15.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> negative cylindrical ends and one positive cylindrical end</span><span id="footnote23" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">23</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">23</sup>
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">23</span>
                          
                          
                          
                        The case with zero positive cylindrical ends, e.g., the case for Poincaré pairing, can be proved as well.</span></span></span><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, a lift of </span><math id="S15.I15.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I15.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by </span><math id="S15.I15.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, which is a monotone multimodule over </span><math id="S15.I15.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu},\ldots,\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu};\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu},\ldots,\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu};\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I15.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I15.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any 1-parameter family of Floer domains </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the associated homotopy </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}^{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> from </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, a lift to </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, denoted by </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}^{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, which is a monotone homotopy from </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}^{\Sigma_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}^{\Sigma_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I15.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}^{\Sigma_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕞</mi><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Dom}_{\mu}^{\Sigma_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I15.i3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the standard unitary representation <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d}={\mathbb{C}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d}={\mathbb{C}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}\cong U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}\cong U(d)</annotation></semantics></math>. The induced representation of the exterior algebra <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda W_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda W_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is also unitary. Then define the <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation with</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d,\mu}:=\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊕</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d,\mu}:=\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">whose Hermitian structure is the direct sum of the Hermitian structures of summands. The inclusion of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d,\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d,\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d,\mu+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d,\mu+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the composition</span></p>
<table id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d,\mu}=\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}\to\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu+1}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}\oplus\{0\}\\
\subseteq\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu+1}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}\oplus\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu+1}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}=W_{d,\mu+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>μ</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊕</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊕</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊕</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⨁</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⊕</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d,\mu}=\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}\to\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu+1}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}\oplus\{0\}\\
\subseteq\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu+1}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}\oplus\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^{\mu+1}(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}\right)^{\oplus 2^{\mu}}=W_{d,\mu+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is isometric. As any finite-dimensional representation of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(d)</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in a sufficiently higher tensor power <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Lambda W_{d})^{\otimes i}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains a <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then for any decomposition <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{0}+d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{0}+d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has the canonical isometry</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d_{0}}\oplus W_{d_{1}}\cong W_{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d_{0}}\oplus W_{d_{1}}\cong W_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is equivariant with respect to <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(d_{0})\times U(d_{1})\to U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(d_{0})\times U(d_{1})\to U(d)</annotation></semantics></math>. This map induces an equivariant isometric embeddings of the exterior algebras</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda W_{d_{0}}\oplus\Lambda W_{d_{1}}\to\Lambda W_{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda W_{d_{0}}\oplus\Lambda W_{d_{1}}\to\Lambda W_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">and hence isometric embeddings</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d_{0},\mu}\oplus W_{d_{1},\mu}\to W_{d,\mu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d_{0},\mu}\oplus W_{d_{1},\mu}\to W_{d,\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">There is an obvious associativity property of such embeddings, which induces well-defined maps for each partition <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=d_{0}+\cdots+d_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=d_{0}+\cdots+d_{l}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d_{0},\mu}\oplus\cdots\oplus W_{d_{l},\mu}\to W_{d,\mu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d_{0},\mu}\oplus\cdots\oplus W_{d_{l},\mu}\to W_{d,\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Then for each <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, the quadruple <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathcal{G}}_{d},B_{d},C_{d},(W_{d,\mu}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathcal{G}}_{d},B_{d},C_{d},(W_{d,\mu}))</annotation></semantics></math> is an object of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and they form a monotone flow category enriched in this category. The cases of multimodules and homotopies are the same; notice that in these cases, there are no well-defined strict embeddings but up to conjugacy, the embeddings are well-defined.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We explain what we will do next. We explain for the flow category case. We will choose sufficiently large <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> for each pair <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> inductively, such that <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> can cover all possible cokernels of the linearized operator of the Floer equation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p7.1" class="ltx_p">First we recall the following definition and lemma from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> with slight modification.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.24</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact Lie group acting smoothly on a manifold <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:V\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:V\to B</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth complex <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle. A <span id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">finite-dimensional approximation scheme</span> is a finite-dimensional <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V_{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V_{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> and a morphism of <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representations <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mu}:V_{\mu}\to C_{c}^{\infty}(B,V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mu}:V_{\mu}\to C_{c}^{\infty}(B,V)</annotation></semantics></math> such that the union of <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mu}(V_{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mu}(V_{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is dense with respect to the <math id="S15.Thmthm24.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}_{\rm loc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>loc</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}_{\rm loc}</annotation></semantics></math>-topology.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm25" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15.25</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm25.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm25.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S15.Thmthm25.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a><span id="S15.Thmthm25.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, Lemma 4.2]</span></cite><span id="S15.Thmthm25.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
There exists a finite-dimensional approximation scheme for given <math id="S15.Thmthm25.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G,B,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G,B,V</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 15.26</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm26.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm26.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.Thmthm26.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="S15.Thmthm26.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=U(d)</annotation></semantics></math>, the finite-dimensional approximation scheme can be taken such that <math id="S15.Thmthm26.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mu}=W_{d,\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mu}=W_{d,\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S15.Thmthm26.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{d,\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{d,\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S15.Thmthm26.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-representation specified in the proof of Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm23" title="Proposition 15.23. ‣ 15.3.6. Proof of Proposition ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.23</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is because any <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in some <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\mu^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\mu^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Now we can prove Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm19" title="Proposition 15.19. ‣ 15.3.3. Transversality ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.19</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm19" title="Proposition 15.19. ‣ 15.3.3. Transversality ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.19</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can choose a collection of collared thickening data</span></p>
<table id="S15.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu_{pq,\mu}:W_{pq,\mu}\to C_{c}^{\infty}({}_{\lfloor}\mathring{C}_{pq}\times X,\Lambda^{0,1}_{{}_{\lfloor}\mathring{C}_{pq}/{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}}\otimes TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{pq,\mu}:W_{pq,\mu}\to C_{c}^{\infty}({}_{\lfloor}\mathring{C}_{pq}\times X,\Lambda^{0,1}_{{}_{\lfloor}\mathring{C}_{pq}/{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}}\otimes TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">such that they are compatible with the structural maps of the flow category. Then using the compactness of each <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the image of <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>, when restricted to the domain of each solution, covers the cokernel of the linearization. Then we can choose <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> inductively. Then define <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}:=W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}:=W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.SS3.SSS6.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{pq}:=\nu_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{pq}:=\nu_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This provides a transverse thickening datum on the flow category. The inductive construction on multimodules and homotopies are exactly the same.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">15.4. </span>Relatively smooth AMS lifts</h4>

<div id="S15.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The topological AMS lifts actually admit refinement in the so-called relatively smooth category (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>). The discussion in this category is important for eventually obtaining smooth Kuranishi spaces. We introduce the category of Kuranishi spaces in this version.</p>
</div>
<section id="S15.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.4.1. </span>Relative spaces and relative smooth structures</h5>

<div id="S15.Thmthm27" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.27</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Relative spaces)<span id="S15.Thmthm27.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm27.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S15.I16" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I16.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I16.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I16.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A (stratified) <span id="S15.I16.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relative space</span> consists of a pair of <math id="S15.I16.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified topological spaces <math id="S15.I16.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S15.I16.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and a stratified continuous map <math id="S15.I16.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:Y\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:Y\to S</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S15.I16.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is understood from the context, we denote a relative space by <math id="S15.I16.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y/S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I16.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I16.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I16.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.I16.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relative map</span> from <math id="S15.I16.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y/S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.I16.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z/T</annotation></semantics></math> is a commutative diagram</p>
<table id="S15.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 13.75293pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-7.01389pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Y\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 44.49197pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-23.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 44.49197pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Z\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 51.2628pt\raise-23.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-13.75293pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\pi(Y)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 37.75293pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 37.75293pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\pi(Z)}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-54.88675313980991px" height="65.03" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="19.03 54.89 108.66 65.03" width="108.66"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 19.02992899889304 65.03385842316573) translate(0,3.46) translate(19.03,0)"> <g transform="translate(-9.71,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.8em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="11.11"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mi>Y</mi></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 9.705134574285232 -0.27673578005007266 L 9.705134574285232 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(61.56,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 9.705134574285232 -0.27673578005007266 L 61.56354486917549 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 61.56354486917549 -0.27673578005007266 L 61.56354486917549 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -7.610350076103501 L 0.27673578005007266 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(0,-32.75)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -32.74755291841791 L 0.27673578005007266 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -32.74755291841791 L 0.27673578005007266 -32.74755291841791" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(61.56,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="10.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mi>Z</mi></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 70.65560422828456 -7.610350076103501 L 71.20907578838471 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(70.93,0) translate(0,-32.75)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 70.65560422828456 -32.74755291841791 L 71.20907578838471 -7.610350076103501" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 70.65560422828456 -32.74755291841791 L 71.20907578838471 -32.74755291841791" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(-19.03,0) translate(0,-43.82) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.15em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="29.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 19.02992899889304 -44.093888809163985 L 19.02992899889304 -43.54041724906384" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(52.24,0) translate(0,-43.82)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 19.02992899889304 -44.093888809163985 L 52.238729330981045 -43.54041724906384" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 52.238729330981045 -44.093888809163985 L 52.238729330981045 -43.54041724906384" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(52.24,0) translate(0,-43.82) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.1em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="29.09"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 13.75293pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-7.01389pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Y\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 44.49197pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-23.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 44.49197pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{Z\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 51.2628pt\raise-23.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-13.75293pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\pi(Y)\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 37.75293pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 37.75293pt\raise-31.66666pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\pi(Z)}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.I16.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S15.I16.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=T</annotation></semantics></math>, without further declaration, we will assume that the underlying map from <math id="S15.I16.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(Y)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.I16.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of the identity map of <math id="S15.I16.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I16.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I16.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I16.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.I16.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relative homeomorphism</span> is a relative map <math id="S15.I16.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:Y/S\to Z/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:Y/S\to Z/T</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of a homeomorphism from <math id="S15.I16.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.I16.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> and a homeomorphism from <math id="S15.I16.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.I16.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I16.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S15.I16.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I16.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S15.I16.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a topological group, a <math id="S15.I16.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action on relative space is a continuous action via relative homeomorphisms. In particular, the map <math id="S15.I16.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:Y\to S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:Y\to S</annotation></semantics></math> is equivariant.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I16.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S15.I16.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I16.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S15.I16.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be another topological space. The <span id="S15.I16.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">horizontal stabilization</span> of a relative space <math id="S15.I16.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y/S</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S15.I16.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the relative space</p>
<table id="S15.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{D}^{\rm hor}(Y/S)=(Y\times D)/(S\times D)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>hor</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{D}^{\rm hor}(Y/S)=(Y\times D)/(S\times D).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.I16.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S15.I16.i5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vertical stabilization</span> of <math id="S15.I16.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y/S</annotation></semantics></math> is the relative space</p>
<table id="S15.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{D}^{\rm vert}(Y/S)=(Y\times D)/S." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>vert</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{D}^{\rm vert}(Y/S)=(Y\times D)/S.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.I16.i5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Notice that both horizontal and vertical stabilizations are functors on the categories of relative spaces. Moreover, given <math id="S15.I16.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1},D_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1},D_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a natural transformation</p>
<table id="S15.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{D_{1}}^{\rm hor}\circ{\rm Stab}_{D_{2}}^{\rm vert}\to{\rm Stab}_{D_{2}}^{\rm vert}\circ{\rm Stab}_{D_{1}}^{\rm hor}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>hor</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>vert</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>vert</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>Stab</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>hor</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{D_{1}}^{\rm hor}\circ{\rm Stab}_{D_{2}}^{\rm vert}\to{\rm Stab}_{D_{2}}^{\rm vert}\circ{\rm Stab}_{D_{1}}^{\rm hor}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm28" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 15.28</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm28.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.Thmthm28.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A fiber bundle is a canonically a relative space. In particular, we denote by <math id="S15.Thmthm28.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{k}/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{k}/S</annotation></semantics></math> the relative space associated to the trivial <math id="S15.Thmthm28.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> bundle over <math id="S15.Thmthm28.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm29" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm29.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.29</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm29.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm29.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U/S\subseteq\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{m}/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U/S\subseteq\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{m}/S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V/T\subseteq\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{n}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V/T\subseteq\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{n}/T</annotation></semantics></math> be open subsets. A continuous map <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:U/S\to V/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:U/S\to V/T</annotation></semantics></math> is called rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty,k}</annotation></semantics></math> if the map <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:U\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:U\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, determined by</p>
<table id="S15.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(v,x)=(F(v,x),\underline{\smash{\varphi}}(x))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(v,x)=(F(v,x),\underline{\smash{\varphi}}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.2" class="ltx_p">has all partial derivatives in <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in{\mathbb{R}}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and those up order <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> varies continuously in <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on compact subsets of <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. A rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty,k}</annotation></semantics></math>-map is called a rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty,k}</annotation></semantics></math>-diffeomorphism if it has a rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty,k}</annotation></semantics></math>-inverse. <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relatively smooth</span>, or rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, if it is rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty,k}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S15.Thmthm29.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.30</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm30.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relative smooth structure</span> on <math id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y/S</annotation></semantics></math> consists of an atlas <math id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\alpha}:U_{\alpha}/S\to\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{n}/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\alpha}:U_{\alpha}/S\to\underline{\smash{\mathbb{R}}}^{n}/S</annotation></semantics></math> which are rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>-compatible. More precisely 1) <math id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=\cup U_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∪</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=\cup U_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and 2) for any <math id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, the map</p>
<table id="S15.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\alpha}\circ\varphi_{\beta}^{-1}:\varphi_{\beta}((U_{\alpha}\cap U_{\beta})/S)\to\varphi_{\alpha}((U_{\alpha}\cap U_{\beta})/S)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\alpha}\circ\varphi_{\beta}^{-1}:\varphi_{\beta}((U_{\alpha}\cap U_{\beta})/S)\to\varphi_{\alpha}((U_{\alpha}\cap U_{\beta})/S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is a rel-<math id="S15.Thmthm30.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>-diffeomorphism.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that if <math id="S15.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y/S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y/S</annotation></semantics></math> has a relative smooth structure, then each fiber of <math id="S15.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> has a well-defined smooth structure. Then there is a well-defined rel-<math id="S15.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> vector bundle</p>
<table id="S15.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vert}Y/S\to Y," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vert</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vert}Y/S\to Y,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS4.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">called the <span id="S15.SS4.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vertical tangent bundle</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S15.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">15.4.2. </span>The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces</h5>

<div id="S15.Thmthm31" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm31.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15.31</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm31.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Category of relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces)<span id="S15.Thmthm31.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm31.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S15.I17" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I17.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I17.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I17.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.I17.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relative smooth Kuranishi space</span> is a quadruple <math id="S15.I17.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/B=(G,V/B,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/B=(G,V/B,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S15.I17.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> is a topological Kuranishi space, <math id="S15.I17.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth <math id="S15.I17.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold, together with a <math id="S15.I17.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant rel-<math id="S15.I17.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> structure on <math id="S15.I17.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V/B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I17.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I17.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I17.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.I17.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stabilization</span> of a relative smooth Kuranishi space <math id="S15.I17.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/B</annotation></semantics></math> by a <math id="S15.I17.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant disk bundle</p>
<table id="S15.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=D^{\rm hor}\oplus D^{\rm vert}\subseteq N^{\rm hor}\oplus N^{\rm vert}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>hor</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>vert</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>hor</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>vert</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=D^{\rm hor}\oplus D^{\rm vert}\subseteq N^{\rm hor}\oplus N^{\rm vert}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.I17.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is the relative Kuranishi space</p>
<table id="S15.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{D}(K/B)=(G,\tilde{V}/\tilde{B},\tilde{E},\tilde{S})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{D}(K/B)=(G,\tilde{V}/\tilde{B},\tilde{E},\tilde{S})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.I17.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S15.I17.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}/\tilde{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}/\tilde{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is the stabilization of the relative space <math id="S15.I17.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V/B</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S15.I17.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> (which carries a canonically induced relative smooth structure), <math id="S15.I17.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S15.I17.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}</annotation></semantics></math> are the natural stabilization.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I17.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I17.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I17.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S15.I17.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">strict embedding</span> of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces from <math id="S15.I17.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}/B_{1}=(G_{1},V_{1}/B_{1},E_{1},S_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}/B_{1}=(G_{1},V_{1}/B_{1},E_{1},S_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.I17.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}/B_{2}=(G_{2},V_{2}/B_{2},E_{2},S_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}/B_{2}=(G_{2},V_{2}/B_{2},E_{2},S_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a strict embedding</p>
<table id="S15.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.I17.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(which includes a group embedding <math id="S15.I17.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{G}:G_{1}\to G_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{G}:G_{1}\to G_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) and an <math id="S15.I17.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant smooth embedding <math id="S15.I17.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1}\to B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1}\to B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I17.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S15.I17.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I17.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S15.I17.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">embedding</span> of relative Kuranishi spaces from <math id="S15.I17.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}/B_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}/B_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S15.I17.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}/B_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}/B_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a conjugacy class of strict embeddings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I17.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S15.I17.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.I17.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S15.I17.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the category of relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces whose morphisms are embeddings. One can also consider the rigidified and collared versions of this category.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that there is an obvious functor</p>
<table id="S15.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}\to\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">by sending</p>
<table id="S15.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S15.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G,V/B,E,S)\mapsto(G,V,E,S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G,V/B,E,S)\mapsto(G,V,E,S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S15.Thmthm32" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S15.Thmthm32.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 15.32</span></span><span id="S15.Thmthm32.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Relative smooth structures on AMS lifts)<span id="S15.Thmthm32.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S15.Thmthm32.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S15.I18" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S15.I18.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S15.I18.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I18.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I18.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationf1" title="Situation Flow(i). ‣ 9.2. Floer flow category ‣ 9. Geometric Flow Categories ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(i)</span></a><span id="S15.I18.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, any topological AMS lift of the Floer flow category is canonically lifted to </span><math id="S15.I18.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I18.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S15.I18.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationm1" title="Situation Module(i). ‣ 10.2. Multimodules from smooth domains ‣ 10. Geometric Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(i)</span></a><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S15.I18.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the AMS lift of the outercollaring of </span><math id="S15.I18.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I18.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as a multimodule over the topological AMS lifts </span><math id="S15.I18.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> enriched in </span><math id="S15.I18.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="S15.I18.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is canonically lifted to </span><math id="S15.I18.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S15.I18.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S15.I18.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationh1" title="Situation Homotopy(i). ‣ 11.1. Homotopies from varying Floer data ‣ 11. Homotopies of Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(i)</span></a><span id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S15.I18.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a topological AMS lift of the outercollaring of </span><math id="S15.I18.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S15.I18.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="S15.I18.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is canonically enriched in </span><math id="S15.I18.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S15.I18.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS4.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We only discuss the case about the flow category. The other cases can be proved in the same manner. For each pair <math id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> of objects in <math id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fiberwise smooth structure of <math id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}V_{pq}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}V_{pq}\to{}_{\lfloor}B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> follows from the implicit function theorem. The fact that these fiberwise structures vary in the rel-<math id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> sense can be proved using the method of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite> (which treats the case of Gromov–Witten theory). Alternatively, it follows from the proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Proposition 6.2]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S15.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We summarize the construction so far in the following situations.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmsituationf3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_situationf">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmsituationf3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Situation Flow(iii)</span></span><span id="Thmsituationf3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmsituationf3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmsituationf3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmsituationf3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationf2" title="Situation Flow(ii). ‣ 15.1.1. Pullback the domain flow category, multimodule, and homotopy ‣ 15.1. Integral modification of topological energy ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(ii)</span></a>, the domain flow category <math id="Thmsituationf3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math> induces an associated flow category <math id="Thmsituationf3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Map}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\mathbb{fr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Map}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\mathbb{fr}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose a transverse thickening datum <math id="Thmsituationf3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{W}}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{W}}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a group reduction, which gives a relatively smooth AMS lift <math id="Thmsituationf3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="Thmsituationf3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmsituationm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_situationm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmsituationm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Situation Module(iii)</span></span><span id="Thmsituationm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmsituationm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmsituationm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmsituationm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationm2" title="Situation Module(ii). ‣ 15.1.1. Pullback the domain flow category, multimodule, and homotopy ‣ 15.1. Integral modification of topological energy ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(ii)</span></a>, <math id="Thmsituationm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a relatively smooth AMS lift subject to an outercollaring width and a compatible list of integral actions on the involved flow categories. <math id="Thmsituationm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a multimodule over <math id="Thmsituationm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> where each member of this tuple is a relative smooth AMS lift of an involved Floer flow category subject to the outercollaring width and the chosen integral action.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmsituationh3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_situationh">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmsituationh3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Situation Homotopy(iii)</span></span><span id="Thmsituationh3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmsituationh3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmsituationh3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmsituationh3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationh2" title="Situation Homotopy(ii). ‣ 15.1.1. Pullback the domain flow category, multimodule, and homotopy ‣ 15.1. Integral modification of topological energy ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(ii)</span></a>, <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a relatively smooth AMS lift of the homotopy <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to an outercollaring width and a compatible list of integral actions on the involved Floer flow categories based on the homotopy <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{H}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂𝐮𝐫𝐯𝐞</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Curve}}_{\rm rig}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The two boundaries of <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> are relatively smooth AMS lifts of multimodules <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{X}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{X}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="Thmsituationh3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{X}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{X}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S16" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">16. </span>Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations</h3>

<section id="S16.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">16.1. </span>Main statements about normal complex structures</h4>

<div id="S16.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that one has defined the category of relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces <math id="S16.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given any object <math id="S16.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/B=(G,V/B,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/B=(G,V/B,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math>, one has a well-defined vertical tangent bundle</p>
<table id="S16.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V\to V" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V\to V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is a <math id="S16.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant relatively smooth vector bundle. Recall the definition of equivariant normal complex structures (Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm23" title="Definition 3.23. ‣ 3.3.3. Normally complex Kuranishi spaces ‣ 3.3. Stable complex structures and normal complex structures ‣ 3. Kuranishi Spaces ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.23</span></a>). Given a relatively smooth Kuranishi space <math id="S16.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/B=(G,V/B,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/B=(G,V/B,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math>, a <span id="S16.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relative NC structure</span> on <math id="S16.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/B</annotation></semantics></math> is by definition a <math id="S16.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant NC structure on <math id="S16.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V\to V</annotation></semantics></math>. One can then define the category of relative NC Kuranishi spaces, denoted by</p>
<table id="S16.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}^{\rm NC}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>NC</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}^{\rm NC}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We can also consider the rigidified and collared versions. We omit the detailed definitions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now we state our main theorems about the existence of fiberwise stable complex structures of Floer flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 16.1</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationf3" title="Situation Flow(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(iii)</span></a>, the relatively smooth AMS lift <math id="S16.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a set of lifts, denoted temporarily by <math id="S16.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S16.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>. We call such a lift a </span><span id="S16.Thmthm1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relatively NC AMS lift</span><span id="S16.Thmthm1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Subsection <a href="#S16.SS3" title="16.3. Proof of Theorem ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 16.2</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the following theorem, what we call a relative NC AMS lifts of <math id="S16.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> actually involves more data than the lifts to <math id="S16.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>; they also include certain choices made for the construction. The construction of the relative NC AMS lifts for multimodules actually depends on these choices, not only on the resulting lifts of the flow categories.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 16.3</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationm3" title="Situation Module(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(iii)</span></a>, suppose <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are relatively NC AMS lifts of them provided by Theorem <a href="#S16.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 16.1. ‣ 16.1. Main statements about normal complex structures ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.1</span></a>. Then <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a set of lifts, denoted temporarily by <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, to <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> as a multimodule over <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Each of such <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is called a </span><span id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relatively NC AMS lifts</span><span id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (of <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S16.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Subsection <a href="#S16.SS4" title="16.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.4</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 16.4</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationh3" title="Situation Homotopy(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(iii)</span></a>, suppose <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are relatively NC AMS lifts of the involved Floer flow categories, <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are relatively NC AMS lifts of the two multimodules subject to the fixed outercollaring width and the fixed list of compatible integral actions. Then the relatively smooth AMS lift <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a lift, denoted by <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> temporarily, to <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> as a homotopy from <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We call <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{H}}}}</annotation></semantics></math> a relatively NC AMS lift (of <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S16.Thmthm4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">A tedious reformulation of the proofs of Theorem <a href="#S16.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 16.1. ‣ 16.1. Main statements about normal complex structures ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S16.Thmthm3" title="Theorem 16.3. ‣ 16.1. Main statements about normal complex structures ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.3</span></a>. There are no essential new ingredients.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S16.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">16.2. </span>Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space</h4>

<div id="S16.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first review the construction of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, Section 11]</cite> in the case of a single moduli space from the Floer flow category. Let <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Floer flow category associated to the Hamiltonian <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider a pair of objects <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> such that there is no intermediate object <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}=(G_{pq},V_{pq},E_{pq},S_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math> be an AMS global chart of <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, viewed as an object of <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can ignore <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> for the discussion but should remember the reletive structure <math id="S16.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}/B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}/B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will also drop the outercollaring for a moment.</p>
</div>
<section id="S16.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">16.2.1. </span>A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation</h5>

<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first specify a family of complex linear Cauchy–Riemann operator for points in <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix an almost complex structure <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-linear connection <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{TX}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{TX}</annotation></semantics></math> such that its holonomy along each 1-periodic orbit of <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial. Choose <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first look at an individual smooth map <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u:{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u:{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> which converges exponentially to 1-periodic orbits of <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the space</p>
<table id="S16.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\subseteq W^{1,\tau}_{\rm loc}(u^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>loc</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\subseteq W^{1,\tau}_{\rm loc}(u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">to be the space of sections which differ from <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{TX}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{TX}</annotation></semantics></math>-parallel sections along the limiting periodic orbits by <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{1,\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{1,\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>-small terms near infinity. Then the <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>-linear connection <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{TX}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{TX}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator</p>
<table id="S16.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u^{*}TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u^{*}TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">As <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> converges exponentially to periodic orbits, it is easy to see that <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is Fredholm.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The operator <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the linearization of the Floer equation can be connected by a particular 1-parameter family of Fredholm operators modulo certain finite-dimensional corrections. Choose a cut-off function</p>
<table id="S16.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi:{\rm Dom}(u)\cong{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to[0,1]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Dom</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi:{\rm Dom}(u)\cong{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which only depends on the <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>-variable such that <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi(s)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi(s)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\ll 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\ll 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi(s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi(s)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\gg 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\gg 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For each object <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{p}:{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{p}:{\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding constant solution to the Floer equation (which does not depend on the capping). Then there is an associated linearized operator</p>
<table id="S16.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u_{p}}(\xi)=\partial_{s}\xi+J_{t}\left(\nabla_{t}\xi-\nabla_{\xi}X_{H_{t}}(p)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ξ</mi></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u_{p}}(\xi)=\partial_{s}\xi+J_{t}\left(\nabla_{t}\xi-\nabla_{\xi}X_{H_{t}}(p)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="S16.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\subseteq W^{1,\tau}_{\rm loc}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>loc</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\subseteq W^{1,\tau}_{\rm loc}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">be the subspace of <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{1,\tau}_{\rm loc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>loc</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{1,\tau}_{\rm loc}</annotation></semantics></math>-sections which satisfies the same asymptotic condition near <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math> and which is <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{1,\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{1,\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>-small near <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then consider the interpolation</p>
<table id="S16.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}D_{p}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\to&amp;\ L^{\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)\\
\xi\mapsto&amp;\ (1-\chi)(\nabla^{TX}\xi)_{J_{0}}^{0,1}+\chi D_{u_{p}}(\xi).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msup><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}D_{p}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\to&amp;\ L^{\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)\\
\xi\mapsto&amp;\ (1-\chi)(\nabla^{TX}\xi)_{J_{0}}^{0,1}+\chi D_{u_{p}}(\xi).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is a real-linear Fredholm operator. Notice that from the definition, <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> only depends on the underlying 1-periodic orbit but not the capping.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now choose, for each object <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (actually, as discussed above, only depending on the underlying orbit), a finite-dimensional complex vector space <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{p}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{p}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, a linear map</p>
<table id="S16.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{p}:R_{p}^{+}\to C_{0}^{\infty}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{p}:R_{p}^{+}\to C_{0}^{\infty}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">such that the map</p>
<table id="S16.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{p}\oplus D_{p}:R_{p}^{+}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{p}\oplus D_{p}:R_{p}^{+}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">is surjective. Denote</p>
<table id="S16.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{p}^{-}:={\rm Ker}(\theta_{p}\oplus D_{p})\subseteq R_{p}^{+}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u^{*}TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{p}^{-}:={\rm Ker}(\theta_{p}\oplus D_{p})\subseteq R_{p}^{+}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u^{*}TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Notice that the pair <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R_{p}^{-},R_{p}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R_{p}^{-},R_{p}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on the Sobolev exponent <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now we would like to construct interpolations between <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, up to factors coming from <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, in a 1-parameter family. The basic idea has been described in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, Section 11]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Appendix B]</cite>. However, we need to be more careful when generalizing to the case of multimodules.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">More precisely, we would like to construct an interpolation between</p>
<table id="S16.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}\oplus D_{u}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus W^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}\oplus D_{u}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus W^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S16.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}\widetilde{\oplus}D_{q}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\widetilde{\oplus}\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u_{q}^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{q}^{*}TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>⊕</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>⊕</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}\widetilde{\oplus}D_{q}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\widetilde{\oplus}\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u_{q}^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u_{q}^{*}TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\oplus}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>⊕</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\oplus}</annotation></semantics></math> means the subset of the direct sum satisfying the matching condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">To build the interpolation, consider the family of cut-off functions</p>
<table id="S16.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{\rho}:{\mathbb{R}}\to[0,1],\ \chi_{\rho}(s)=\chi(s-\rho)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{\rho}:{\mathbb{R}}\to[0,1],\ \chi_{\rho}(s)=\chi(s-\rho).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Then for all <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S16.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}D_{u,\rho}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\to&amp;\ L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u^{*}TX),\\
\xi\mapsto&amp;\ (1-\chi_{\rho})(\nabla^{TX}\xi)_{J_{0}}^{0,1}+\chi_{\rho}D_{u}(\xi).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msup><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}D_{u,\rho}:\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(u^{*}TX)\to&amp;\ L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes u^{*}TX),\\
\xi\mapsto&amp;\ (1-\chi_{\rho})(\nabla^{TX}\xi)_{J_{0}}^{0,1}+\chi_{\rho}D_{u}(\xi).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Notice that even if <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> has bubble components, these operators are still defined. Then intuitively, we have</p>
<table id="S16.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S16.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \lim_{\rho\to-\infty}D_{u,\rho}\approx D_{p}\oplus D_{u},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \lim_{\rho\to-\infty}D_{u,\rho}\approx D_{p}\oplus D_{u},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \lim_{\rho\to+\infty}D_{u,\rho}\approx D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}\widetilde{\oplus}D_{q}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>⊕</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \lim_{\rho\to+\infty}D_{u,\rho}\approx D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}\widetilde{\oplus}D_{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.4" class="ltx_p">This is the underlying idea of interpolating the linearized operator <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> and a complex linear operator <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, up to the two operators <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> which are independent of <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">To better formulate this construction over the whole Kuranishi chart <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to introduce an auxiliary space. Denote</p>
<table id="S16.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{pq}:=B_{pq}\times[-\infty,+\infty]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{pq}:=B_{pq}\times[-\infty,+\infty],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">viewed as a product of stratified spaces where <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-\infty,+\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-\infty,+\infty]</annotation></semantics></math> has one open stratum and two boundary strata. We define an auxiliary universal curve <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> whose fiber <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(-\infty,+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(-\infty,+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> is still <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, while for <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> has the additional component of the domain of the map <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. the domain of <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>. One can then define the additional space <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> which is identical to <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\times[-\infty,+\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\times[-\infty,+\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>. However, for each point <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, we regard <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> as a map <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{u}:\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho}\to X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{u}:\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho}\to X</annotation></semantics></math> where if <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{u}</annotation></semantics></math> maps the extra cylindrical component to the constant loop at the negative or the positive end. Then <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is still relatively smooth. The operator <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u,\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u,\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as a Cauchy–Riemann operator <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\widetilde{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\widetilde{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> acting on the bundle <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{u}^{*}TX" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{u}^{*}TX</annotation></semantics></math> (and extended to suitable Sobolev completions). We remark that, this setup facilitates the gluing construction: when <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, if the operator <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p9.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u,\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u,\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective, then each vector in the kernel can be glued to an element in the kernel at a nearby point.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">With the above viewpoint understood, using basic gluing construction, one obtains the following technical lemma. Let</p>
<table id="S16.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">be the infinite-dimensional vector bundle whose fiber over <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)</annotation></semantics></math> is the space</p>
<table id="S16.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}=\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho},\widetilde{u}^{*}TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}=\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(\widetilde{C}_{\phi,\rho},\widetilde{u}^{*}TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p10.3" class="ltx_p">Notice that when <math id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, one has the splitting</p>
<table id="S16.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}=\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}=\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p10.4" class="ltx_p">or</p>
<table id="S16.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}=\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{q}^{*}TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}=\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{q}^{*}TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16.5</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist a unitary representation <math id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and a continuous <math id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant bundle map over <math id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pq}\times X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pq}\times X</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}:\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+}\to\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}:\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+}\to\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfying the following conditions. Let <math id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S16.Thmthm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\phi}=(\phi,\rho)\in\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\phi}=(\phi,\rho)\in\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="S16.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S16.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S16.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="S16.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, with respect to the splitting (</span><a href="#S16.E4" title="In 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.4</span></a><span id="S16.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), </span><math id="S16.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has the block form</span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}\nu_{p}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{array}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}\nu_{p}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{array}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="S16.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is specified in (</span><a href="#S16.E2" title="In 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.2</span></a><span id="S16.I1.i1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S16.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="S16.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, with respect the splitting (</span><a href="#S16.E5" title="In 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.5</span></a><span id="S16.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), </span><math id="S16.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has the block form</span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}0&amp;\nu_{\widetilde{x}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\nu_{q}\end{array}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>ν</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}0&amp;\nu_{\widetilde{x}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\nu_{q}\end{array}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\widetilde{x}}:W_{pq}\to\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\widetilde{x}}:W_{pq}\to\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I1.i2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is a complex-linear linear map.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S16.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="S16.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the image of </span><math id="S16.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> at </span><math id="S16.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is transverse to the image of the operator </span><math id="S16.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\widetilde{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\widetilde{u}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS2.SSS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Basic Fredholm theory and a portion of gluing argument.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S16.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">16.2.2. </span>An extended index bundle</h5>

<div id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now assume <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is given as in Lemma <a href="#S16.Thmthm5" title="Lemma 16.5. ‣ 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.5</span></a>, consider the family of linear maps parametrized by <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S16.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{\widetilde{u}}:\big(R_{p}^{+}\oplus W_{pq}\oplus R_{q}^{+}\big)\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(\widetilde{u}^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes\widetilde{u}^{*}TX)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{\widetilde{u}}:\big(R_{p}^{+}\oplus W_{pq}\oplus R_{q}^{+}\big)\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(\widetilde{u}^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes\widetilde{u}^{*}TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 16.6</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The union of kernels of <math id="S16.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{\widetilde{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{\widetilde{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> form a continuous <span id="footnote24" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">24</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">24</sup>
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">24</span></span>
                      
                      
                      
                    <span id="footnote24.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">In fact it is a relative smooth vector bundle.</span></span></span></span> vector bundle</span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{pq}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{pq}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is based on the typical gluing construction. However, one needs to maintain the linear structure in the gluing procedure. The pregluing is constructed using parallel transport on the target manifold <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and cut-paste on the domain, which are linear in the input. The use of the implicit function theorem can also respect the linear feature.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Hence the vector bundles on the two boundary pieces, <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{\pm}\widetilde{V}_{pq}:=V_{pq}\times\{\pm\infty\}\cong V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>±</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{\pm}\widetilde{V}_{pq}:=V_{pq}\times\{\pm\infty\}\cong V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are (non-canonically) isomorphic. The family of kernels selects a homotopy class of isomorphisms. By the specific characterization of <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> given in Lemma <a href="#S16.Thmthm5" title="Lemma 16.5. ‣ 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.5</span></a>, one can see that</p>
<table id="S16.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{pq}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{pq}}\cong\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{-}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+};" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{pq}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{pq}}\cong\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{-}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S16.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{pq}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{pq}}\cong\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{-}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{pq}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{pq}}\cong\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{-}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is formed by the kernels of the complex-linear operator</p>
<table id="S16.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}:W_{pq}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}:W_{pq}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)\to L^{\tau}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">hence is a complex vector bundle.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can then choose a continuous bundle isomorphism</p>
<table id="S16.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{-}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+}\cong\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{-}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{-}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+}\cong\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{-}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> acts trivially on the vector spaces <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{p}^{\pm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>±</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{p}^{\pm}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{q}^{\pm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>±</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{q}^{\pm}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex, one can see that this is a stable isomorphism from <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence induces an NC structure on <math id="S16.SS2.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S16.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">16.3. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S16.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 16.1. ‣ 16.1. Main statements about normal complex structures ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.1</span></a></h4>

<section id="S16.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">16.3.1. </span>An extended Kuranishi flow category</h5>

<div id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We extend the previous construction to all moduli spaces involved in a single Floer flow category <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To construct the interpolation in a compatible way for all moduli spaces, we utilize the lateral lines (see Definition <a href="#S14.E5" title="In 14.3.4. Concatenation of cylinders ‣ 14.3. Construction of the domain flow categories ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.5</span></a>). Recall that for each pair of objects <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq q</annotation></semantics></math>, in the AMS construction there is a <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> parametrizing certain curves in <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the moduli space</p>
<table id="S16.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2,+}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},d_{pq})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2,+}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},d_{pq})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">of 1-marked stable cylinders with the interior marked points lying on the lateral lines of domains. There is the forgetful map with <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> as generic fibers</p>
<table id="S16.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2,+}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},d_{pq})\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},d_{pq})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℂ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2,+}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},d_{pq})\to\overline{\mathcal{M}}{}_{0,2}^{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{CP}^{d_{pq}},d_{pq}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> be the preimage of <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>; let <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a typical element of <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> with the underlying point <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\in B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\in B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the convention that this interior marked point does not go to sphere bubbles but only stay in cylindrical components; namely, it can coincide with a node. Let</p>
<table id="S16.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">be the pullback of <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{pq}\to B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{pq}\to B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, which still gives an equivariant family of curves</p>
<table id="S16.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{C}}_{pq}:=({\mathcal{G}}_{pq},\widetilde{B}_{pq},\widetilde{C}_{pq})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{C}}_{pq}:=({\mathcal{G}}_{pq},\widetilde{B}_{pq},\widetilde{C}_{pq}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\widetilde{\phi}}\subseteq\widetilde{C}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\widetilde{\phi}}\subseteq\widetilde{C}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> be the fiber over <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\phi}\in\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\phi}\in\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is a natural map</p>
<table id="S16.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\widetilde{\phi}}\to C_{\phi}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\widetilde{\phi}}\to C_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which collapses at most one constant cylindrical component. Notice that for each <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\phi}\in\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\phi}\in\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a special cylindrical component</p>
<table id="S16.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}\subseteq C_{\widetilde{\phi}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}\subseteq C_{\widetilde{\phi}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">which contains the marked point.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that there two disjoint closed subsets</p>
<table id="S16.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S16.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \partial^{-}\widetilde{B}_{pq},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \partial^{-}\widetilde{B}_{pq},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \partial^{+}\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \partial^{+}\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">corresponding to configurations where the marked points is at the very left resp. very right of the curve. Notice that one has canonical identifications</p>
<table id="S16.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{-}\widetilde{B}_{pq}\cong B_{pq}\cong\partial^{+}\widetilde{B}_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{-}\widetilde{B}_{pq}\cong B_{pq}\cong\partial^{+}\widetilde{B}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> can also be organized as morphism spaces of a flow category. However, as they are objects in a special category which does not have an obvious symmetric monoidal structure, therefore, we will describe the flow category structure in a more <span id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ad hoc</span> way, without specifying an underlying category of stratified objects. Define a “product” <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{B}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{B}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> via the diagram</p>
<table id="S16.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 24.53438pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-20.89206pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\widetilde{B}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{rq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 49.8pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.19446pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 49.8pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\widetilde{B}_{pq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 59.84712pt\raise-24.19446pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-24.53438pt\raise-31.52777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{B_{pr}\times B_{rq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 26.1136pt\raise-38.73111pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.23114pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\zeta_{prq}^{B}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 48.53438pt\raise-31.52777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 48.53438pt\raise-31.52777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{B_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-63.559517781896446px" height="74.24" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="33.95 63.56 132.41 74.24" width="132.41"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 33.94821924969948 74.24476616145401) translate(33.95,0)"> <g transform="translate(-28.91,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.95" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="49.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 28.908363892294087 -0.27673578005007266 L 28.908363892294087 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(68.91,0)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 28.908363892294087 -0.27673578005007266 L 68.90826491179993 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 68.90826491179993 -0.27673578005007266 L 68.90826491179993 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(0,-33.48)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.47787188018888 L 0.27673578005007266 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.47787188018888 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.47787188018888" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(68.91,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.41em;--ltx-fo-height:0.72em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.95" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.99)" width="19.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 82.53372802565467 -11.569253138458645 L 83.0871995857548 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(82.81,0) translate(0,-33.48)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 82.53372802565467 -33.47787188018888 L 83.0871995857548 -11.569253138458645" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 82.53372802565467 -33.47787188018888 L 83.0871995857548 -33.47787188018888" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(-33.95,0) translate(0,-43.63) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.31em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="59.59"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 33.94824036328612 -43.90171294359477 L 33.94824036328612 -43.348241383494624" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(36.13,0) translate(0,-53.59) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.09)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.48em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.9)" width="20.54"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">ζ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.710em">q</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">B</mi></msubsup></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(67.16,0) translate(0,-43.63)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 33.94824036328612 -43.90171294359477 L 67.15701958178748 -43.348241383494624" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 67.15701958178748 -43.90171294359477 L 67.15701958178748 -43.348241383494624" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(67.16,0) translate(0,-43.63) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.66em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="23"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vbox{\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\kern 24.53438pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;\cr&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-20.89206pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\widetilde{B}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{rq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 49.8pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-24.19446pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 49.8pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{\widetilde{B}_{pq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 59.84712pt\raise-24.19446pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern-24.53438pt\raise-31.52777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{B_{pr}\times B_{rq}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 26.1136pt\raise-38.73111pt\hbox{{}\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise-2.23114pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\zeta_{prq}^{B}}$}}}\kern 3.0pt}}}}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 48.53438pt\raise-31.52777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\lx@xy@droprule}}{\hbox{\kern 48.53438pt\raise-31.52777pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{B_{pq}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which we require to be a pullback. The “product” universal curves also be defined as a pullback, which admits a domain map</p>
<table id="S16.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{C}_{rq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{rq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{C}_{rq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{rq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now suppose we are in Situation <a href="#Thmsituationf3" title="Situation Flow(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(iii)</span></a> where <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a relativley smooth AMS lift of the Floer flow category <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> enriched in <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each pair of <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq q</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="S16.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pq}\to\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">be the pullback of <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\to B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\to B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then one can define similarly <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{V}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{V}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> and corresponding maps</p>
<table id="S16.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{V}_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}\widetilde{V}_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pr}\boxtimes\widetilde{V}_{rq}\to\partial^{prq}\widetilde{V}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Denote</p>
<table id="S16.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q}:=\widetilde{V}_{pr_{1}}\boxtimes\cdots\boxtimes\widetilde{V}_{r_{l}q}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q}:=\widetilde{V}_{pr_{1}}\boxtimes\cdots\boxtimes\widetilde{V}_{r_{l}q},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">which is well-defined due to the associativity assumption of compositions of the flow category. Notice that there is also a corresponding stratum</p>
<table id="S16.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q}\widetilde{V}_{pq}\subseteq\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q}\widetilde{V}_{pq}\subseteq\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">which contains <math id="S16.SS3.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pr_{1}\cdots r_{l}q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S16.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">16.3.2. </span>The construction of the normal complex structure</h5>

<div id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">—<span id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The family of Cauchy–Riemann operators</span>—Then we would like to build a family of Fredholm operators indexed by <math id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>. The construction appears to depend on <math id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> but the resulting normal complex structure does not. Notice that for each <math id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, there are a pair of Banach spaces</p>
<table id="S16.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S16.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{1}:=\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(C_{\widetilde{\phi}},\widetilde{u}^{*}TX),\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{1}:=\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}(C_{\widetilde{\phi}},\widetilde{u}^{*}TX),\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}:=L^{\tau}(C_{\widetilde{\phi}},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes\widetilde{u}^{*}TX)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}:=L^{\tau}(C_{\widetilde{\phi}},\Lambda^{0,1}\otimes\widetilde{u}^{*}TX).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We regard them as “vector bundles” over <math id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> only in a set-theoretic sense, denoted by</p>
<table id="S16.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S16.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{1}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{1}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ {\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">However, we keep in mind that the induced index-theoretic constructions over the finite-dimensional moduli spaces is nevertheless well-defined as topological objects, and we can perform gluing constructions over the nodal locus to make sense of them.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We give an <span id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ad hoc</span> construction of a family of Cauchy–Riemann operators between these spaces. First we construct a family of cut-off functions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16.7</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist a collection of <math id="S16.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant cut-off functions</span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi_{pq}:{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{pq}\to[0,1]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}:{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{pq}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all pairs of objects <math id="S16.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq q</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S16.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following conditions.</span></p>
<ol id="S16.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S16.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S16.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S16.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on components to the right of </span><math id="S16.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S16.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\chi}_{pq}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\chi}_{pq}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> on components to the left of </span><math id="S16.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S16.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">On </span><math id="S16.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\widetilde{\phi}}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S16.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="S16.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\ll 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\ll 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S16.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\chi}_{pq}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\chi}_{pq}=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="S16.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\gg 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≫</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\gg 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> where </span><math id="S16.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a cylindrical coordinate.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S16.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S16.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is collared.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S16.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> respects the flow category structure. Namely, whenever </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\phi}\in{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{pr}\boxtimes{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\phi}\in{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{pr}\boxtimes{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, if the marked point is on the </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="pr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">pr</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-section then on this part </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> coincides with </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; if the marked point is on the </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rq</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-section then on this section </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> coincides with </span><math id="S16.I2.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S16.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S16.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> respect the rigidification. </span><math id="S16.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> does not vary with the normal direction near </span><math id="S16.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{pr}\boxtimes{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{pr}\boxtimes{}_{\lfloor}\widetilde{C}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> inside </span><math id="S16.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial^{prq}\widetilde{C}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{prq}\widetilde{C}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I2.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS3.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">An inductive construction similar to the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma14" title="Theorem N. ‣ 8.2. FOP perturbations on flow categories, multimodules, and homotopies ‣ 8. FOP Perturbations ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">N</span></a>, which is standard at this point.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now for each <math id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the Cauchy–Riemann operator</p>
<table id="S16.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\widetilde{x}}:{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{1}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\widetilde{x}}:{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{1}\to{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">given by the same formula as (<a href="#S16.E3" title="In 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.3</span></a>). We would like to consider the index bundles. Let</p>
<table id="S16.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}\subseteq{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}\subseteq{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">be the subspace of compactly supported smooth sections and let</p>
<table id="S16.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}\to\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS3.SSS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">denote the corresponding “subbundle.”</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 16.8</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An <span id="S16.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">index bundle interpolator</span> over the Kuranishi flow category <math id="S16.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the following items.</p>
<ol id="S16.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S16.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S16.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each object <math id="S16.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a finite-dimensional complex vector space <math id="S16.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{p}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{p}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and a complex-linear map</p>
<table id="S16.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{p}:R_{p}^{+}\to\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{p}:R_{p}^{+}\to\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is transverse to the image of <math id="S16.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. We require that <math id="S16.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> only depends on the <math id="S16.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>-orbit, i.e., the underlying uncapped orbit <math id="S16.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote</p>
<table id="S16.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{p}^{-}={\rm ker}(\nu_{p}\oplus D_{p})\subseteq R_{p}^{+}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ker</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{p}^{-}={\rm ker}(\nu_{p}\oplus D_{p})\subseteq R_{p}^{+}\oplus\widetilde{W}^{1,\tau}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I3.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is only a real vector space.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S16.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S16.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq q</annotation></semantics></math>, a finite-dimensional Hermitian representations <math id="S16.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S16.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S16.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant complex-linear bundle maps over <math id="S16.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S16.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}:\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+}\to\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}:\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+}\to\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pq}^{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S16.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each triple <math id="S16.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, a complex-linear map</p>
<table id="S16.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\iota}_{prq}:W_{pr}\oplus R_{r}^{+}\oplus W_{rq}\to W_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ι</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\iota}_{prq}:W_{pr}\oplus R_{r}^{+}\oplus W_{rq}\to W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I3.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is equivariant with respect to the group homomorphism <math id="S16.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\to G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pr}\times G_{rq}\to G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S16.Thmthm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">They are required to satisfy the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S16.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S16.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S16.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(The original index bundle)</span> For each <math id="S16.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, with respect to the natural decomposition</p>
<table id="S16.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}\cong\Omega^{0,1}_{c}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega^{0,1}_{c}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}\cong\Omega^{0,1}_{c}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{p}^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega^{0,1}_{c}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I4.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we have</p>
<table id="S16.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}\nu_{p}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{array}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}\nu_{p}&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\end{array}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S16.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(The complex index bundle)</span> For each <math id="S16.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\partial^{+}\widetilde{B}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}=(\widetilde{\phi},\widetilde{u},e,F)\in\partial^{+}\widetilde{B}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, with respect to the natural decomposition</p>
<table id="S16.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}\cong\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{q}^{*}TX)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{\widetilde{x}}^{0}\cong\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)\oplus\Omega_{c}^{0,1}({\mathbb{R}}\times S^{1},u_{q}^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we have</p>
<table id="S16.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}0&amp;\nu_{\widetilde{x}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\nu_{q}\end{array}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>ν</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pq}=\left[\begin{array}[]{ccc}0&amp;\nu_{\widetilde{x}}&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\nu_{q}\end{array}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I4.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S16.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\widetilde{x}}:W_{pq}\to\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\widetilde{x}}:W_{pq}\to\Omega_{c}^{0,1}(C_{\phi},u^{*}TX)</annotation></semantics></math> is a complex-linear map.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S16.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Flow category structure I)</span> The above conditions imply that <math id="S16.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{pr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{pr}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S16.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{rq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math> determine a bundle map</p>
<table id="S16.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{prq}:(\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pr}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{r}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{rq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+})|_{\widetilde{V}_{prq}}\to\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pr}^{0}\boxplus\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{rq}^{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>⊞</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>̊</mo></mover><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{prq}:(\underline{\smash{R}}_{p}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{pr}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{r}^{+}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{rq}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{q}^{+})|_{\widetilde{V}_{prq}}\to\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{pr}^{0}\boxplus\mathring{\mathcal{E}}_{rq}^{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I4.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We require that the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S16.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
