</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16.13</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.Thmthm13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given index bundle interpolators for <math id="S16.Thmthm13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an index bundle interpolator for <math id="S16.Thmthm13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Induction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Then we obtain a family of continuous real <math id="S16.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundles</p>
<table id="S16.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS4.p11.2" class="ltx_p">whose fiber over <math id="S16.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is the kernel of the operator</p>
<table id="S16.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\nu}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus D_{\widetilde{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\nu}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus D_{\widetilde{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS4.p11.3" class="ltx_p">We examine its restrictions to specific lower strata. By one of the conditions of Definition <a href="#S16.Thmthm12" title="Definition 16.12. ‣ 16.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.12</span></a>, one has</p>
<table id="S16.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{-}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{+}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>T</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>vt</mi></msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{-}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{+}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS4.p11.4" class="ltx_p">which is a stabilization of the original vertical tangent bundle. On the other hand,</p>
<table id="S16.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{+}\oplus I_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{-}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{+}\oplus I_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS4.p11.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S16.SS4.p11.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is fiberwise the kernel of the complex-linear operator</p>
<table id="S16.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{\widetilde{x}}\oplus D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS4.p11.6" class="ltx_p">Since both the negative and positive inclusions</p>
<table id="S16.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{\pm}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>±</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{\pm}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS4.p11.7" class="ltx_p">are equivariant homotopy equivalences, the above two restriction bundles are isomorphic. One needs to choose a compatible system of isomorphisms in order to obtain a relative normal complex structure on the Kuranishi multimodule.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We consider certain codimension 1 strata of the thickenings.</p>
<ol id="S16.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S16.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S16.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}&lt;q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}&lt;q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is a corresponding relative space <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to\widetilde{B}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊠</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\to\widetilde{B}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\boxtimes\widetilde{B}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that there are further lower strata of the form</p>
<table id="S16.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\times\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\times\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I9.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">corresponding to where the <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th marked point is on the very left,</p>
<table id="S16.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\times\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\times\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I9.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where all the marked points are on the very right. Notice that here we have the usual direct product but not <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxtimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊠</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxtimes</annotation></semantics></math>. There is also an intermediate strata</p>
<table id="S16.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial^{0}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\times\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial^{0}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}\times\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}q_{j}p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.I9.i1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">corresponding to configurations where the <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th marked point is at the breaking at <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and all other marked points are on the very left. Notice that all these strata are isomorphic with <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that, the bundle <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, when restricted to <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, contains a subbudnle <math id="S16.I9.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{j-1}(p_{j}q_{j})p_{j+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> coming from the index bundle interpolators, whose restrictions to the above three strata are canonically identified with</p>
