<div id="S16.Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S16.Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16.14</span></span><span id="S16.Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S16.Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.Thmthm14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given bundle isomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S16.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S16.Ex107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \widetilde{I}_{p_{j}q_{j}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}}\cong\widetilde{I}_{p_{j}q_{j}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}},\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \widetilde{I}_{p_{j}q_{j}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}}\cong\widetilde{I}_{p_{j}q_{j}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{j}q_{j}}},\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S16.Ex107.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ \widetilde{I}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}}\cong\widetilde{I}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>−</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>≅</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mo>+</mo></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ \widetilde{I}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}}\cong\widetilde{I}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p^{\prime}q^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.Thmthm14.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm14.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfying conditions listed in Lemma <a href="#S16.Thmthm10" title="Lemma 16.10. ‣ 16.3.2. The construction of the normal complex structure ‣ 16.3. Proof of Theorem ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.10</span></a>, there exists a system of <math id="S16.Thmthm14.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant real vector bundle isomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}\cong\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">≅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}\cong\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.Thmthm14.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.Thmthm14.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">satisfying the following conditions.</span></p>
<ol id="S16.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S16.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S16.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="S16.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}&lt;q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}&lt;q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I10.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the following diagram commutes</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S16.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When </span><math id="S16.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}&lt;p^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S16.I10.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the following diagram commutes.</span></p>
<table id="S16.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S16.Ex109.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="72.26" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-61.267152339966444px" version="1.1" viewBox="90.06 61.27 442.65 72.26" width="442.65"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 90.06008825411651 72.25989899530407) translate(0,3.54) translate(90.06,0)"><g transform="translate(-90.06,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.42em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.68em;font-size:10pt;" height="19.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="171.82"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S16.Ex109.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}\times\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}\times\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -17.065605352540818 L 0.27673578005007266 -17.065605352540818" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -17.065605352540818" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M -0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088 L 0.27673578005007266 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 90.06010936770315 -0.27673578005007266 L 90.06010936770315 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(164.78,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 90.06010936770315 -0.27673578005007266 L 164.77988900131453 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 164.77988900131453 -0.27673578005007266 L 164.77988900131453 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(164.78,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.97em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.68em;font-size:10pt;" height="19.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="179.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S16.Ex109.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}\times\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">×</mo><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}\times\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 258.4069276954584 -17.065605352540818 L 258.96039925555857 -17.065605352540818" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(258.69,0) translate(0,-33.21)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -2.77 6.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 258.4069276954584 -33.208800332088 L 258.96039925555857 -17.065605352540818" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 258.4069276954584 -33.208800332088 L 258.96039925555857 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(-67.76,0) translate(0,-44.2) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.19em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.68em;font-size:10pt;" height="19.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="127.21"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S16.Ex109.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{-}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 67.75675101020911 -44.4782827674757 L 67.75675101020911 -43.924811207375555" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(189.01,0) translate(0,-44.2)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 67.75675101020911 -44.4782827674757 L 189.0050904688473 -43.924811207375555" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 189.0050904688473 -44.4782827674757 L 189.0050904688473 -43.924811207375555" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(189.01,0) translate(0,-44.2) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.68em;font-size:10pt;" height="19.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="131.06"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S16.Ex109.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{\widetilde{I}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}|_{\partial^{+}\widetilde{V}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S16.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I10.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The isomorphisms are collared.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S16.I10.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S16.I10.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.I10.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.I10.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The isomorphisms respect the rigidifications.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S16.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S16.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S16.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Induction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Now using the identifications of the extended index bundles over the negative and positive strata, one obtains the equivariant bundle isomorphisms</p>
<table id="S16.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{-}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{+}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{+}\oplus I_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{-}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>T</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>vt</mi></msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≅</mo><mo movablelimits="false">⨁</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{-}\oplus\underline{\smash{W}}_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{+}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}\cong\bigoplus_{j=1}^{m}\underline{\smash{R}}_{p_{j}}^{+}\oplus I_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{p^{\prime}}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS4.p14.2" class="ltx_p">In particular, this gives an equivariant normal complex structure (see Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm23" title="Definition 3.23. ‣ 3.3.3. Normally complex Kuranishi spaces ‣ 3.3. Stable complex structures and normal complex structures ‣ 3. Kuranishi Spaces ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.23</span></a>) of the vertical tangent bundle <math id="S16.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>vt</mi></msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the chart <math id="S16.SS4.p14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="K_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes an object of <math id="S16.SS4.p14.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditions of Lemma <a href="#S16.Thmthm14" title="Lemma 16.14. ‣ 16.4. Proof of Theorem ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.14</span></a> imply that the structural maps are also morphisms in this category. Hence one obtains a lift of the Kuranishi flow category <math id="S16.SS4.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S16.SS4.p14.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>. This finishes the proof of Theorem <a href="#S16.Thmthm3" title="Theorem 16.3. ‣ 16.1. Main statements about normal complex structures ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S16.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">16.5. </span>Orientations</h4>

<div id="S16.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We explain how to obtain coherent orientations on the AMS construction. We give orientations on the tangent bundles of the domain moduli spaces as well as the vertical tangent bundles. After the stable smoothing to be done in the next section, they induce coherent orientations on the AMS lifts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first look at the operator <math id="S16.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> given by (<a href="#S16.E1" title="In 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.1</span></a>). Its Fredholm index is congruent (mod <math id="S16.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>) to the cohomological degree of the periodic orbit <math id="S16.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S16.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p|</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S16.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> be its real determinant line.</p>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the flow category case. For each pair of objects <math id="S16.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math>, one can use the 1-parameter family of operators (<a href="#S16.E3" title="In 16.2.1. A complex-linear Cauchy–Riemann operator and an interpolation ‣ 16.2. Abouzaid–Blumberg’s construction for a single moduli space ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.3</span></a>) to obtain an interpolation; in particular an isomorphism between determinant lines</p>
<table id="S16.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det D_{p}\otimes\det D_{u}\cong\det(D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus D_{q})\cong\det D_{q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det D_{p}\otimes\det D_{u}\cong\det(D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}\oplus D_{q})\cong\det D_{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The last isomorphism comes from the fact that <math id="S16.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{u}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex. We may regard the orientation of the moduli space as the family of isomorphismss on the determinant lines</p>
<table id="S16.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det D_{u}:\det D_{p}\to\det D_{q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.111em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det D_{u}:\det D_{p}\to\det D_{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">In terms of the AMS lift, this means one obtains a family of isomorphisms (well-defined up to homotopy)</p>
<table id="S16.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{pq}:\det D_{p}\to\det D_{q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.111em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{pq}:\det D_{p}\to\det D_{q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS5.p3.4" class="ltx_p">over the thickened moduli <math id="S16.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. The construction implies</p>
<table id="S16.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{rq}\circ\sigma_{pr}=\sigma_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{rq}\circ\sigma_{pr}=\sigma_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S16.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S16.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The case with multimodules and homotopies are essentially the same. For a Floer multimodule <math id="S16.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, using the interpolation constructed before, one obtains a family of isomorphisms</p>
<table id="S16.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:\bigotimes_{i=1}^{m}\det D_{p_{i}}\to\det D_{p^{\prime}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mo movablelimits="false">⨂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}:\bigotimes_{i=1}^{m}\det D_{p_{i}}\to\det D_{p^{\prime}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">By considering indices, one has that</p>
<table id="S16.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=(-1)^{(\sum_{j&lt;i}|p_{j}|)(|p_{i}|-|q_{i}|)}\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\circ\sigma_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=(-1)^{(\sum_{j&lt;i}|p_{j}|)(|p_{i}|-|q_{i}|)}\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\circ\sigma_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS5.p4.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S16.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S16.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=\sigma_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\circ\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}=\sigma_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\circ\sigma_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S16.SS5.p4.4" class="ltx_p">The case of homotopy is similar and we omit it.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S17" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">17. </span>Stable Smoothings</h3>

<div id="S17.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We proceed with the last step of constructing the AMS lifts. The original argument of such abstract smoothing of moduli spaces was contained in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>. The inductive argument in the setting of Floer theories was first systematically discussed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S17.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">17.1. </span>Main results about stable smoothings</h4>

<div id="S17.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the construction we will frequently stabilize thickened moduli spaces obtained in the AMS construction. To simplify the discussion, we always stabilize by trivial complex vector bundles. We make the following formal definition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17.1</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The category <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> has objects being <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K,R)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> is a Kuranishi space and <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite-dimensional unitary complex representation of <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. A strict embedding from <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K_{1},R_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K_{1},R_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K_{2},R_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K_{2},R_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a strict embedding of Kuranishi spaces <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and an <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant isometric linear embedding <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}^{R}:R_{1}\to R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}^{R}:R_{1}\to R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Morphisms of <math id="S17.Thmthm1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> are unitary conjugacy classes of strict embeddings.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, one can consider the collared and rigidified versions. Then there are two natural functors from <math id="S17.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math>: the first is to forget the representation <math id="S17.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>; the other is to take the stabilization by <math id="S17.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>. What we would consider is the version</p>
<table id="S17.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for collared, rigidified, relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17.2</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S17.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stabilizer</span> of a flow category/multimodule/homotopy enriched in <math id="S17.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lift to <math id="S17.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 17.3</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the AMS construction, a stabilizer can be viewed as adding trivial pieces to the thickening data.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that there are two natural functors from <math id="S17.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>. The first is to forget the stabilizer. The second is to stabilize each Kuranishi space by the corresponding trivial vector bundle via the vertical stabilization (see Definition <a href="#S15.Thmthm27" title="Definition 15.27 (Relative spaces). ‣ 15.4.1. Relative spaces and relative smooth structures ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.27</span></a>). We often freely switch between the stabilizer, which is a system of representations, and the corresponding vertical stabilization, viewed as total space of the corresponding product equivariant vector bundles.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17.4</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S17.Thmthm4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">smoothing</span> of a flow category/multimodule/homotopy enriched in <math id="S17.Thmthm4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lift to <math id="S17.Thmthm4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S17.Thmthm4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stable smoothing</span> of a flow category/multimodule/homotopy enriched in <math id="S17.Thmthm4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a lift to <math id="S17.Thmthm4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf Kur}}_{\rm rig}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and a smoothing of the corresponding stabilization.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 17.5</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.Thmthm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.Thmthm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Stable Smoothing Theorem)</span></p>
<ol id="S17.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S17.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationf1" title="Situation Flow(i). ‣ 9.2. Floer flow category ‣ 9. Geometric Flow Categories ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(i)</span></a><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, suppose </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a relatively smooth AMS lift of </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> subject to a certain outercollaring width. Then there exists a stable smoothing of </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. In other words, there exists a vertical stabilization </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a smoothing of </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. We still denote the flow category enriched in </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> by </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and call it an </span><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AMS stable smoothing</span><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S17.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S17.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationm1" title="Situation Module(i). ‣ 10.2. Multimodules from smooth domains ‣ 10. Geometric Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(i)</span></a><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, suppose </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\cdots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are relatively smooth AMS lifts and </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a relatively smooth AMS lift as a multimodule over </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Suppose </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are AMS stable smoothings of </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> respectively. Then there exists a class of stable smoothings of </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as multimodules over </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. These stable smoothings are called </span><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AMS stable smoothings</span><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S17.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S17.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationh3" title="Situation Homotopy(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\cdots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\cdots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be AMS stable smoothings of the relatively smooth AMS lifts </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Let </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be AMS stable smoothings of </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> resp. </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as multimodules over </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then the relatively smooth AMS lift </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> has a class of stable smoothings as a homotopy from </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Such stable smoothings are called </span><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AMS stable smoothings</span><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S17.I1.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I1.i3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S17.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">17.2. </span>Preliminaries</h4>

<section id="S17.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">17.2.1. </span>Microbundles</h5>

<div id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that a <span id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">microbundle</span> of rank <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> over a topological space <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a topological space <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> together with two structural maps <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:{\mathscr{F}}\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:{\mathscr{F}}\to M</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i:M\to{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i:M\to{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\circ i={\rm Id}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\circ i={\rm Id}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and such that near the image of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, locally <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>-bundle. Any real vector bundle <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\to M</annotation></semantics></math> together with the bundle projection and the zero section induces a microbundle <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is a topological manifold, then its tangent microbundle <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math> has the total space <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\times M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\times M</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> the projection onto the first factor and <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> the diagonal embedding of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">morphism</span> of microbundles over <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a germ of continuous maps from a neighborhood of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i(M)\subseteq{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i(M)\subseteq{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> which commutes with the structural maps. A morphism is called an <span id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">isomorphism</span> if it can be represented by a homeomorphism. An <span id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">isotopy</span> of microbundle isomorphisms from <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{0}:{\mathscr{F}}\to{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{0}:{\mathscr{F}}\to{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}:{\mathscr{F}}\to{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}:{\mathscr{F}}\to{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a microbundle isomorphism from <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathscr{F}}\to\tilde{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathscr{F}}\to\tilde{\mathscr{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\times[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\times[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> whose restriction to <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\times\{i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\times\{i\}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (as germs) for <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0,1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, a <span id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">vector bundle reduction</span> of a microbundle <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}\to M</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a vector bundle <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\to M</annotation></semantics></math> and a microbundle isomorphism <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. When a topological manifold <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with a smooth structure, denoted by <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, then there is a vector bundle reduction <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(TM_{\alpha})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(TM_{\alpha})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math>: a concrete choice could be the exponential map associated to a Riemannian metric. The isotopy class of such a vector bundle reduction is canonical. Hence it is a necessary condition for a topological manifold to admit a smooth structure that its tangent microbundle admits a vector bundle reduction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">All the above notions admit equivariant extensions with respect to actions by compact Lie groups. In particular, when a topological <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with a smooth structure <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action is smooth, then there is a well-defined isotopy class of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle reduction <math id="S17.SS2.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(TM_{\alpha})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(TM_{\alpha})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 17.6</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We need the notion of smooth microbundles over smooth manifolds. These are microbundles whose total spaces and structural maps are all in the <math id="S17.Thmthm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> category. One can also define smooth microbundle maps and smooth vector bundle reductions. Equivariant versions can be formulated as well. For example, when <math id="S17.Thmthm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is already a smooth manifold, the tangent microbundle is smooth and any vector bundle reduction of <math id="S17.Thmthm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math> using a smooth Riemannian metric is smooth.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S17.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">17.2.2. </span>Stable <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothings</h5>

<div id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we recall notions about equivariant smoothings. Let <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a topological manifold with an action by a compact Lie group <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. A <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-smoothing</span> of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth structure <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> such that the <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action is smooth. Two <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothings <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are called <span id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">equivalent</span> if the identity map <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\alpha_{0}}\to M_{\alpha_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\alpha_{0}}\to M_{\alpha_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a diffeomorphism; they are called <span id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">isotopic</span> if the identity map is homotopic through <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant homeomorphisms to a diffeomorphism. More generally, a <span id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stable <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing</span> of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> consists of an orthogonal <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing on <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\times R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\times R</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that given any stable <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M\times R)_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M\times R)_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and any other orthogonal <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the product smooth structure <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M\times R)_{\alpha}\times R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M\times R)_{\alpha}\times R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> gives another stable <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing. Two stable <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothings <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M\times R_{1})_{\alpha_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M\times R_{1})_{\alpha_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M\times R_{2})_{\alpha_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M\times R_{2})_{\alpha_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> are <span id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stably isotopic</span> if there exist orthogonal <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representations <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}^{\prime},R_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}^{\prime},R_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}\oplus R_{1}^{\prime}\cong R_{2}\oplus R_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}\oplus R_{1}^{\prime}\cong R_{2}\oplus R_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as orthogonal <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representations and such that the two <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothings <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M\times R_{1})_{\alpha_{1}}\times R_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M\times R_{1})_{\alpha_{1}}\times R_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M\times R_{2})_{\alpha_{2}}\times R_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M\times R_{2})_{\alpha_{2}}\times R_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\times R_{1}\times R_{1}^{\prime}=M\times R_{2}\times R_{2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\times R_{1}\times R_{1}^{\prime}=M\times R_{2}\times R_{2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are isotopic.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that given a <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, there is an induced isotopy class of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle reductions <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(TM_{\alpha})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(TM_{\alpha})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math>. In view of stable smoothings, one also need to define the notion of stable isotopy of stable vector bundle reductions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17.7</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, Page 300]</cite>
Let <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}\to M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}\to M</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-microbundle. A <span id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stable <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reduction</span> of <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and an orthogonal <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representation <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> together with a <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-microbundle isomorphism</p>
<table id="S17.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:F_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{F}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{\mu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:F_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{F}}\oplus\underline{\smash{R}}_{\mu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Two stable <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reductions <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}:(F_{i})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{F}}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{i})_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}:(F_{i})_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{F}}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{i})_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0,1</annotation></semantics></math>, are called <span id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">stably isotopic</span> if there exist orthogonal <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-representations <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}^{\prime},R_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}^{\prime},R_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\oplus R_{0}^{\prime}\cong R_{1}\oplus R_{1}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\oplus R_{0}^{\prime}\cong R_{1}\oplus R_{1}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and the stabilizations <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{0}\oplus{\rm Id}_{\underline{\smash{R}}_{0}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{0}\oplus{\rm Id}_{\underline{\smash{R}}_{0}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{1}\oplus{\rm Id}_{\underline{\smash{R}}_{1}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Id</mi><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{1}\oplus{\rm Id}_{\underline{\smash{R}}_{1}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> are isotopic vector bundle reductions of <math id="S17.Thmthm7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{F}}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{0})_{\mu}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{0}^{\prime})_{\mu}\cong{\mathscr{F}}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{1})_{\mu}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{1}^{\prime})_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℱ</mi><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><munder accentunder="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{F}}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{0})_{\mu}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{0}^{\prime})_{\mu}\cong{\mathscr{F}}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{1})_{\mu}\oplus(\underline{\smash{R}}_{1}^{\prime})_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 17.8</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the above discussions, we can replace “orthogonal representations” by “unitary representations” to suit our purpose. Any orthogonal representation can be stabilized to a unitary representation.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now given any stable <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M\times R)_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M\times R)_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, there is an isotopy class of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reductions <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(M\times R)_{\alpha}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}(M\times R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(M\times R)_{\alpha}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}(M\times R)</annotation></semantics></math>. The restriction of this reduction to <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\times\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\times\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> gives a stable isotopy class of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reductions of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math>. Lashof’s theorem says that this association has an inverse.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 17.9</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">[</span><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a><span id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">]</span></cite><span id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Let <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a topological <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold with finitely many orbit types. Then the above map which sends each stable isotopy class of stable <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothings to a stable isotopy class of <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reductions of <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible. In particular, if <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M</annotation></semantics></math> admits a <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reduction, then <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> admits a stable <math id="S17.Thmthm9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S17.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">17.2.3. </span>Micro-connections</h5>

<div id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:V\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:V\to B</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant relatively smooth manifold such that <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold. Then there is a well-defined <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-microbundle over <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S17.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B\oplus{\mathscr{T}}^{\rm vt}_{\mu}V." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B\oplus{\mathscr{T}}^{\rm vt}_{\mu}V.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To facilitate the stable smoothing of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to identify the above microbundle with the tangent microbundle of <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that there are natural microbundle maps</p>
<table id="S17.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}^{\rm vt}_{\mu}V\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V\to\pi^{*}{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}^{\rm vt}_{\mu}V\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V\to\pi^{*}{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence such an identification can be regarded as a microbundle version of connections.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17.10</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.Thmthm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S17.Thmthm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V/B</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S17.Thmthm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant topological submersion. A <span id="S17.Thmthm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">micro-connection</span> is a <math id="S17.Thmthm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant microbundle map <math id="S17.Thmthm10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mu}:{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mu}:{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<ol id="S17.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S17.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The restriction of <math id="S17.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity map.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S17.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by a germ of the map <math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\Delta^{+}(V)\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\Delta^{+}(V)\to V</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b,b^{\prime})\in(\pi\times\pi)(\Delta^{+}(V))\subseteq B\times B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b,b^{\prime})\in(\pi\times\pi)(\Delta^{+}(V))\subseteq B\times B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\pi^{-1}(b)\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\pi^{-1}(b)\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, the restriction of <math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{+}(V)\cap(\{p\}\times\pi^{-1}(b^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{+}(V)\cap(\{p\}\times\pi^{-1}(b^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math> is a homeomorphism onto an open neighborhood of <math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p,p)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S17.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p\}\times\pi^{-1}(b))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p\}\times\pi^{-1}(b))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that a micro-connection induces a microbundle isomorphism <math id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M\cong\pi^{*}{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B\oplus{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}M\cong\pi^{*}{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B\oplus{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}M</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 17.11</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant closed subset and <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant open neighborhood of <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> be another <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant closed set. Suppose <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mu}:{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}U\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mu}:{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}U\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}U</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant micro-connection. Then there exists a <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant open neighborhood <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\cup D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\cup D</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant micro-connection <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mu}^{\prime}:{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}W\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mu}^{\prime}:{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}W\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}W</annotation></semantics></math> which coincides with <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S17.Thmthm11.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is a restatement of the extension lemma <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Lemma 4.24]</cite> and a relative version of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Proposition 4.25]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S17.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">17.3. </span>Pre-smoothed relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces</h4>

<div id="S17.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To describe the structures one needs to perform the stable smoothing, we enhance the category of relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces to include various specific add-ons.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17.12</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.Thmthm12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S17.Thmthm12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V/B,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V/B,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> be an object of <math id="S17.Thmthm12.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="S17.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S17.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">pre-smoothing</span> on <math id="S17.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> consists of</p>
<ol id="S17.I3.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant Riemannian metric <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{TB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{TB}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant metric <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{T^{\rm vt}V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{T^{\rm vt}V}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A micro-connection <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S17.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V/B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A pre-smoothing is called <span id="S17.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">collared</span> if for each stratum <math id="S17.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}/B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}/B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds.</p>
<ol id="S17.I3.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Near <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{TB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{TB}</annotation></semantics></math> is the product of <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{TB_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{TB_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the standard metric on the collar.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Near <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{T^{\rm vt}V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{T^{\rm vt}V}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant in collar coordinates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Near <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> factors as</p>
<table id="S17.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S17.Ex5.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="23.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-11.569253138458645px" version="1.1" viewBox="18.43 11.57 196.18 23.24" width="196.18"><g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 18.430957659590337 23.240041515054223) translate(0,3.46) translate(18.43,0)"><g transform="translate(-18.43,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="28.56"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S17.Ex5.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 18.430957659590337 -0.27673578005007266 L 18.430957659590337 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(51.64,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 18.430957659590337 -0.27673578005007266 L 51.639757991678344 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 51.639757991678344 -0.27673578005007266 L 51.639757991678344 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(51.64,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.63em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.41" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="36.45"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S17.Ex5.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V_{\alpha}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V_{\alpha}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 96.387048966495 -0.27673578005007266 L 96.387048966495 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(129.6,0)"><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -6.92 2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -6.92 -2.77" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path></g><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 96.387048966495 -0.27673578005007266 L 129.595849298583 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 129.595849298583 -0.27673578005007266 L 129.595849298583 0.27673578005007266" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path><g transform="translate(129.6,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.88em;--ltx-fo-height:0.79em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.94" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.98)" width="39.86"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S17.Ex5.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textstyle{{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V_{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textstyle{{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V_{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the first arrow is induced from the collar structure and the second arrow is the restriction of the micro-connection on the stratum <math id="S17.I3.i2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\alpha}/B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\alpha}/B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A pre-smoothed Kuranishi space is a relatively smooth Kuranishi space equipped with a pre-smoothing.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A stabilization of a pre-smoothed Kuranishi space <math id="S17.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> by a trivial <math id="S17.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant disk bundle <math id="S17.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=D^{\rm hor}\oplus D^{\rm vt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>hor</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=D^{\rm hor}\oplus D^{\rm vt}</annotation></semantics></math> is the stabilized Kuranishi space <math id="S17.I3.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Stab}_{D}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Stab}_{D}K</annotation></semantics></math> together with the naturally induced pre-smoothing (where <math id="S17.I3.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\rm hor}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>hor</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\rm hor}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.I3.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\rm vt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\rm vt}</annotation></semantics></math> are equipped with linear metrics).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S17.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidified strict embedding</span> of pre-smoothed Kuranishi spaces from <math id="S17.I3.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S17.I3.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a rigidified strict embedding <math id="S17.I3.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ι</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota_{21}:K_{1}\to K_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (with normal disk bundle <math id="S17.I3.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{21}=D_{21}^{\rm hor}\oplus D_{21}^{\rm vt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>hor</mi></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>21</mn><mi>vt</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{21}=D_{21}^{\rm hor}\oplus D_{21}^{\rm vt}</annotation></semantics></math> equipped with the direct sum of linear metrics) such that the induced germ of strict open embedding preserves the pre-smoothings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S17.I3.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rigidified embedding</span> is a unitary conjugacy class of rigidified strict embeddings. Let <math id="S17.I3.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> be the regular stratification category whose objects are collared, pre-smoothed Kuranishi spaces and whose morphisms are rigidified embeddings. There is an obvious forgetful functor</p>
<table id="S17.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}\to{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I3.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(7)</span> 
<div id="S17.I3.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.I3.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S17.I3.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">pre-smoothing</span> of a flow category/multimodule/homotopy enriched in <math id="S17.I3.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lift to <math id="S17.I3.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 17.13</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S17.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S17.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationf3" title="Situation Flow(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, the relatively smooth AMS lift </span><math id="S17.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> admits a pre-smoothing.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S17.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationm3" title="Situation Module(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, suppose the AMS lifts </span><math id="S17.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of the involved Floer flow categories are equipped with pre-smoothings, then </span><math id="S17.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> admits a pre-smoothing as a multimodule enriched in </span><math id="S17.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S17.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationh3" title="Situation Homotopy(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, suppose the AMS lifts </span><math id="S17.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are equipped with pre-smoothings so </span><math id="S17.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S17.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are multimodules over the tuple of pre-smoothed flow categories, then </span><math id="S17.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> admits a pre-smoothing as a homotopy enriched in </span><math id="S17.I4.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I4.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S17.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The collared and rigidified structure of the relatively smooth AMS lifts allows us to choose invariant horizontal and vertical Riemannian metrics inductively. On the other hand, Lemma <a href="#S17.Thmthm11" title="Lemma 17.11. ‣ 17.2.3. Micro-connections ‣ 17.2. Preliminaries ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.11</span></a> allows us to inductively construct micro-connections.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Once one obtains a pre-smoothed Kuranishi space <math id="S17.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V/B,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V/B,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains a <math id="S17.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reduction of the tangent microbundle. More precisely, the exponential map of <math id="S17.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{TB}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{TB}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a reduction</p>
<table id="S17.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(TB)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(TB)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The vertical exponential map of <math id="S17.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{T^{\rm vt}V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{T^{\rm vt}V}</annotation></semantics></math> induces a reduction</p>
<table id="S17.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T^{\rm vt}V)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi>vt</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T^{\rm vt}V)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}^{\rm vt}V.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Together with the micro-connection, one obtains</p>
<table id="S17.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi^{*}TB\oplus T^{\rm vt}V)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi^{*}TB\oplus T^{\rm vt}V)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Notice that such <math id="S17.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reductions are compatible with morphisms of <math id="S17.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S17.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">17.3.1. </span>Post-smoothed Kuranishi spaces</h5>

<div id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Definition <a href="#S17.Thmthm12" title="Definition 17.12. ‣ 17.3. Pre-smoothed relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.12</span></a> ensures the existence of coherent vector bundle lifts. The next definition is designed to make the stabizers explicit in order to carry out the inductive smoothing construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 17.14</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm14.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V/B,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V/B,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> be an object of <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm pre}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>. A <span id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">post-smoothing</span> on <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothing of <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, a collared smooth <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant vector bundle reduction</p>
<table id="S17.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp:(TV)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒯</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp:(TV)_{\mu}\to{\mathscr{T}}_{\mu}V,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and a collared <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant vector bundle isomorphism</p>
<table id="S17.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV\cong\pi^{*}TB\oplus T^{\rm vt}V" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV\cong\pi^{*}TB\oplus T^{\rm vt}V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.3" class="ltx_p">such that <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>exp</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reduction induced from the pre-smoothing are in the same stable <math id="S17.Thmthm14.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-isotopy class on the interior of each stratum.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now we state the results about constructing stable smoothings. Since we need to constantly stabilize charts, we would like to use the convenient system of unitary representations of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{d}\cong U(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{d}\cong U(d)</annotation></semantics></math> specified by Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm23" title="Proposition 15.23. ‣ 15.3.6. Proof of Proposition ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.23</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 17.15</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S17.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S17.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationf3" title="Situation Flow(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S17.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a pre-smoothed AMS lift of </span><math id="S17.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> provided by Lemma </span><a href="#S17.Thmthm13" title="Lemma 17.13. ‣ 17.3. Pre-smoothed relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.13</span></a><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a stabilization </span><math id="S17.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a post-smoothing of </span><math id="S17.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Each such flow category is called a post-smoothed AMS lift of </span><math id="S17.I5.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S17.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationm3" title="Situation Module(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be pre-smoothed AMS lifts of the involved Floer flow categories. Let </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a pre-smoothed AMS lift of the multimodule </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> provided by Lemma </span><a href="#S17.Thmthm13" title="Lemma 17.13. ‣ 17.3. Pre-smoothed relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.13</span></a><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Suppose </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are post-smoothings of </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a stabilization </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a post-smoothing of it as a multimodule over </span><math id="S17.I5.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S17.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationh3" title="Situation Homotopy(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}^{+},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m}^{+};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}{}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be post-smoothed AMS lifts of the involved flow categories and </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be post-smoothed AMS lifts of the two multimodules </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕏</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Let </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a pre-smoothed AMS lift of the homotopy provided by Lemma </span><a href="#S17.Thmthm13" title="Lemma 17.13. ‣ 17.3. Pre-smoothed relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.13</span></a><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a stabilization </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a post-smoothing of it as a homotopy from </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S17.I5.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I5.i3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS3.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Again, it suffices to demonstrate the argument in the case of flow categories. Recall the system of unitary representations <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{d,\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{d,\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each pair <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, denote <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq,\mu}:=W_{d_{pq},\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq,\mu}:=W_{d_{pq},\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is the integer specified via the choice of integral action. Notice that once we choose a system of positive integers <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="S17.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{pq}&gt;\max\{\mu_{pr},\mu_{rq}\ |\ p&lt;r&lt;q\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}&gt;\max\{\mu_{pr},\mu_{rq}\ |\ p&lt;r&lt;q\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">then one obtains a stabilization <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with each chart <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> vertically stabilized by <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The main claim is that one can choose such a stabilizer together with a post-smoothing of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the condition on stable isotopy classes of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-vector bundle reductions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We construct <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and the post-smoothing inductively. For the base case when <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> has no boundary strata, the existence of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the post-smoothing is a consequence of Lashof’s theorem (Theorem <a href="#S17.Thmthm9" title="Theorem 17.9. ‣ 17.2.2. Stable 𝐺-smoothings ‣ 17.2. Preliminaries ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.9</span></a>), since every finite-dimensional representation of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in a certain <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq,\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq,\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large. Choose such <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{+}=V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{+}=V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we can choose a smooth <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant Riemannian metric on <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and obtain the exponential map <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> as a smooth vector bundle reduction of the tangent microbundle.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we state the induction hypothesis. Given <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose we have chosen <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{rs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{rs}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,s</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{rs}&lt;d_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying (<a href="#S17.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ 17.3.1. Post-smoothed Kuranishi spaces ‣ 17.3. Pre-smoothed relatively smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.1</span></a>) and post-smoothings such that the induced embeddings of the smoothed Kuranishi spaces are morphisms of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="footnote25" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">25</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">25</sup>
                      <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">25</span>
                      
                      
                      
                    This claim is a purpose of using rigidified embeddings: the trivialized normal bundle induces a canonical smoothing in the tubular neighborhood of the embedding. If we do not require the normal bundle to be trivialized, then one needs to make the painful choices of smooth bundle structures.</span></span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we can construct the stable smoothing on <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large such that the already stabilized boundary strata can all be included into <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, the interior <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Int}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Int}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> can be stably smoothed by Theorem <a href="#S17.Thmthm9" title="Theorem 17.9. ‣ 17.2.2. Stable 𝐺-smoothings ‣ 17.2. Preliminaries ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.9</span></a>, meaning that one can choose <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large and a smoothing of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Int}V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Int</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Int}V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By choosing <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> greater than both <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can assume <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}^{\prime}=\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}^{\prime}=\mu_{pq}^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that the induction hypothesis implies a canonically induced smoothing near the boundary. On overlaps, these two smoothings induce the same stable <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-isotopy class of microbundle reductions. Hence by the relative smoothing result proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Appendix B]</cite>, one can interpolate the two smoothings in the collar region, possibly after a further enlargement of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that near the boundary the smoothing is still the one canonically induced from other already-stabilized charts. Therefore, one obtains a stabilization by <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a smoothing of this stabilization, so that all the chart embeddings are morphisms of <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, we choose the smooth vector bundle reduction on the stabilized chart <math id="S17.SS3.SSS1.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}\times W_{pq,\mu_{pq}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S17.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">17.4. </span>Normally complex AMS lifts</h4>

<div id="S17.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally we are at the last step of proving Theorem <a href="#Thmthma15" title="Theorem O. ‣ 12.1. Main statements for Floer flow categories ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">O</span></a> and counterparts for Floer multimodules and homotopies.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.Thmthm16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S17.Thmthm16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 17.16</span></span><span id="S17.Thmthm16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S17.Thmthm16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S17.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S17.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S17.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationf3" title="Situation Flow(iii). ‣ 15.4.2. The category of relative smooth Kuranishi spaces ‣ 15.4. Relatively smooth AMS lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(iii)</span></a><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a post-smoothed AMS lift of </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, viewed as a lift in </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, admits a class of lifts to </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Each of such lifts, denoted by </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> temporarily, is called an </span><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NC AMS lift</span><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of (either </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or </span><math id="S17.I6.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S17.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationm1" title="Situation Module(i). ‣ 10.2. Multimodules from smooth domains ‣ 10. Geometric Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(i)</span></a><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be post-smoothed AMS lifts of involved Floer flow categories and let </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a post-smoothed AMS lift of the multimodule </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Suppose </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are NC AMS lifts of </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then there exists a class of lifts of </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as multimodules over </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m};\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Each of such lifts, denoted by </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> temporarily, is called an </span><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NC AMS lift</span><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> of (either </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or </span><math id="S17.I6.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S17.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S17.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation </span><a href="#Thmsituationh1" title="Situation Homotopy(i). ‣ 11.1. Homotopies from varying Floer data ‣ 11. Homotopies of Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Homotopy(i)</span></a><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, let </span><math id="S17.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1},\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m},\hat{\mathbb{F}},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0},\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1},\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be post-smoothed AMS lifts of the involved flow categories, multimodules, and homotopy. Suppose </span><math id="S17.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}_{m},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{F}}}}^{\prime},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0},\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be NC AMS lifts. Then there exists a lift of </span><math id="S17.I6.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S17.I6.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as a homotopy from </span><math id="S17.I6.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to </span><math id="S17.I6.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\vphantom{\rule{1.0pt}{5.71527pt}}\smash{\hat{\mathbb{X}}}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S17.I6.i3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S17.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that the post-smoothing of a relatively smooth Kuranishi space <math id="S17.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=(G,V/B,E,S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=(G,V/B,E,S)</annotation></semantics></math> still remembers the vector bundle <math id="S17.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}TB\oplus T^{\rm vt}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}TB\oplus T^{\rm vt}V</annotation></semantics></math> although the relative structure is destroyed. As the post-smoothing also includes the identification between this vector bundle and the smooth tangent bundle, we may assume <math id="S17.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV</annotation></semantics></math> has the canonical splitting.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now notice that <math id="S17.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with the <math id="S17.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant NC structure while <math id="S17.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TB</annotation></semantics></math> is equipped with the <math id="S17.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant stable complex structure. This does not yet provide an NC structure on <math id="S17.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S17.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV</annotation></semantics></math> contains the subbundle of the infinitesimal <math id="S17.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-action. To obtain the NC structure, one needs to make the obstruction bundle complex first.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that from the construction of the AMS lifts, the obstruction bundle is always trivial and decomposes as</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\underline{\smash{W}}\oplus\underline{\smash{Q}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\underline{\smash{W}}\oplus\underline{\smash{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is a complex representation of <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is a real representation of <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we observe that in all the Kuranishi spaces we obtained in the construction, the direct sum</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{g}}\oplus Q" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔤</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{g}}\oplus Q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">is naturally isomorphic to the Lie algebra of the complex Lie group <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can stabilize all charts by the Lie algebra. Denote by</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}:={\rm Stab}_{\mathfrak{g}}(K)=(G,\tilde{V},\tilde{E},\tilde{S})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Stab</mi><mi>𝔤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}:={\rm Stab}_{\mathfrak{g}}(K)=(G,\tilde{V},\tilde{E},\tilde{S}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">In this way, the obstruction bundles of all involved Kuranishi spaces are equivariant complex vector bundles. Let</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}\subseteq T\tilde{V}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}\subseteq T\tilde{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">be the subbundle spanned by infinitesimal <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-actions. Then by Definition <a href="#S3.Thmthm24" title="Definition 3.24. ‣ 3.3.3. Normally complex Kuranishi spaces ‣ 3.3. Stable complex structures and normal complex structures ‣ 3. Kuranishi Spaces ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.24</span></a>, it remains to construct <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant NC structures on the bundles <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\tilde{V}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\tilde{V}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, for each chart <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}=(G,\tilde{V},\tilde{E},\tilde{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}=(G,\tilde{V},\tilde{E},\tilde{S})</annotation></semantics></math> after the stabilization, let <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\tilde{V}\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\tilde{V}\to V</annotation></semantics></math> be the projection. Then one has</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\tilde{V}=\pi^{*}TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\tilde{V}=\pi^{*}TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the previous constructions provide <math id="S17.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV</annotation></semantics></math> with NC structures. Therefore, it surfaces to define compatible equivariant bundle isomorphisms</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}TV\cong(\pi^{*}TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})/{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}TV\cong(\pi^{*}TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})/{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">One chooses such isomorphisms in the following way. Choose a compatible system of <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant metrics on <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> inductively. Then one obtains an equivariant splitting</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV\cong{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}^{\bot}\oplus{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msubsup><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV\cong{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}^{\bot}\oplus{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is isomorphic with the trivial bundle <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then define</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}TV\cong\pi^{*}({\mathfrak{g}}_{V}^{\bot})\oplus\pi^{*}{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}\to\pi^{*}(TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>⊥</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}TV\cong\pi^{*}({\mathfrak{g}}_{V}^{\bot})\oplus\pi^{*}{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}\to\pi^{*}(TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">by sending <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}TV" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}TV</annotation></semantics></math> while sending <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}{\mathfrak{g}}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is then easy to see that the composition</span></p>
<table id="S17.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}TV\to\pi^{*}(TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})\to\pi^{*}(TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})/{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}TV\to\pi^{*}(TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})\to\pi^{*}(TV\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}})/{\mathfrak{g}}_{\tilde{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S17.SS4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">is an isomorphism. This equips the Kuranishi spaces <math id="S17.SS4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>-equivariant NC structures.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S17.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">17.5. </span>Coherent orientations</h4>

<div id="S17.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all involved flow categories and all objects <math id="S17.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in{\mathbb{O}b}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in{\mathbb{O}b}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose a trivialization of the determinant line <math id="S17.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det D_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det D_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>. In last section, the isomorphism <math id="S17.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> hence determines an orientation on the vertical tangent bundle <math id="S17.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, there are orientations on the vertical tangent bundle <math id="S17.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>vt</mi></msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> for a multimodule.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After stable smoothing, one has equivariant bundle isomorphisms</p>
<table id="S17.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV_{pq}\cong\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV_{pq}\cong\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Both summands have been given certain orientations. We then orient <math id="S17.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> using the above decomposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">One can then verify the coherence requirement of Definition <a href="#S7.Thmthm12" title="Definition 7.12. ‣ 7.1.4. Orientations ‣ 7.1. Unobstructedness, local finiteness, grading, and orientations ‣ 7. Algebraic Structures ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7.12</span></a>. Indeed, for <math id="S17.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math>, the isomorphism</p>
<table id="S17.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big(\pi_{pr}^{*}TB_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\Big)\oplus\Big(\pi_{rq}^{*}TB_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\Big)\to\pi^{*}TB_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big(\pi_{pr}^{*}TB_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}^{\mathbb{F}}\Big)\oplus\Big(\pi_{rq}^{*}TB_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}\Big)\to\pi^{*}TB_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">is orientation preserving up to a sign</p>
<table id="S17.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{{\rm rank}T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}}=(-1)^{|p|-|r|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{{\rm rank}T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}}=(-1)^{|p|-|r|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">because <math id="S17.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{rq}^{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is odd-dimensional.</p>
</div>
<div id="S17.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S17.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose the AMS lifts of <math id="S17.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{F}}_{m};{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are oriented as above. W orient the multimodule <math id="S17.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. For each tuple <math id="S17.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},\ldots,p_{m};p^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, orient the tangent bundle of the thickening <math id="S17.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> via the direct sum decomposition</p>
<table id="S17.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cong\pi_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{*}TB_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>≅</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>T</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝔽</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>T</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>vt</mi></msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\cong\pi_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{*}TB_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{F}}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Notice that the domain moduli is even-dimensional. Then one can see that with respect to breakings, the isomorphism</p>
<table id="S17.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\oplus TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV_{p_{i}q_{i}}^{{\mathbb{F}}_{i}}\oplus TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{i-1}q_{i}p_{i+1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\to TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS5.p4.3" class="ltx_p">has a sign <math id="S17.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{(\sum_{j&lt;i}|p_{i}|)(|p_{i}|-|q_{i}|)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{(\sum_{j&lt;i}|p_{i}|)(|p_{i}|-|q_{i}|)}</annotation></semantics></math> while the isomorphism</p>
<table id="S17.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S17.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus TV_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\cong TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><mo>⊕</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>≅</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}\oplus TV_{q^{\prime}p^{\prime}}^{{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}}\cong TV_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S17.SS5.p4.4" class="ltx_p">has a sign <math id="S17.SS5.p4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(-1)^{{\rm rank}T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mi>T</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>vt</mi></msup><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{{\rm rank}T^{\rm vt}V_{p_{1}\cdots p_{m};q^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S18" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">18. </span>Proofs of the Main Theorems on AMS Lifts</h3>

<div id="S18.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we summarize the previous constructions as formal proofs of the main theorems about the AMS lifts for Floer flow categories, multimodules and homotopies to the category of (rigidified and collared) normally complex derived orbifolds <math id="S18.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐝𝐎𝐫𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf dOrb}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S18.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">18.1. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma15" title="Theorem O. ‣ 12.1. Main statements for Floer flow categories ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">O</span></a></h4>

<div id="S18.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume we are in Situation <a href="#Thmsituationf1" title="Situation Flow(i). ‣ 9.2. Floer flow category ‣ 9. Geometric Flow Categories ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Flow(i)</span></a>. The construction is illustrated and summarized in Figure <a href="#S18.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ 18.1. Proof of Theorem ‣ 18. Proofs of the Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. Each step of the roadmap is completed by a concrete theorem or proposition in previous sections. Upon taking the quotient orbifold, we obtain the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma15" title="Theorem O. ‣ 12.1. Main statements for Floer flow categories ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">O</span></a> except the orientation part.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S18.F9" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S18.F9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="437.43" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 541.85 437.43" width="541.85"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,437.43) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(74.07,0) translate(0,416.4)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFB3B3;" fill="#FFB3B3" stroke="#000000"><path d="M 68.26 20.76 L -68.26 20.76 C -71.32 20.76 -73.8 18.28 -73.8 15.22 L -73.8 -15.22 C -73.8 -18.28 -71.32 -20.76 -68.26 -20.76 L 68.26 -20.76 C 71.32 -20.76 73.8 -18.28 73.8 -15.22 L 73.8 15.22 C 73.8 18.28 71.32 20.76 68.26 20.76 Z M -73.8 -20.76"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -69.19 5.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.45em;font-size:10pt;" height="29.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="138.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S18.F9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:10em;">
