</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 275.59 -78.74 L 393.7 -78.74 L 393.7 -156.93"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 393.7 -157.2)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 275.59 -377.95 L 393.7 -377.95 L 393.7 -236.77"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 393.7 -236.5)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#FFB3B3;" fill="#FFB3B3" stroke="#000000"><path d="M 461.96 -166.99 L 325.44 -166.99 C 322.38 -166.99 319.9 -169.46 319.9 -172.52 L 319.9 -221.18 C 319.9 -224.24 322.38 -226.71 325.44 -226.71 L 461.96 -226.71 C 465.02 -226.71 467.5 -224.24 467.5 -221.18 L 467.5 -172.52 C 467.5 -169.46 465.02 -166.99 461.96 -166.99 Z M 319.9 -226.71"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 324.52 -181.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:2.96em;font-size:10pt;" height="50.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="138.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S18.F9.pic1.9" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:10em;">
<span id="S18.F9.pic1.9.1" class="ltx_p"></span>
<span id="S18.F9.pic1.9.2" class="ltx_p">Stabilization and lift to <math id="S18.F9.pic1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorem <a href="#S16.Thmthm1" title="Theorem 16.1. ‣ 16.1. Main statements about normal complex structures ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#S17.Thmthm16" title="Theorem 17.16. ‣ 17.4. Normally complex AMS lifts ‣ 17. Stable Smoothings ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17.16</span></a>)</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9. </span>Roadmap of the AMS construction for Floer flow categories. Here the pink, rounded rectangles involve choices to be made and the orange rectangles are items canonically induced from previous steps.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S18.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now we explain how to obtain a coherent orientation for the AMS lift. Given a pair of objects <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q\in{\rm Ob}{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one needs to specify an orientation on the virtual vector bundle</p>
<table id="S18.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S18.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(V_{pq}/G_{pq})-E_{pq}/G_{pq}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(V_{pq}/G_{pq})-E_{pq}/G_{pq}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S18.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{pq}=W_{pq}\oplus Q_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{pq}=W_{pq}\oplus Q_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from the thickening data and <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝔤</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>ℂ</mi></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}^{\mathbb{C}}/{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>. As the thickening space <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex, it can be neglected for orientation considerations. Moreover, if we stabilize the virtual vector bundle by <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>, then as <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{pq}\oplus{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}\cong{\mathfrak{g}}^{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>𝔤</mi><mi>ℂ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{pq}\oplus{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}\cong{\mathfrak{g}}^{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is complex and hence canonically oriented, it is equivalent to orient the vector bundle</p>
<table id="S18.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S18.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(V_{pq}/G_{pq})\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}/G_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(V_{pq}/G_{pq})\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}/G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S18.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}\to V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}\to V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is the trivial bundle with fibres being <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}/G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}/G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> is the induced orbifold vector bundle.</p>
</div>
<div id="S18.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, the stable smoothing operation preserves the (<math id="S18.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) isomorphism</p>
<table id="S18.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S18.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TV_{pq}\cong\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vert}V_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vert</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TV_{pq}\cong\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vert}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S18.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where both summands have been given <math id="S18.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-invariant orientations. Moreover, there is a summand <math id="S18.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}\subseteq TV_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔤</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathfrak{g}}_{pq}\subseteq TV_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the infinitesimal <math id="S18.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math>-actions. Then the direct sum orientation descends to an orientation on the bundle</p>
<table id="S18.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S18.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(V_{pq}/G_{pq})\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}/G_{pq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔤</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(V_{pq}/G_{pq})\oplus\underline{\smash{\mathfrak{g}}}_{pq}/G_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S18.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">which is what we need.</p>
</div>
<div id="S18.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to verify that the individual orientations on the derived orbifolds are coherent. Suppose <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;r&lt;q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;r&lt;q</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that the domain moduli spaces <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are oriented in a way which respects breakings (see Lemma <a href="#S14.Thmthm20" title="Lemma 14.20. ‣ 14.3.7. Orientation and concatenation ‣ 14.3. Construction of the domain flow categories ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.20</span></a>). On the other hand, the orientations on the vertical tangent bundles <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</p>
<table id="S18.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S18.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}\cong\det T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}\otimes\det T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}\cong\det T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}\otimes\det T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S18.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">as oriented bundles. As <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{pq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{pq}</annotation></semantics></math> are always odd-dimensional, there holds</p>
<table id="S18.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S18.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\Big(\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\Big)|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}\cong\det\Big(\pi_{pr}^{*}TB_{pr}\oplus\pi_{rq}^{*}TB_{rq}\oplus Q_{prq}\Big)\otimes\det\Big(T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}\oplus W_{prq}\Big)\\
\cong(-1)^{{\rm rank}T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}}\det\Big(\pi_{pr}^{*}TB_{pr}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}\Big)\otimes\det\Big(\pi_{rq}^{*}TB_{rq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⊗</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>vt</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\Big(\pi_{pq}^{*}TB_{pq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pq}\Big)|_{\partial^{prq}V_{pq}}\cong\det\Big(\pi_{pr}^{*}TB_{pr}\oplus\pi_{rq}^{*}TB_{rq}\oplus Q_{prq}\Big)\otimes\det\Big(T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}\oplus W_{prq}\Big)\\
\cong(-1)^{{\rm rank}T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}}\det\Big(\pi_{pr}^{*}TB_{pr}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{pr}\Big)\otimes\det\Big(\pi_{rq}^{*}TB_{rq}\oplus T^{\rm vt}V_{rq}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S18.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Notice that here <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{prq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{prq}</annotation></semantics></math> are both complex. The rank of the vertical bundle here is congruent mod 2 to the difference <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p|-|r|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p|-|r|</annotation></semantics></math> of cohomological gradings. This means the orientations on the derived orbifolds specified above provide a coherent orientation on <math id="S18.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">18.2. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma16" title="Theorem P. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">P</span></a></h4>

<div id="S18.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also summarize the construction of AMS lifts of multimodules associated to a smooth Floer domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="S18.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S18.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 18.1</span></span><span id="S18.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S18.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In Situation <a href="#Thmsituationm1" title="Situation Module(i). ‣ 10.2. Multimodules from smooth domains ‣ 10. Geometric Multimodules ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Module(i)</span></a>, fix an outercollaring width and choose a list of integral actions on the involved flow categories which are compatible with respect to <math id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be AMS lifts to <math id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> (subject to the fixed outercollaring width and the integral actions). Then there exists a lift of the outercollaring of <math id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> as a multimodule over <math id="S18.Thmthm1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\ldots,\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{m};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S18.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S18.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To save notations, we write the proof in the case of bimodules and write <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}={\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔹</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}={\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The case of multimodules is the same. Abbreviate <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The constructions of <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> start with the monotone flow categories <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by Proposition <a href="#S14.Thmthm22" title="Proposition 14.22. ‣ 14.4.2. Rigidification and stable complex structure ‣ 14.4. Multimodules and homotopies for smooth domains ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.22</span></a>, there exists a monotone bimodule <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma^{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Sigma^{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom};{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝔻</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><mo>;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝔻</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕠</mi><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom};{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then using the compatible integral actions, one obtains the corresponding bimodule <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>𝕠</mi><mi>𝕞</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}};{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝔻</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕠</mi><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔽</mi></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝔻</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mi>𝕠</mi><msup><mi>𝕞</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}};{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Dom}^{\Omega,{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The choices of transverse thickening data for <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can be extended, by Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm19" title="Proposition 15.19. ‣ 15.3.3. Transversality ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.19</span></a>, to a transverse thickening datum <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{W}}^{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕎</mi><mi>𝕏</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{W}}^{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The choices of the group reductions for <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can be extended, by Proposition <a href="#S15.Thmthm9" title="Proposition 15.9. ‣ 15.2.6. Group reductions ‣ 15.2. Framed maps ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.9</span></a>, to a group reduction on <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Map}_{{\mathbb{X}}}^{\mathbb{fr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>𝕒</mi><mi>𝕡</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝕏</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕣</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\mathbb{Map}_{{\mathbb{X}}}^{\mathbb{fr}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by Definition <a href="#S15.Thmthm16" title="Definition 15.16. ‣ 15.3.2. The thickenings ‣ 15.3. The topological Kuranishi lifts ‣ 15. Relatively Smooth AMS lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15.16</span></a>, one obtains the collections of thickenings <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mi>𝔹</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p;p^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> which provides (in a canonical way) a lift of the outercollaring of <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔹</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mi>rel</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf S^{\rm rel}Kur}}_{\rm rig}</annotation></semantics></math> as a bimodule over <math id="S18.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}};\hat{\mathbb{F}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. The remaining structures, including the relative NC structure, the stable smoothing, and the NC structure can all be constructed using the inductive procedure. We omit the details.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S18.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The two exceptional cases, i.e., the multimodules for Poincaré pairing and the cigar bimodule can be established similarly. We only give the statement without detailed proofs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S18.Thmthm2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S18.Thmthm2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 18.2</span></span><span id="S18.Thmthm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S18.Thmthm2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1},{\mathbb{F}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1},{\mathbb{F}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be Floer flow categories associated to <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H_{1},J_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H_{1},J_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H_{2},J_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H_{2},J_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Let <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}^{\rm PD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕏</mi><mi>PD</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}^{\rm PD}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Poincaré multimodule over <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{F}}_{1},{\mathbb{F}}_{2};{\mathbb{O}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕆</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{F}}_{1},{\mathbb{F}}_{2};{\mathbb{O}})</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a Floer data interpolating on the infinite cylinder. Fix an outercollaring width and choose integral actions <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}}^{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{1}}^{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{2}}^{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{{\mathbb{F}}_{2}}^{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> which are compatible with respect to this multimodule. Let <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be AMS lifts of <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the outercollaring width and the chosen integral actions. Then there exists a lift of the outercollaring of <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}^{\rm PD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕏</mi><mi>PD</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}^{\rm PD}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> as a multimodule over <math id="S18.Thmthm2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{2};{\mathbb{O}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕆</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{1},\hat{\mathbb{F}}_{2};{\mathbb{O}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we call an AMS lift subject to the outercollaring width and the chosen integral actions.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S18.Thmthm3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S18.Thmthm3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 18.3</span></span><span id="S18.Thmthm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S18.Thmthm3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a Floer flow category associated to <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H,J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H,J)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>cigar</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}</annotation></semantics></math> be the cigar bimodule over <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{O}};{\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝔽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{O}};{\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> associated to a Floer data on the complex plane. Let <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an AMS lift of <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to an outercollaring width and an integral action <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>𝔽</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{A}}_{\mathbb{F}}^{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> which is compatible with respect to the bimodule <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>cigar</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exists a lift of the outercollaring of <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>cigar</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> which is a bimodule over <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{O}};\hat{\mathbb{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕆</mi><mo>;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{O}};\hat{\mathbb{F}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which we call an AMS lift of <math id="S18.Thmthm3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝔹</mi><mi>cigar</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}^{\rm cigar}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the outercollaring width and the chosen integral action.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S18.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Propositions <a href="#S18.Thmthm1" title="Proposition 18.1. ‣ 18.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ 18. Proofs of the Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18.1</span></a>–<a href="#S18.Thmthm3" title="Proposition 18.3. ‣ 18.2. Proof of Theorem ‣ 18. Proofs of the Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18.3</span></a> lead to the first item of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma16" title="Theorem P. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">P</span></a> (without the orientation claim). To establish the second item, consider the trivial homotopy <math id="S18.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S18.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> to itself. Notice that the chosen integral actions are still compatible with respect to <math id="S18.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any two AMS lifts <math id="S18.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S18.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbb{X}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the same outercollaring width and the same set of integral actions, one can construct a lift of the outercollaring of <math id="S18.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S18.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo></msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐒𝐊𝐮𝐫</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>rig</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>NC</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\lfloor}\underline{\smash{\bf SKur}}_{\rm rig}^{\rm NC}</annotation></semantics></math> by using the corresponding homotopy version of each step of the AMS construction. We omit the details. After passing to derived orbifolds, one obtains the second item of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma16" title="Theorem P. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">P</span></a> (without the orientation claim).</p>
</div>
<div id="S18.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain coherent orientations, one can follow the same argument as in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma15" title="Theorem O. ‣ 12.1. Main statements for Floer flow categories ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">O</span></a>. The signs come from the properties of the orientations on the domain moduli spaces (see Proposition <a href="#S14.Thmthm22" title="Proposition 14.22. ‣ 14.4.2. Rigidification and stable complex structure ‣ 14.4. Multimodules and homotopies for smooth domains ‣ 14. The Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies of Domains ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14.22</span></a>) as well as the orientations on vertical tangent bundles (see Subsection <a href="#S16.SS5" title="16.5. Orientations ‣ 16. Vertical Normal Complex Structures and orientations ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16.5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S18.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">18.3. </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma17" title="Theorem Q. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Q</span></a></h4>

<div id="S18.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S18.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is simply a different organization of the previous constructions for flow categories and multimodules. Notice that it is important to choose integral actions which are compatible throughout the consideration. Then each stage of the AMS construction, starting from the domain flow category, rigidifications, choosing thickening data and group reductions, constructing relative NC structures, stable smoothing, and smooth NC structures, can all be inductively accomplished. The statement of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma17" title="Theorem Q. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Q</span></a> then follows without any new difficulties than flow category and multimodule cases.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S19" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">19. </span>Concatenation and Gluing—Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthma18" title="Theorem R. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">R</span></a></h3>

<div id="S19.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S19.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove Theorem <a href="#S12.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 12.4. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12.4</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#Thmthma18" title="Theorem R. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">R</span></a>. Note that, although the statement of Theorem <a href="#S12.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 12.4. ‣ 12.2. Multimodules and homotopies ‣ 12. Main Theorems on AMS Lifts ‣ Part II GEOMETRIC FLOW CATEGORIES, BIMODULES, AND HOMOTOPIES ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12.4</span></a> is on the level of derived orbifolds, the constructions of the rigidification and NC structure require us to go through the AMS construction on the level of Kuranishi spaces.</p>
</div>
<section id="S19.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">19.1. </span>Concatenation and gluing of domains</h4>

<section id="S19.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">19.1.1. </span>Concatenations of monotone multimodules</h5>

<div id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We make the analgoue of Definition <a href="#S6.Thmthm13" title="Definition 6.13. ‣ 6.5.2. General concatenations ‣ 6.5. Multimodule concatenations ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.13</span></a> for the case of monotone multimodules. Let <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{f}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{f}}_{m},{\mathbb{g}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{n},{\mathbb{g}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕗</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{f}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{f}}_{m},{\mathbb{g}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{n},{\mathbb{g}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be monotone flow categories enriched in <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> resp. <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be monotone multimodules over <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{f}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{f}}_{m};{\mathbb{g}}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕗</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{f}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{f}}_{m};{\mathbb{g}}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> resp. over <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{g}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{n};{\mathbb{g}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{g}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{n};{\mathbb{g}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="S19.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S19.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S19.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ A_{d}^{\mathbb{x}}\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ A_{d}^{\mathbb{x}}\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S19.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ A_{d}^{\mathbb{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ A_{d}^{\mathbb{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">be the underlying regular posets of the objects <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}^{\mathbb{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}^{\mathbb{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}^{\mathbb{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}^{\mathbb{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Define</p>
<table id="S19.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S19.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{d^{\prime}+d^{\prime\prime}=d}A_{d^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d^{\prime\prime}}^{\mathbb{y}}\right)/\sim" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⨆</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">∼</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}:=\left(\bigsqcup_{d^{\prime}+d^{\prime\prime}=d}A_{d^{\prime}}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d^{\prime\prime}}^{\mathbb{y}}\right)/\sim</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the equivalence relation <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> is similar to the case discussed in Subsection <a href="#S6.SS5" title="6.5. Multimodule concatenations ‣ 6. Flow Categories, Multimodules, and Homotopies ‣ Part I FORMAL NOTIONS ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.5</span></a>. More precisely, the equivalence relation is generated by</p>
<table id="S19.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S19.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 29.2166pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-3.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 53.2166pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{A_{d_{1}}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d}\times A_{d_{2}}^{\mathbb{y}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 20.68222pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 156.05238pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}{\hbox{\kern 173.72745pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern-29.2166pt\raise-31.33331pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{A_{d_{1}+d}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d_{2}}^{\mathbb{y}}}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 85.36372pt\raise-31.33331pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 147.51085pt\raise-31.33331pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{A_{d_{1}}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d+d_{2}}^{\mathbb{y}}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-54.425505726139825px" height="64.57" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="40.43 54.43 325.39 64.57" width="325.39"> <g transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 40.427007763584044 64.57261100949565) translate(0,3.46) translate(40.43,0)"> <g transform="translate(73.64,0) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="88.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 91.04915422012289 -11.069600110696001 L 91.04915422012289 -11.079692405108448" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(28.62,0) translate(0,-33.21)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 7.45 -0.3" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 5.6 4.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 91.04915422012289 -11.069600110696001 L 28.617988735276565 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 28.617988735276565 -33.198496901809186 L 28.617988735276565 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 153.47780718815943 -11.069600110696001 L 153.51184228981813 -11.16480127284186" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(215.93,0) translate(0,-33.21)"> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 0 -5.6 4.92" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 0 0 A 13.84 13.84 45 0 1 -7.45 -0.3" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> </g> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 153.47780718815943 -11.069600110696001 L 215.92968510149655 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <path style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" d="M 215.89564999983784 -33.11053769987979 L 215.92968510149655 -33.208800332088" fill="none" stroke="#000000"></path> <g transform="translate(-40.43,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="72.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> <g transform="translate(204.11,0) translate(0,-43.36) translate(4.15,0) translate(0,-3.46)"> <foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.24em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="72.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup></mrow></span></span></foreignObject> </g> </g> </svg> </mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lx@xy@svg{\hbox{\raise 2.5pt\hbox{\kern 29.2166pt\hbox{\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\hbox{\vtop{\halign{\entry@#!@&amp;&amp;\entry@@#!@\cr&amp;&amp;\cr&amp;&amp;\crcr}}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern-3.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 53.2166pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{A_{d_{1}}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d}\times A_{d_{2}}^{\mathbb{y}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 20.68222pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\kern 156.05238pt\raise-24.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\lx@xy@tip{1}\lx@xy@tip{-1}}}}}}\ignorespaces\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}\ignorespaces{\hbox{\lx@xy@drawline@}}{\hbox{\kern 173.72745pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern-29.2166pt\raise-31.33331pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{A_{d_{1}+d}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d_{2}}^{\mathbb{y}}}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 85.36372pt\raise-31.33331pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{}$}}}}}}}{\hbox{\kern 147.51085pt\raise-31.33331pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 0.0pt\raise 0.0pt\hbox{\hbox{\kern 3.0pt\raise-2.5pt\hbox{$\textstyle{A_{d_{1}}^{\mathbb{x}}\times A_{d+d_{2}}^{\mathbb{y}}}$}}}}}}}\ignorespaces}}}}\ignorespaces.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Then for each pair <math id="S19.SS1.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,e\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,e\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a codimension zero subset</p>
<table id="S19.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S19.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}}\times A_{e}^{{\mathbb{y}}}\cong A_{d;e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}\subseteq A_{d+e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}}\times A_{e}^{{\mathbb{y}}}\cong A_{d;e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}\subseteq A_{d+e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S19.Thmthm1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_defn">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S19.Thmthm1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 19.1</span></span><span id="S19.Thmthm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S19.Thmthm1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S19.Thmthm1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <span id="S19.Thmthm1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">concatenation</span> of <math id="S19.Thmthm1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S19.Thmthm1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S19.Thmthm1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{g}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{g}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the following objects.</p>
<ol id="S19.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S19.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S19.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S19.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A monotone multimodule denoted by <math id="S19.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S19.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\mathbb{g}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{i-1},{\mathbb{f}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{f}}_{m},{\mathbb{g}}_{i+1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{n};{\mathbb{g}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕗</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕗</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝕘</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝕘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\mathbb{g}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{i-1},{\mathbb{f}}_{1},\ldots,{\mathbb{f}}_{m},{\mathbb{g}}_{i+1},\ldots,{\mathbb{g}}_{n};{\mathbb{g}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of objects</p>
<table id="S19.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S19.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Ob</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}\in{\rm Ob}\underline{\smash{\bf C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S19.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">together with structural maps.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S19.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S19.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S19.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S19.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,e\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,e\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, codimension zero morphisms</p>
<table id="S19.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S19.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}^{\mathbb{x}}\times M_{e}^{\mathbb{y}}\to M_{d+e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}^{\mathbb{x}}\times M_{e}^{\mathbb{y}}\to M_{d+e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S19.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">whose underlying poset map the inclusion <math id="S19.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}}\times A_{e}^{{\mathbb{y}}}\to A_{d+e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>𝕪</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}}\times A_{e}^{{\mathbb{y}}}\to A_{d+e}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S19.Thmthm1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">They are required to satisfy the following conditions.</p>
<ol id="S19.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S19.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S19.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S19.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The objects <math id="S19.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is stratified by the poset <math id="S19.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>𝕪</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}^{{\mathbb{x}}\circ_{i}{\mathbb{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by (<a href="#S19.E1" title="In 19.1.1. Concatenations of monotone multimodules ‣ 19.1. Concatenation and gluing of domains ‣ 19. Concatenation and Gluing—Proof of Theorem ‣ Part III THE AMS CONSTRUCTION ‣ Integral Hamiltonian Floer Theory: Foundations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19.1</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S19.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S19.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S19.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="S19.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,d_{i},e\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,d_{i},e\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the following diagram commutes.</p>
<table id="S19.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
